window.L5R_TECHNIQUE_TEXT = {"battleinthemind":"<ul><li>As two masters of any martial art square off before a duel, each seeks to predict the other’s angle of attack and strategy, and the ways their predictions might be foiled by the opponent’s.</li><li>When you make an Initiative check for a Duel using your Void Ring, you may spend (op):</li><li>Void (op): You name two rings, then your opponent must name one. When your opponent selects their stance during their first turn, they cannot select the ring they named.</li><li>Void +(op): Choose a technique category. Learn one of your opponent&#x27;s known techniques of that category (chosen by opponent) per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","bearsswipestyle":"<ul><li>Activation: While you perform an Attack action check, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: Earth (op)(op): Choose one condition (Bleeding, Dazed, Disoriented, Prone). If this check inflicts that condition, targets cannot remove it until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","boarswrathstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a check to resist a critical strike during a skirmish, if you are Enraged and not Incapacitated, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Fire or Void (op)+: Choose one unarmed profile or readied improvised weapon. Each other character at range 0-1 with vigilance lower than or equal to (op) spent suffers physical damage equal to base damage of unarmed profile plus 1 for each (op) spent in excess of their vigilance.</li></ul>","bonebreakerstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check with a Cumbersome weapon, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>(op)(op): If target would suffer a critical strike, instead of making a check to resist, they suffer the severity 5-6: Debilitating Gash result.</li></ul>","breathofwindstyle":"<ul><li>A swift strike to the solar plexus or throat can leave the target reeling; an experienced bushi can steal the breath from their foe with a quick jab even while executing another attack.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Air) check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Air +(op): One target must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Earth 4, Fire 1) or suffer Disoriented and fatigue equal to their shortfall. Increase the TN to resist by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","cautioustread":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a Movement action check while riding a mount, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op)(op): Choose one terrain quality: Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring. You and your mount ignore its effects. Persists until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chaoticscattering":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Movement and Scheme action using a readied improvised weapon, make a TN 2 Survival (Air) check targeting one position at range 1-2.</li><li>Throw improvised weapon to chosen position. If you succeed, choose one terrain quality (Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring). All terrain within 1 range band of targeted position gains that quality. Persists for 1 round plus 1 additional round per two bonus successes. If you fail, weapon lands at target position.</li></ul>","coilingserpentstyle":"<ul><li>Entrapping techniques can be performed with many different weapons, from the kusari-gama wielded by brigands to the ornate, hook-headed polearms used by the Phoenix Clan’s greatest masters of the spear.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Unarmed] check using a Snaring weapon, you may spend (op):</li><li>+(op): Choose one weapon a target has readied; that weapon cannot be used for Attack actions. Persists until end of your next turn.</li><li>(op) +(op): One target of your action per (op) spent this way becomes Immobilized.</li></ul>","crashingwavestyle":"<ul><li>The wave washes over the stone, wearing it away, and so the bushi’s weapon passes across their foe’s flesh, leaving behind a bloody gash or slice that is sure to slow their enemy even if the hit is not fatal.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Water) check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Water +(op): One target must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Earth 1, Fire 4) or suffer Bleeding and fatigue equal to their shortfall. Increase the TN to resist by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","crescentmoonstyle":"<ul><li>Striking first is valuable, but so is surviving. To defend without sacrificing offense, a bushi must be ready to retaliate swiftly after blocking or evading. With a quick shift, the bushi switches from defense to bring down their full force upon their enemy.</li><li>When you perform Guard action, you may spend (op):</li><li>(op): After a character at range 1-2 performs an Attack action targeting you or another character you are guarding, you may perform a Strike action with one readied Martial Arts [Melee or Unarmed] weapon targeting that character (if within weapon&#x27;s range). Persists until start of your next turn, or until you perform a Strike action this way.</li></ul>","crimsonleavesstrike":"<ul><li>Sweeping their blade down in a sudden arc, the bushi lands a blow atop the enemy’s weapon, scattering it from their hand like falling leaves.</li><li>As an Attack action using a readied weapon, make a TN 4 Martial Arts (Earth) check targeting one character within weapon&#x27;s range.</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers physical damage equal to your Earth Ring plus bonus successes. Choose one of target&#x27;s readied weapons; target must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 2, Water 5) or lose control of the chosen weapon, which travels 3 range bands in a direction of your choice.</li><li>Earth (op): If you disarm your opponent, you may take control of their weapon instead of knocking it away.</li></ul>","daringswing":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action using a readied Snaring weapon, make a TN 3 Martial Arts [Melee] (Water) check targeting one position within range you could not normally reach.</li><li>If you succeed, snag weapon and swing to the position.</li></ul>","deflectivedefense":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Movement and Support action using a readied Cumbersome weapon, make a TN 2 Martial Arts [Melee] (Earth) check.</li><li>If you succeed, treat physical resistance against attacks from characters at range 2-6 as increased by your ranks in Fitness.</li></ul>","descendingswarmshot":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack action using a readied bow or sling, you may make a TN 3 Martial Arts [Ranged] (Air) check targeting one character within range. Reduce TN by 1 if target is silhouette 3 or larger.</li><li>If you succeed, your target becomes vulnerable. When a character makes an Attack action check targeting the affected target and succeeds, they add one bonus success. Persists until end of your next turn.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): If you succeed, characters attacking the affected target add bonus successes equal to your ranks in Command instead. (op)(op)+: This effect persists for one additional round per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","disappearingworldstyle":"<ul><li>Seeing nothing but their enemy, the bushi surges forward in a flurry of strikes, seeking to land a hit to the eyes, temple, or other vulnerable area rapidly after their initial attack. This stunning blow can leave the enemy staggered, giving the bushi a chance to finish the battle with their next attack.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Fire) check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Fire +(op): One target must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Air 4, Water 1) or suffer Dazed and fatigue equal to their shortfall. Increase the TN to resist by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","distractingflurrystyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check using Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Unarmed], if you are in Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op): If you fail, your target suffers the Disoriented condition.</li></ul>","eyelesssightshot":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action using a readied ranged weapon, make a Martial Arts [Ranged] (Void) check targeting one character within range to whom you do not have line of sight. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers physical damage equal to weapon&#x27;s base damage and receives strife equal to bonus successes.</li></ul>","fallingheavensshot":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as an Attack and Movement action using a readied ranged weapon, make a Martial Arts [Ranged] (Void) check targeting one character within range. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, at start of target&#x27;s next turn, they suffer a critical strike with severity equal to weapon&#x27;s deadliness.</li></ul>","fiercebadgerstyle":"<ul><li>Type: Kata</li><li>Subtype: Close Combat Kata</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] check targeting a character at range 0</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: If the target is Immobilized, they receive 1 strife per (op) spent this way. (op)+: If the target&#x27;s silhouette and vigilance both are lower than or equal to (op) spent this way, the target is thrown 2 range bands in a direction of your choice and suffers 3 fatigue.</li></ul>","flashingsteelstrike":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack and Scheme action using a readied weapon, make a Martial Arts [Melee] (Air or Fire) check targeting one character in weapon&#x27;s range. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, target must choose: receive strife equal to your ranks in Performance and the Dazed condition; OR suffer a critical strike with severity equal to your weapon&#x27;s deadliness.</li></ul>","flexiblegrip":"<ul><li>Activation: Movement and Support action, shift grip on a polearm.</li><li>If you have a readied polearm, treat it as a staff with profile: 2-hand Melee; Range 0-1, DMG 4, DLS 2. Treated as both polearm and blunt weapon. End at end of any turn or persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","flight":"<ul><li>Activation: Movement action, take flight.</li><li>While flying, when you move 1+ range bands, move that many plus 1 instead (horizontally or vertically). For each range band moved upward, receive 1 fatigue. Ignore terrain effects while moving. Do not fall or suffer falling effects. Persists until end of scene or ended as Movement action.</li></ul>","flowingwaterstrike":"<ul><li>A skilled warrior is not restricted by the optimal range of their weapon, and can open or close gaps to compensate for positional disadvantages.</li><li>As an Attack and Movement action using a readied weapon, make a TN 3 Martial Arts (Water) check targeting one character at range 0-2 (regardless of weapon&#x27;s usual range restrictions).</li><li>If you succeed, the target suffers physical damage equal to your Water Ring and suffers Bleeding. Target must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Earth 2, Fire 5); if they fail, increase the physical damage by your weapon&#x27;s base damage.</li><li>Water (op): Remove Dazed, Disoriented, Immobilized, or Prone from yourself.</li></ul>","hawksprecision":"<ul><li>While most bushi are expected to be proficient in the use of the bow, some are terrifyingly accurate, capable of hitting targets well beyond the expected engagement range.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Ranged] check, you may spend (op):</li><li>+(op): Treat the range of the weapon as 1 higher per (op) spent this way, to a maximum of range 6.</li></ul>","heartpiercingstrike":"<ul><li>Battle is the art of killing, and woe betide any warrior who forgets it. With a roar, the bushi launches forward, stabbing out with their weapon to fatally impale their enemy. Even if the strike does not slay the foe, it is likely to weaken them significantly.</li><li>As an Attack and Movement action using a readied weapon, make a TN 4 Martial Arts (Fire) check targeting one character within weapon&#x27;s range.</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers a Critical Strike with severity equal to weapon&#x27;s deadliness plus bonus successes. The TN of the Fitness check to resist is 3 (Air 4, Water 1) instead of the normal TN.</li><li>If you fail, you suffer Disoriented.</li><li>Fire (op): Before resolving the effect, move up to 1 range band toward your target.</li></ul>","heronsgraspstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: While you perform an Attack action check using a polearm, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Choose one Cumbersome weapon that a target with vigilance lower than or equal to (op) spent is wielding. That character loses persistent benefits and cannot use it for actions. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","howlinggaledefense":"<ul><li>Activation: While you make a check to resist a critical strike with a readied staff (such as bo), you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you reduce severity to 0, do not suffer effects. (op)(op): If you would suffer Bleeding, do not; your staff gains Damaged quality instead.</li></ul>","iaijutsucutcrossingblade":"<ul><li>The bushi twists their scabbard outward as they draw, The bushi grips their scabbard against their hip and cutting horizontally to extend their reach. draws, cutting upward to catch an advancing foe without being cut themself.</li><li>As an Attack and Movement action using one sheathed Razor-Edged weapon, make a TN 2 Martial Arts [Melee] check targeting one character at range 1-2.</li><li>You draw and ready the sheathed weapon in a one-handed grip.</li><li>If you succeed, deal physical damage equal to the weapon&#x27;s deadliness plus bonus successes.</li><li>(op): Ready one other sheathed Razor-Edged weapon.</li></ul>","iaijutsucutreversedraw":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack, Movement, and Scheme action using a sheathed Razor-Edged weapon, make a Martial Arts [Melee] check targeting one character at range 1. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>Draw and ready weapon in one-handed grip. You suffer Disoriented condition. If you succeed, target suffers physical damage equal to weapon&#x27;s deadliness plus 1 per two bonus successes.</li></ul>","iaijutsucutrisingblade":"<ul><li>The bushi grips their scabbard against their hip and draws, cutting upward to catch an advancing foe without being cut themself.</li><li>As an Attack action using one sheathed Razor-Edged weapon, you may make a Martial Arts [Melee] check targeting one character at range 0-1. The TN of this check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>You draw and ready the sheathed weapon in a one-handed grip.</li><li>If you succeed, deal physical damage equal to the weapon&#x27;s deadliness. Target cannot defend against this damage if they are Compromised.</li><li>(op): Ready one other sheathed Razor-Edged weapon.</li></ul>","iaijutsucutswordandsheath":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action using a sheathed Razor-Edged weapon, make a TN 2 Martial Arts [Melee] check targeting one character at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers 5 physical damage with deadliness 2 plus additional damage equal to bonus successes. Draw and ready weapon in one hand and sheath in the other.</li></ul>","improvisedassault":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 2 Tactics (Water) or Smithing (Water) check using a readied improvised weapon.</li><li>If you succeed, choose a Martial Arts [Melee] weapon profile for a similar weapon. Treat improvised weapon as having that profile with damage and deadliness reduced by 1. Persists until end of scene, then weapon gains Destroyed quality.</li></ul>","ironforeststyle":"<ul><li>A bushi versed in the spear can control their spacing with their opponent, forcing their foe to risk impalement each time they advance or catching loose clothes or stray body parts on the head of the weapon. Akodo’s Leadership refers to such a technique as the Iron Forest style, which turns the length of a single spear into an insurmountable distance.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] check using a polearm, you may spend (op):</li><li>+(op): The area in range of your weapon counts as Dangerous terrain for one target per (op) spent this way. When an affected character attempts to move closer to you, they must make a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 2, Water 5); if they fail, they cannot advance. Persists until start of your next turn.</li></ul>","ironinthemountainsstyle":"<ul><li>The bushi strikes with crushing force, breaking their enemy’s footing and knocking them to the ground with an overwhelming blow or sweeping their stance out from underneath them with a well-placed kick.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Earth) check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Earth +(op): One target must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Air 1, Water 4) or suffer Prone and fatigue equal to their shortfall. Increase the TN to resist by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","ironshellstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you perform a Guard action, if you have not moved any range bands this turn, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Earth or Void (op)+: Choose one character you can perceive per (op) spent. The next time you defend against physical damage from that character, your fatigue cannot be increased to a value greater than your endurance. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","landslidestrike":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack and Scheme action, make a Martial Arts [Melee] (Earth or Water) check targeting one character in weapon&#x27;s range. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance, or TN 1 if target is in Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain.</li><li>If you succeed, target must choose: receive fatigue equal to your ranks in Fitness and the Prone condition; OR switch to a different stance and suffer the Immobilized condition.</li></ul>","laughingfoxstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When targeted by an Attack action, if you have an empty hand, spend 1 Void point to immediately make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Air) check targeting another character at range 0-1 (not the attacker). TN equals new target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, you cease being the target of the Attack action; your target becomes the target instead.</li></ul>","lordhidasgripcrab":"<ul><li>The Kami Hida, patron of the Crab Clan, was a legendary slayer of monsters. He beheaded the massive demon that once menaced the rose-marble palace, and ripped out one skull of the two-headed Kabuto no Oni and crushed the other head with it. However, Hida was no mere brute: he was cunning, killing monsters by exploiting their weaknesses. Warriors of the Crab Clan train in similar techniques. They turn their foes&#x27; great weight against them by pinning or strategically damaging specific body parts.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a Fitness (Void) check targeting one creature of Silhouette 3 or larger at range 0-1. TN equals the target&#x27;s silhouette (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers Immobilized.</li><li>If you succeed, you count as granting Assistance to all characters who perform Attack actions against your target. Persists until beginning of your next turn.</li><li>Void (op): Target must resist with a Fitness check or suffer physical damage equal to its silhouette (ignoring resistance) and Prone. TN of this check equals your school rank.</li></ul>","lordshibasvalorphoenix":"<ul><li>Once, in the Shadowlands, the Kami Shiba stood alone between a vast horde of its foul denizens and the last of the Seven Thunders after their victory against Fu Leng. Drawing the legendary sword Ofushikai, Shiba cut his way through the host to the First Oni. Legends say that their blades flashed for a hundred days, shattering mountains around them and cutting great rifts across the ground. In the end, each slew the other, but Shiba fell with his oath to protect unbroken.</li><li>Once per game session, as a Support action using one readied weapon, make a TN 2 Tactics (Void) check targeting any number of friendly characters in range of your weapon.</li><li>If you succeed, other characters cannot select your targets as the targets of their Attack or Scheme actions if they could select you instead. If an action has multiple targets, you must be the first target chosen. Persists for a number of rounds equal to your school rank.</li><li>Void (op): If you succeed, increase the TN of Attack and Scheme checks targeting you by 1. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","mindsedge":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene, after you perform an action that does not require a check while in a Void stance, make a TN 1 Meditation (Void) check.</li><li>If you succeed, the next time you would receive strife, reduce the amount by 3 plus 1 per two bonus successes. Persists until start of your next turn.</li></ul>","openhandstyle":"<ul><li>Power does not come from speed alone. A master martial artist can apply force for maximum effect, making even gentle movements devastatingly effective blocks and strikes. With enough experience, a martial artist can even control their opponent’s stance.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] check using a weapon with the Snaring quality, you may spend (op):</li><li>(op) +(op): One target per (op) spent this way must switch to a different stance of your choice. Targets of Silhouette 3 or greater may resist with a TN 3 Fitness check and ignore this effect if they succeed.</li></ul>","owlsswoopstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: While you perform a Martial Arts [Melee] or Unarmed check, if 1+ range bands above target horizontally, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op)+: Choose 1 target per (op) spent; they suffer Disoriented condition.</li></ul>","peltinghailstyle":"<ul><li>A volley of arrows on the battlefield can be deadly, but most importantly from a strategic standpoint, it is terrifying to even the staunchest veterans. Even if only one in ten shots finds its mark, the salvo rattles opponents and forces caution.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Ranged] check, you may spend (op):</li><li>+(op): Choose a number of other characters at range 0-2 of your target equal to (op) spent this way. Each chosen character receives strife equal to the base damage of your weapon.</li></ul>","piercingboltstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check using an ax or polearm, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>(op): Treat weapon&#x27;s deadliness as increased by number of range bands you have traveled this round, and if thrown, add range bands the weapon has traveled.</li></ul>","pinthefan":"<ul><li>While it is difficult to kill at range with a single arrow, it can certainly be done, and master archers have been performing legendary feats of precision since the early days of Rokugan. From Hantei Genji’s famous shots to the arrow loosed by Doji Hotaru that slew Akodo Arasou, killing shots have often changed the course of the Emerald Empire’s history.</li><li>As an Attack and Movement action using a readied ranged weapon, make a Martial Arts [Ranged] check targeting one character within weapon&#x27;s range. TN equals the target&#x27;s vigilance plus the range of the attack.</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers damage equal to two times the weapon&#x27;s base damage plus bonus successes.</li><li>(op): If the target becomes Incapacitated as a result of damage from this action, they suffer a Critical Strike with severity equal to two times the weapon&#x27;s deadliness plus bonus successes.</li></ul>","polevault":"<ul><li>Type: Kata</li><li>Subtype: Close Combat Kata</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action using one readied polearm</li><li>Check: TN 3 Martial Arts [Melee] (Air or Water) targeting one character at range 3-4</li><li>You move to range 2 of your target, ignoring the effects of any terrain you pass over. If you succeed, deal physical damage equal to the weapon&#x27;s base damage plus bonus successes. If you fail with shortfall of 2 or more, suffer Prone condition, 2 fatigue and 2 strife.</li></ul>","razorbite":"<ul><li>Activation: While you perform an Attack action check using bite unarmed profile in true form, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Treat deadliness 2 higher per (op) spent. Water (op)(op): Ignore target&#x27;s physical resistance up to Survival ranks; if you succeed, target suffers Bleeding. Earth (op)(op): If Naga or creature with venomous bite, target suffers Exhausted.</li></ul>","recklesslunge":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action using unarmed punch or kick profile, make a TN 3 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Fire) check to launch at target at range 2-3.</li><li>Move to range 0 of target; suffer Prone condition. Reduce TN of target&#x27;s next Attack action targeting you by 1. If you succeed, target suffers damage equal to base unarmed damage plus ranks in Fitness and must make TN 3 Fitness check (Water 2, Air 5) or suffer Prone.</li></ul>","ridershaste":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Movement and Support action, if you are riding a mount, you may spur it to move more quickly.</li><li>Your mount receives fatigue up to your ranks in Survival, then carries you that many range bands plus one, to a maximum of 6.</li></ul>","rushingavalanchestyle":"<ul><li>When adopting this style, the bushi strikes with reckless abandon using a heavy armament. Thanks to the sheer weight of their weapon and the ferocity of their strikes, even a glancing blow can cause serious harm, and a telling blow usually ends the battle.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] check using a blunt weapon, you may spend (op):</li><li>(op): If you fail with a shortfall of two or less, your target suffers physical damage equal to your ranks in Fitness.</li><li>(op): If you succeed and your target is Prone, increase the damage you deal by your ranks in Fitness.</li></ul>","rushingoxstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you perform a Maneuver action during your turn, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Fire or Water (op)(op): After you move, perform a Strike action using a readied Martial Arts [Melee] weapon or unarmed profile targeting one character in range. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance. You can only target a character you moved toward.</li></ul>","scouringwindstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check using Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Unarmed] while wielding a non-Razor-Edged weapon in two hands, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op)(op): If you succeed, instead of dealing damage, choose one defensive item your target is using (armor or readied shield). The item receives the Damaged quality; if already Damaged, it becomes Destroyed instead.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): If you succeed and you are wielding an ax, in addition to dealing damage, choose one defensive item your target is using. It receives the Damaged quality; if already Damaged, it becomes Destroyed instead.</li></ul>","serowsleapstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: While you perform an Attack action check using a spear (yari, trident, ji), you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Spear ignores an amount of target&#x27;s physical resistance equal to (op) spent, max the distance you moved this round or distance thrown (whichever higher). Treat deadliness as increased by the same amount.</li></ul>","serpentstwiststyle":"<ul><li>Activation: While you make a Fitness check to resist a critical strike caused by another character&#x27;s Attack action at range 0-2, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: Water (op): The attacking character receives fatigue equal to the number of (st) results they kept. If you succeed, add that many bonus successes to your check.</li></ul>","shatteringtidestyle":"<ul><li>Type: Kata</li><li>Subtype: Close Combat Kata</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] check</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you succeed, and both you and your target are in Confining or Dangerous terrain, treat the damage and deadliness of the weapon you used as 1 higher for each kept (st) result on your check. (op)(op): If both you and your target are in Confining or Dangerous terrain, your target suffers the Dazed condition.</li></ul>","skitteringshift":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as Movement and Support action, receive 2 fatigue.</li><li>Increase TN of Attack action checks targeting you by 1. After a failed Attack action check targeting you, move 1 range band. After defending against damage, move 1 range band. Persists until end of next turn.</li></ul>","slashingsandstormstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check using Martial Arts [Melee] while wielding an ax, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op): If you succeed and your target is a minion, your target suffers additional damage equal to the deadliness of your weapon.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: If you fail and your target&#x27;s ranks in Meditation are less than or equal to (op) spent this way, your target receives strife equal to the deadliness of your weapon.</li></ul>","snappingbranchstrike":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack and Support action using a readied blunt weapon or polearm, make a TN 3 Fitness (Earth) check targeting one character at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers physical damage equal to 5 plus bonus successes with deadliness 2.</li></ul>","soaringslice":"<ul><li>Jerking their arm in a sudden motion, the bushi hurls their weapon at the enemy, hoping to take the foe off guard or open a gap in their defenses.</li><li>As an Attack action using one readied weapon in a one-handed grip, make a TN 2 Martial Arts check targeting one character at range 2-3.</li><li>You hurl your weapon at the target.</li><li>If you succeed, deal physical damage equal to the weapon&#x27;s base damage plus bonus successes. Weapon lands at range in a direction of your choice from target if they defend, or embeds in them if they suffer a Critical Strike.</li><li>If you fail, weapon travels range bands equal to the maximum range of the technique in the direction of the target.</li><li>+(op): Treat the maximum range of this technique as 1 higher per (op) spent this way.</li><li>(op): Reduce the TN of the next Attack action against the target before end of your next turn by 1.</li></ul>","soulsunder":"<ul><li>While bushi are generally less well equipped to deal with supernatural threats than shugenja, mastery of any art reveals how the world is all interconnected. Warriors deeply engaged with the mysteries of the sword can attune themselves to their ancestral blades to cut even those beings who walk between worlds and whose flesh steel normally will not bite.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 4 Meditation (Void) check to attune your blade to the spirits of your honored ancestors.</li><li>If you succeed, choose one readied weapon. It gains the Sacred quality, and when you use it to inflict a Critical Strike on an Otherworldly being, treat its deadliness as increased by your bonus successes. Persists until end of your next turn.</li><li>Void +(op): This effect persists for one additional round per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Void (op)(op): Otherworldly beings cannot perform Attack actions targeting you until start of your next turn.</li><li>Void (op)(op)(op): You may immediately perform a Strike action using your readied weapon.</li></ul>","spinningbladesstyle":"<ul><li>The biggest advantage of dual wielding does not usually stem from striking with two weapons simultaneously, largely because this is a very difficult feat. Instead, it comes from the fact that the warrior does not need to sacrifice defense while attacking or offense while defending. The off-hand blade can deflect and threaten even as the main-hand weapon attacks, or the bushi can strike with the offhand weapon while the main-hand weapon is locked with the foe’s blade. Either weapon can deliver death, and so the enemy must watch both at all times.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Unarmed] Attack action check, if you have a second readied weapon you did not use for the attack, you may spend (op):</li><li>+(op): You must spend (op) equal to your target&#x27;s Vigilance to activate this technique. You use your second readied weapon against one target, inflicting physical damage equal to its base damage. If that target is Dazed, increase this damage by your ranks in the skill you used.</li></ul>","staggeringshot":"<ul><li>Activation: When you perform a Martial Arts [Ranged] check, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Earth or Fire (op): Target treats all terrain as Dangerous. Persists until end of your next turn. Air or Water (op): Target treats all terrain as Entangling. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","stalkingleopardstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op)(op): If you succeed and your target is Disoriented or Prone, treat the damage and deadliness of your weapon as increased by your ranks in Survival.</li></ul>","strikingasair":"<ul><li>Not every stroke a warrior throws in battle is intended to kill—even if they all lead to that end goal. A skilled fighter can tell when an attack will not land and subtly shift it into a different sort of attack, meant to probe the enemy’s defenses or draw their guard out of position. By carefully placing attack after attack, a master of the blade can eventually whittle down their opponent’s options until none remain but death.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Air) check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Air +(op): Reserve one of your rolled dice, plus one additional die per (op) spent this way. These become dropped dice. When making a check with the same skill before end of your next turn, you may roll one fewer (skill) per reserved (skill) and one fewer (ring) per reserved (ring), then add the reserved dice set to their original results. They count as rolled dice.</li></ul>","strikingasearth":"<ul><li>After striking, the bushi roots themself to the ground, hunkering down to make sure their armor takes the brunt of a hit or raising a weapon in a warding position where it can deflect harm without being damaged.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Earth) check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Earth +(op): Treat your physical resistance as 1 higher per (op) spent this way until beginning of your next turn.</li></ul>","strikingasfire":"<ul><li>Victory cannot be achieved through defense alone, and it is a poor student of the sword who forgets that their most important goal is simple: cut down their enemy. All else fades to the background as the bushi fiercely presses the attack, trying to force an error or open an opportunity to end their foe.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Fire) Attack action check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Fire +(op): The next time your target suffers a Critical Strike, increase its severity by 1 per (op) spent this way. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","strikingasvoid":"<ul><li>The future is part of Void’s domain, infinite in possibility and unfathomable in depth. Because of its formlessness, one cannot scheme to undermine the uncertain future—but the instant it takes shape, an action is vulnerable to countermeasures. The bushi rests until the last possible second, allowing the potential energy of their strike to take shape only after it is too late for their enemy to respond.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Void) check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Void (op): Immediately switch to a different stance of your choice.</li><li>Void (op): If you fail, you may perform another action. This must be an action you have not yet performed this turn. You can only activate this opportunity once per round.</li></ul>","strikingaswater":"<ul><li>The finest armor is useless if a warrior can bypass it, slipping a blade through the gaps that allow the wearer to move or using blunt, concussive force to create a space. As the bushi strikes, they attempt to slide past the target’s defenses to deliver a lethal blow.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee, Ranged, or Unarmed] (Water) Attack action check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Water +(op): Your target treats their physical resistance as 1 lower per (op) spent this way. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","suddendownpourstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check using a bow or polearm, if you are mounted, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op)(op): If your target makes a check to resist an effect of this Attack action (including a check to resist a critical strike), increase the TN of that check by your mount&#x27;s Water ring.</li></ul>","swallowsdartstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: While you perform a Movement action check, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op)(op): Next time you defend against damage, reduce damage by focus minus physical resistance of your armor (instead of normal resistance). Persists until start of next turn.</li></ul>","swayinggrassevasion":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Movement and Support action, if you are in Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain, you may receive fatigue up to your ranks in Survival to duck into cover.</li><li>Increase the TN of Martial Arts [Ranged] checks targeting you by half the fatigue received this way (rounded up). Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","swirlingtempeststyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] check with a blunt weapon or polearm, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>(op)+: Choose one character in range of your weapon (not your target) with vigilance lower than or equal to (op) spent. That character suffers physical damage equal to weapon&#x27;s base damage. May activate multiple times choosing different characters.</li></ul>","swirlingviperstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you perform a Maneuver action during your turn, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Air or Water (op)(op): After you move, perform a Strike action using a readied ranged weapon targeting one character in range (TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance). Can only target a character you moved away from.</li></ul>","tacticalassessment":"<ul><li>Akodo’s Leadership and Bayushi’s Lies agree on a few topics, for both leaders were practical to a certain degree, even if Akodo famously scorned many of Bayushi’s methods. As the scholar Hida Fuyuko noted in her revelatory commentary on Leadership’s lessons for commanders on the Kaiu Wall, the most famous meeting of these two minds comes on the matter of preparation: battles are not won in the field, but in the leadup to the conflict. Even in small clashes, the warrior who better understands the terrain, the strength of their own forces, and the composition of the enemy’s troops is usually victorious.</li><li>When you make an Initiative check, you may spend (op):</li><li>Air (op): Choose an enemy. Learn one of their advantages (their choice) and their physical or supernatural resistance (your choice).</li><li>Earth (op): Choose a character. They do not apply any of their disadvantages to their checks until end of their first turn.</li><li>Water (op): Choose a piece of Terrain. Until start of your first turn, it counts as having the Obscuring quality for Attack action checks targeting you and your allies.</li><li>Fire (op): Choose a character and one of their advantages you know. Until end of their first turn, they apply that advantage to all of their checks.</li></ul>","tailsweep":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as Attack and Movement action, make Martial Arts [Unarmed] check targeting one character at range 0-2. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance minus 1 (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers physical damage equal to Fitness ranks plus bonus successes with deadliness 1.</li><li>Opportunities: Earth (op): If you succeed, target suffers Prone; if already Prone, suffers Immobilized instead. Water (op)(op): If you fail, immediately move 1 range band.</li></ul>","thicketsembracestyle":"<ul><li>Type: Kata</li><li>Subtype: Close Combat Kata</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] or Fitness check</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you are in Entangling or Obscuring terrain, reduce the TN of the next attack check you make by 1 (to a minimum of 1). This effect persists until the end of your next turn. (op)(op): If you are in Entangling or Obscuring terrain, you may ignore its negative effects. This effect persists until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","thunderboltstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check in which you throw your weapon, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op)+: Choose another character at range 0-1 of your target with vigilance lower than your ranks in Fitness plus (op) spent this way. That character suffers damage equal to your weapon&#x27;s base damage. Can activate multiple times, choosing different characters each time.</li></ul>","thunderclapstrike":"<ul><li>Sweeping their weapon in a wide arc, the bushi lashes out at their foes, driving them back to make an opening for their next move.</li><li>As an Attack action using a readied weapon, make a TN 3 Martial Arts [Melee or Unarmed] (Air) check targeting each character within weapon&#x27;s range.</li><li>If you succeed, each target suffers damage equal to weapon&#x27;s base damage and must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Earth 4, Fire 1) or move 2 range bands directly away from you.</li><li>Air +(op): Increase the TN of checks to resist the effect by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","thunderousblowsstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make an Attack action check with a blunt weapon, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Fire (op)(op)+: One character at range 0-1 of your target per (op)(op) spent receives 1 fatigue, or 3 fatigue if suffering the Dazed condition.</li></ul>","thunderoushoovesstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a Fitness check as part of a Movement action while mounted, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>(op)+: One character at range 0 of your ending position per (op) spent suffers fatigue and strife equal to your mount&#x27;s silhouette unless they immediately move 1 range band away. (op)(op): Your mount may perform a Strike action with your assistance targeting one character at range 0.</li></ul>","tigerslungestyle":"<ul><li>Activation: While you perform a Movement action check, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op)+: Choose a character at range 0-1 with focus lower than or equal to Fitness ranks plus (op) spent. That character must move 1 range band away and suffer Dazed unless they choose to receive strife equal to your Fire ring.</li></ul>","triptheleg":"<ul><li>Type: Kata</li><li>Subtype: Close Combat Kata</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: As an Attack action using one readied polearm</li><li>Check: TN 2 Martial Arts [Melee] targeting one character at range 1-2</li><li>If you succeed, your target suffers the Prone condition.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you succeed, the target receives 2 fatigue and 2 strife. (op)+: If target&#x27;s vigilance is lower than or equal to (op) spent this way, they suffer the Disoriented condition.</li></ul>","tumblingoakstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: While you make an Attack action check using a staff (bo) or blunt weapon, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: If this check causes targets to make a check to resist a condition, critical strike, or other effect, increase TN of that check by 2 per (op) spent.</li></ul>","twinstreamsstyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you perform an Attack action check using a sword or ax, if you have another readied weapon of the same category, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>(op)(op): If target suffers a critical strike, increase its severity by the deadliness of your other readied weapon.</li></ul>","veiledmenacestyle":"<ul><li>Assassination and other clandestine tactics are frowned upon by many samurai. None can deny the effectiveness of such techniques, however. By drawing their enemy’s gaze away from the true threat, a bushi can often tip the scales against a strong foe.</li><li>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Unarmed] Attack action check using a weapon in a one-handed grip, you may spend (op):</li><li>+(op): If you succeed, choose one unaware or Disoriented target. That target suffers a Critical Strike with severity equal to weapon&#x27;s deadliness plus 1 per (op) spent this way beyond the first.</li></ul>","voidembracestyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a Meditation (Void) check during a duel or skirmish, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>(op)(op): Choose one character you can perceive, then secretly select a number. Next time you are dealt damage or suffer a critical strike from that character, reveal the number. If number is higher than damage/severity, suffer as normal. If lower or equal, reduce by that amount (minimum 0). If reduced to 0, character suffers 5 strife. If critical strike reduced to 0, you do not suffer it. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","warriorsresolve":"<ul><li>The bushi draws a deep breath, exhaling as they rise to their feet. Pain can be conquered as long as there is a duty to be done. Honor is stronger than steel, it is said, and it falls to the samurai to prove it.</li><li>Once per scene, as a Support action, you may spend 1 Void Points to recover.</li><li>Remove fatigue equal to your Honor rank.</li></ul>","waspsspitestyle":"<ul><li>Activation: When you perform a Martial Arts [Ranged] check, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Air or Void (op)(op): If you did not succeed, choose another target at range 0-2 of your target with vigilance lower than or equal to your target&#x27;s. New target suffers physical damage equal to weapon&#x27;s base damage.</li></ul>","wheelingsweep":"<ul><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action targeting a character with silhouette 2 or lower using unarmed punch profile, make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Water) check targeting one character at range 0. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, hurl target 1 range band in direction of your choice plus 1 per two bonus successes. Target suffers effects of falling the distance moved.</li></ul>","airfist":"<ul><li>The monk swirls their hands in an intricate pattern, channeling their ki into the air and turning even a placid breeze into a funnel of roaring wind. A gale follows the monk’s strikes, hurling foes back and slamming them against intervening objects.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 1 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Air) check. You may choose one other character at range 0-1 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>Treat the maximum range of your Punch and Kick unarmed profiles as equal to your Air Ring.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Target suffers physical damage equal to your Air Ring. Target must make a TN 4 Fitness check (Earth 5, Fire 2) or be pushed 1 range band away from you, plus range bands equal to their shortfall.</li></ul>","auraawareness":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 2 Meditation (Void)</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, perceive beings normally invisible to human sight (spirits, supernaturally concealed characters). After a character or object at range 0-3 activates a supernatural ability, become aware of it and its effects. However, natural senses are diminished: treat Vigilance as 2 lower (minimum 1) for non-supernatural effects, and increase TN of checks to detect non-supernatural characters, objects, and phenomena by 2.</li><li>Burst Effect: 2+ bonus successes: During next Attack action check targeting an Otherworldly being, treat its resistances as reduced by ranks in Theology. Persists until end of next turn.</li></ul>","blisteringretribution":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 1 Meditation (Fire) to empower counterstrikes with ki.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, after you defend against damage dealt by a character in the scene, decrease TN of your next Attack or Scheme action check targeting that character by half the fatigue you received from defending (rounded up, minimum TN 1).</li><li>Burst Effect: 3+ bonus successes: Next time you defend against damage, each other character at range 0-2 suffers physical damage equal to your ranks in Fitness. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","breakingblow":"<ul><li>A kihō practitioner skilled in aligning their energy to the element of Fire can deliver a strike that forces a spark of ki into an object and ignites the latent energy within; causing the object to explode or shatter.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 1 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Fire) check. You may choose one object at range 0-1 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>When you succeed at a Martial Arts [Unarmed] check against a target, choose one worn armor or readied weapon in target&#x27;s possession. It gains Damaged unless the target chooses to receive 2 fatigue.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Chosen object gains Damaged. At GM&#x27;s discretion, can shatter tough mundane objects (wooden doors, earthen walls, trees). 4+ bonus successes: Chosen object gains Destroyed instead. Can destroy reinforced mundane objects (metal doors, stone walls).</li></ul>","channelthefiredragon":"<ul><li>Fire is not just destruction; it is also life. The monk inhales sharply, igniting their ki to strengthen themself. While this life-giving fire smolders within their lungs, the monk is largely immune to cold weather and flames alike. Ki practitioners experienced in this art can even exhale scorching torrents of flame.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 2 Meditation (Fire) check. You may choose to have each other character at range 0-1 become a target for the burst effect.</li><li>Automatically succeed on all checks to resist extreme weather with bonus successes equal to your Fire Ring. If you would suffer damage from physical or supernatural fire (invocations, kihō), you may spend 1 Void Points to prevent that damage and remove that much fatigue instead.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Each target must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 5, Water 2) or suffer physical damage equal to your Fire Ring and Burning. Flammable objects ignite, creating Dangerous terrain at GM&#x27;s discretion.</li></ul>","cleansingspirit":"<ul><li>The monk centers their ki, then reaches out and touches another character, counterbalancing their turbulent energies with the stillness of the monk’s own soul. This restores the character’s spirit, driving out poison, disease, and even the grip of evil spirits, provided they have not yet taken root in the character’s soul.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Earth) check. You may choose one other character at range 0-1 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>Reduce the TN of all your checks to resist poison, disease, Mahō, the Defiled terrain quality, and the effects of Otherworldly and Tainted beings by your Earth Ring.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Remove one of the following conditions from your target: Afflicted, Bleeding, Dazed, Disoriented, Dying, Fatigued, or Intoxicated.</li></ul>","cuttingwindtalons":"<ul><li>Activation: Scheme and Support action, TN 1 Fitness (Air) to enhance unarmed strikes. Choose one character at range 0-3 as target for Burst effect.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, your unarmed attacks have Razor-Sharp quality.</li><li>Burst Effect: 2+ bonus successes: Reduce TN of next Attack action check against target by your ranks in Skulduggery. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","danceoffire":"<ul><li>Activation: Movement and Support action, TN 2 Performance (Fire) to empower body with exceptional energy.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, if you would fail a check, you must receive 2 fatigue to roll 1 additional (ring) and keep it. If this would not cause you to succeed, repeat until you succeed or become Incapacitated. After becoming Incapacitated by fatigue this way, gain Exhausted condition; if already Exhausted, gain Dying [3 rounds] instead.</li><li>Burst Effect: 2+ bonus successes: Treat focus as increased by your Fire ring and increase initiative by the same amount. Persists 1 round. When ending, receive 2 fatigue to persist one additional round.</li></ul>","deathtouch":"<ul><li>The monk delivers a blow to a single point on their target’s body and gives a dread proclamation that echoes across the ensuing stillness. The lucky are merely wounded by this experience, but a single brush from a master of such a deadly ki technique can be fatal.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 3 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Void) check. You may choose a character at range 0-1 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>When you perform an Attack action using a Punch or Kick, the target cannot defend against the damage you deal unless they spend 1 Void Points.</li><li>3+ bonus successes: Target suffers Dazed and Disoriented and must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check or suffer Unconscious. 4+ bonus successes against a minion NPC: target is simply slain.</li></ul>","earthneedsnoeyes":"<ul><li>The monk who waits and listens sees much, even without eyes. Sending out waves of their own energy and letting the ki of the life around them flow back into their body through the ground, the monk feels the reverberations of everything moving nearby, from the thunderous breaths of a warrior in battle to the footsteps of the tiniest ants.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Meditation (Earth) check.</li><li>You can use vibrations through the earth to &#x27;see&#x27; a number of range bands in all directions equal to your Earth Ring. Increase your vigilance by your Earth Ring.</li><li>3+ bonus successes: Instantly become aware of all living creatures and objects touching the ground within range bands equal to your Earth Ring plus bonus successes.</li></ul>","earthenfist":"<ul><li>Placing their hand on the ground, the monk draws forth the hardness of stone, pulling up clumps of rocky soil that coat their skin or invisibly reinforcing their bones and muscles with the durability of granite.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 1 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Earth) check. You may choose a character at range 0-1 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>Treat base damage of your unarmed Punch and Kick profiles as increased by your Earth Ring. Increase your physical resistance by 1.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Target suffers physical damage equal to your Earth Ring. Target must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 2, Water 5) or suffer Prone.</li></ul>","essenceofstillness":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 3 Fitness (Void)</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, ignore the effects of Bleeding, Lightly Wounded, Heavily Wounded, and Unconscious conditions.</li><li>Burst Effect: 2+ bonus successes: Ignore effects of Dying condition until end of scene. If Dying is removed before end of scene, you do not die even if duration expired.</li></ul>","eternalmindsgate":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 3 Meditation (Void)</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, identify locations, objects, and individuals related to your past life (but not reincarnations). Become aware of the general nature of your relationship with them, without specific memories.</li><li>Burst Effect: 3+ bonus successes: Choose two skills in the same group and swap their values. Must explain details about the past life. GM is final arbiter. Persists until end of game session.</li></ul>","fistofspreadingvenom":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 1 Medicine (Water) and expend one charge of a poison to imbue unarmed strikes. You suffer no ill effects from consuming a poison this way. Choose one other character at range 0-1 as target for Burst effect.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, your unarmed attacks count as having the consumed poison applied to them.</li><li>Burst Effect: 3+ bonus successes: Target counts as having ingested one dose of the poison and immediately suffers its effects.</li></ul>","flamefist":"<ul><li>The monk throws a rapid, reckless strike, and flame streams out, seizing and charring whatever the monk touches. While sustaining this kihō, the monk’s hands and feet trail fire, lending power to their strikes.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 1 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Fire) check. You may choose a character at range 0-1 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>Treat the deadliness of your unarmed Punch and Kick profiles as increased by your Fire Ring and treat their damage type as supernatural.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Target suffers physical damage equal to your Fire Ring and must make a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 5, Water 2) or suffer Dazed.</li></ul>","freezingthelifeblood":"<ul><li>The monk touches a single point on the target’s body and, with an icy stare, causes the ki within the target to seize up, contracting muscles into a spasmed state and then making them fall slack.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 2 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Water) check. You may choose one character at range 0-1 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>After a character defends against damage you inflict with an Attack action using a Punch or Kick, they suffer Immobilized unless they choose to receive 3 fatigue.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Water Ring (ignoring resistance) and Immobilized. 4+ bonus successes: Target suffers a Critical Strike with severity equal to your Water Ring plus ranks in Medicine instead.</li></ul>","graceofthegentlebreeze":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 2 Survival (Air). Choose any number of characters at range 0-3 as targets for Burst effect.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, characters unaware of your presence treat their vigilance as 2 lower when you make checks to avoid notice, and increase TN of checks to look for you by +2. Animals are not disturbed by your presence.</li><li>Burst Effect: 1+ bonus successes: Each target with vigilance lower than or equal to bonus successes loses track of you, becoming unaware of your location.</li></ul>","grasptheearthdragon":"<ul><li>Planting a foot on the ground and taking a wide stance, the monk stomps, sending reverberations of ki rushing down into the depths. An instant later, the monk’s body is filled with the resilience of bedrock; stones rise and orbit their body to deflect attacks, rocks adhere to their flesh forming rocky scales, or their flesh becomes as difficult to crack as granite.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 2 Meditation (Earth) check.</li><li>Reduce severity of all Critical Strike from physical sources by your Earth Ring. After a character performs an Attack action against you, you may spend 1 Void Points to cause them to suffer fatigue equal to your ranks in Fitness.</li><li>3+ bonus successes: Reduce all physical damage you suffer to 1. After any character deals physical damage to you, they suffer Prone. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","kiprotection":"<ul><li>The monk touches the injured individual, feeling the flow of their ki and using their own to gently correct its flow. While the monk sustains this kihō, their touch continues to heal, though repeating the effort numerous times is quite draining.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 1 Meditation (Water) check. You may choose one character at range 0-1 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>When you perform the Calming Breath action, you may remove 2 fatigue instead of 1. After you perform an action, you may spend 1 Void Points to remove fatigue equal to your ranks in Medicine from one other character at range 0-1.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Target removes fatigue equal to your ranks in Medicine plus your bonus successes. Each target cannot be affected by this again until end of scene.</li></ul>","mercyofthestonefortune":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 1 Meditation (Earth)</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, when another friendly character at range 0-1 defends against damage, you may receive fatigue up to your Earth ring to reduce their damage by that amount. When a friendly character at range 0-1 suffers a critical strike, you may spend 1 Void point to suffer it instead.</li><li>Burst Effect: 2+ bonus successes: Treat Fitness ranks as increased by 2 (max 6) for checks to resist critical strikes and conditions; persists rounds equal to bonus successes.</li></ul>","rejuvenatingbreath":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 2 Fitness (Earth). Once per session, spend 1 Void point to perform even while Incapacitated or Unconscious.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, increase your endurance by your Earth ring.</li><li>Burst Effect: 3+ bonus successes: Remove Heavily Wounded condition and gain Lightly Wounded for the same ring, or remove Unconscious condition.</li></ul>","ridethewaterdragon":"<ul><li>The monk shifts their stance and moves with inexorable purpose, making their ki fluid and allowing mystical energy to ripple off them like harmless raindrops.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 3 Meditation (Water) check.</li><li>When you are targeted by a check for an invocation, Mahō, or kihō, increase the TN of the check by your ranks in Meditation. At GM&#x27;s discretion, you may pass through certain supernatural barriers and wards without triggering their effects.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Remove all persistent effects from supernatural sources (invocations, mahō, kihō) from yourself. 4+ bonus successes: Remove all such effects from all characters at range 0-2 instead.</li></ul>","ridingtheclouds":"<ul><li>The monk inhales and lets go their earthly bonds to ascend to new heights. Lifted by a small tornado, an invisible current of air, or even a cloud, the monk can move far more freely. While this current of wind does not fully negate the effects of gravity, it allows the user to traverse terrain they otherwise could not and enhances their athleticism greatly.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 2 Meditation (Air) check.</li><li>When you move 1+ range bands, you may move that number plus 1, and you may move 1 of those range bands vertically or horizontally. You may ignore effects of Terrain while moving. If you fall, treat the distance as 1 range band.</li><li>1+ bonus successes: Immediately move 1 range band, plus one additional per bonus success. May move vertically or horizontally, ignoring terrain.</li></ul>","riversflowingstride":"<ul><li>Activation: Movement and Support action, TN 2 Fitness (Water) to make body fluid and malleable.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, do not suffer damage from terrain qualities while performing Movement actions. When targeted by Attack action check, spend 1 Void point to reduce attacker&#x27;s bonus successes by your Water ring (minimum 0 bonus successes).</li><li>Burst Effect: 1+ bonus successes: Immediately move up to 2 range bands. During this movement, may pass through small gaps that would normally prevent movement so long as it accommodates your head.</li></ul>","seepingki":"<ul><li>Activation: Attack and Support action, TN 3 Meditation (Water) to imbue your touch with spreading ki.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, after succeeding at an unarmed Attack action check, target receives strife equal to Medicine ranks. If this causes Compromised, target must resist with TN 4 Meditation (Fire 5, Earth 2). If failed, on their next turn they must unmask in one of your chosen ways: move away, Strike an ally, drop a held item, or other effect. You choose which dice the character keeps. Minion NPCs automatically fail the resistance check.</li><li>Burst Effect: 2+ bonus successes: Next successful unarmed Attack action check inflicts Bleeding condition. Persists until end of next turn.</li></ul>","shadowofancientpeaks":"<ul><li>Activation: Scheme or Support action, TN 3 Tactics (Earth)</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, after you succeed at a check to resist an effect or critical strike, the character whose effect you resisted receives strife equal to your bonus successes.</li><li>Burst Effect: 2+ bonus successes: Next time you suffer a critical strike and reduce it to severity 0 or lower with Fitness check, remove fatigue equal to the severity (before reductions). Persists until end of next turn.</li></ul>","stepofthestorm":"<ul><li>Activation: Movement and Support action, TN 3 Fitness (Air). Once per session, spend 1 Void point to perform immediately after being declared target of another character&#x27;s Attack action.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, when targeted by an Attack action check, gain 1 fatigue to negate 1 (op) from attacker&#x27;s check. At end of your turn, you must move 1 range band.</li><li>Burst Effect: 2+ bonus successes: Immediately move 2 range bands.</li></ul>","stilltheelements":"<ul><li>The monk seeks the infinite Void within themself, delving into their ki and pushing back spiritual beings and tipping the balance between the elements as they desire. Kansen, kami, other spiritual powers, and sometimes even mortals are repelled by the emptiness in the monk.</li><li>As an Intrigue and Support action, make a TN 4 Meditation (Void) check. When you perform this action, choose Air, Earth, Fire, or Water.</li><li>When you are targeted by a check using the chosen ring, you may choose 1 kept die from the check and set it to a blank face. You may spend 1 Void Points to choose additional kept dice up to your ranks in Meditation and set them to blank faces.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: The Terrain at range 0-3 becomes Imbalanced [Chosen Element] until end of scene.</li></ul>","thebodyisananvil":"<ul><li>The monk focuses their ki to the point where they expect a foe’s blow to land, expelling energy to counter the force of the strike. Weapons have been known to shatter into clouds of sparks and chunks of metal when touching a monk’s body, unmade by the force of the monk’s inner energy.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 3 Meditation (Fire) check. You may choose a character at range 0-2 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>When you defend against damage from an Attack action, the character who attacked you suffers supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring and Dazed.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Before you defend against damage dealt by the target, reduce the damage by your Fire Ring. If you successfully defend, one weapon the target used gains Damaged, and the target suffers Burning.</li></ul>","thegreatsilence":"<ul><li>The monk swirls their hands in a spiral, pulling noise inward and stealing even the reverberations that sounds make through the air. Lies die on the lips unspoken, and prayers never reach the spirits for whom they were intended. Skilled practitioners often maintain this technique, twisting the wind around them to steal away pernicious words and wicked prayers alike.</li><li>As a Scheme and Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Air) check.</li><li>Increase the TN of Scheme action checks targeting you by one plus your ranks in Command.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Characters at range 0-3 suffer Silenced and cannot hear. Persists until beginning of your next turn.</li></ul>","touchthevoiddragon":"<ul><li>The root of the universe is nothing and everything, and the monk pursues this spiral to its depths, finding limitless power within. The monk sees many realities swirl around them while maintaining this kihō, the storm of possibilities slowly solidifying into the present. Thus, they can jump at opportunities that might otherwise have passed them by.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 4 Meditation (Void) check.</li><li>You may spend (op) from Void checks as if it were (op) from a check using any Element. You may spend (op) from Air, Earth, Fire, or Water checks as if it were (op) from a Void check.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Gain 1 Void Points. You can only gain 1 Void point from this effect per scene.</li></ul>","volcanicfist":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 3 Fitness (Fire). Once per session, spend 1 Void point to perform immediately after succeeding on an Attack action check, before resolving results.</li><li>Enhancement Effect: While active, increase TN of checks to resist critical strikes you inflict by unarmed attacks by your Fire ring plus your ranks in Fitness.</li><li>Burst Effect: 1+ bonus successes: Unarmed attacks treat damage and deadliness as increased by Fitness ranks plus bonus successes. Persists 1 round. Receive 2 fatigue to persist one additional round.</li></ul>","waterfist":"<ul><li>The monk throws a soft blow against a nearby object and makes their ki as water, rippling across intervening objects and sliding past protections to reach its destination. The force of the strike travels through any contact surface, striking another target touching it, even if they are on the other side of a wooden door, stone wall, or other physical barrier.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 1 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Water) check. You may choose one character at range 0-3 who shares a contact surface with you as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>Your Attack checks using Punch or Kick ignore an amount of target&#x27;s physical resistance up to two times your Water Ring. You may spend 1 Void Points to perform an unarmed attack through any solid surface your target is touching, as long as you are both in contact with the same surface at range 0 to your Water Ring.</li><li>If you succeed: Target suffers physical damage equal to your Water Ring.</li></ul>","wayoftheearthquake":"<ul><li>The monk slams a hand or foot into the ground, and the earth itself shudders under the weight of the blow as their ki rushes through the soil. Nearby enemies are hurled to the ground and find it shifting treacherously underneath them as they struggle to rise.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 2 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Earth) check. You may choose any number of other characters at range 0-1 as targets for the burst effect.</li><li>After you perform an Attack or Support action, or defend against damage, you may choose one other character at range 0-2 who must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 2, Water 5) or suffer physical damage equal to your Earth Ring and Prone.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Each target suffers physical damage equal to your Earth Ring. Each Prone target suffers physical damage equal to your Earth Ring plus bonus successes and Immobilized instead.</li></ul>","wayoftheedgelesssword":"<ul><li>The wise know that it is not the blade that cuts, but the swordmaster. After all, the Tao of Shinsei teaches that weapons are simply another tool, no more sacred than a harvesting thresher or plow. The monk runs their hand along an object, channeling ki into it and transforming it into a killing edge, even if it appears to be nothing more than a common stick, a wooden sword, or their wizened hand.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 3 Meditation check. You may choose any number of characters at range 0-1 as targets.</li><li>Treat the base damage and deadliness of your unarmed profile and improvised weapons you wield as equal to your ranks in Martial Arts [Unarmed] plus your Void Ring. They count as possessing Durable and Razor-Edged.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Each target suffers a Critical Strike with deadliness equal to your Void Ring plus ranks in Martial Arts [Unarmed].</li></ul>","wayofthefallingstar":"<ul><li>The monk hurls a series of rapid strikes. With each one, fire or rippling heat erupts from their palm, elbow, foot, or other striking surface scorching their target.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 3 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Fire) check. You may choose one character at range 0-2 as the target for the burst effect.</li><li>When you perform an Attack action using a Punch or Kick against a Dazed target, increase the damage you inflict by your Fire Ring.</li><li>3+ bonus successes: Target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring plus your ranks in Fitness. Target must resist with a TN 5 Fitness check (Air 6, Water 3) or suffer Burning and Dazed.</li></ul>","wayoftheseafoam":"<ul><li>The monk shifts and matches their movements to their surroundings, sliding to their feet and righting themself like a duck bobbing to the surface of a pond. In this state, the monk can even traverse water, their ki buoying them where they contact the waves.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 1 Meditation (Water) check.</li><li>You may walk on water as if it were solid ground.</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Remove Immobilized and Prone from yourself. Then switch to any stance and move up to 2 range bands.</li></ul>","wayofthewillow":"<ul><li>The oak stands firm against the storm and breaks, but the willow survives it by bending. The monk dances on the wind like the willow, feeling the currents of ki upon the air and moving out of the way of attacks effortlessly.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 3 Meditation (Air) check.</li><li>When a character performs an Attack action check targeting you, reduce any damage you suffer by 2 for each kept die containing (op).</li><li>2+ bonus successes: Increase the TN of Attack action checks targeting you by your ranks in Meditation until beginning of your next turn.</li></ul>","distancedistorted":"<ul><li>Activation: Scheme and Support action, TN 3 Theology (Void), target two objects/characters at range 0-3</li><li>Augment and curse targets; choose range 0, 1, 2, or 3; targets always treat each other as that distance; each character target receives 2 fatigue; persists until end of next turn</li><li>Magnitude: 1-2: persists additional rounds; 3+: persists until end of scene</li></ul>","essenceeternal":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 4 Theology (Void), target one character or object at range 0-2</li><li>Bind target to current state and location (note fatigue, strife, conditions, persistent effects, critical strikes suffered, position); when effect ends, target returns to noted state even if no longer existing; target remembers everything; persists until end of next turn</li><li>Magnitude: 1-3: persists additional rounds; 4+: target returns to noted state at end of each of your turns for rest of scene</li></ul>","etherealflicker":"<ul><li>Activation: Scheme and Support action, TN 3 Theology (Void), target yourself</li><li>Augment and curse self to be out of phase; use Theology instead of Fitness to reduce critical strike severity; if reduced to 0, do not suffer it; persists until start of next turn</li><li>Magnitude: 1-2: persists additional rounds; 2+: redirect critical strike (severity before reductions) to character at range 0-1 with vigilance &lt;= magnitude; 3+: persists until end of scene</li></ul>","hurlfromthestream":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene, Scheme action, Theology (Void), TN = target&#x27;s vigilance + silhouette (silhouette only for objects), target one character or object at range 0-3</li><li>Bind target outside reality; unaffected by everything and affects nothing; returns after 1 round</li><li>Magnitude: 1-3: removed for additional rounds; 4+: Adversary/PC removed until end of scene; Minion/mundane object ceases to exist permanently</li></ul>","moonontheshiftingsea":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene, Scheme and Support action, TN 3 Theology (Void), target position at range 0-2</li><li>Simultaneously exist at current position and target position (must be reachable by normal movement); can receive 2 fatigue to choose additional targets or target same target multiple times from multiple positions; persists for rounds equal to Meditation ranks; when effect ends, choose one position and cease to occupy all others</li><li>Magnitude: 1-2: persists additional rounds; 1+: one additional position per magnitude; 3+: persists until end of scene (1 fatigue per position per round)</li></ul>","onewithinthevoid":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 2 Sentiment (Void), target yourself and one other character at range 0-3</li><li>Augment targets with wordless communication; any target may receive 2 fatigue to assist another regardless of distance; persists until end of scene</li><li>Magnitude: 1+: strife can be redirected to another target; 3+: choose ring or skill, any target may use another target&#x27;s rank</li></ul>","realitystitch":"<ul><li>Activation: Scheme action, Theology (Void), TN = highest vigilance among targets, target up to Meditation ranks characters at range 0-2</li><li>Curse targets; whenever one receives strife or fatigue, all targets receive same amount; persists until end of scene</li><li>Magnitude: 1+: conditions shared; 2+: critical strikes shared; 3+: persistent effects shared and removed together</li></ul>","shatteringcaress":"<ul><li>Activation: Attack action with readied melee weapon, TN 3 Martial Arts [Melee or Unarmed] (Void), target one character or mundane object in range</li><li>Mundane object gains Destroyed quality. Character takes supernatural damage equal to weapon&#x27;s base damage; if Incapacitated, suffer Dying [3 rounds]</li><li>Magnitude: 1-2: reduce Dying duration by magnitude; 3+: target killed outright instead of Dying</li></ul>","shroudinsolitude":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 3 Theology (Void), target one character at range 0</li><li>Augment and curse target; use Void Ring to reduce damage instead of normal resistance; fatigue becomes strife instead; persists until end of next turn</li><li>Magnitude: 1-2: persists additional rounds; 3+: persists until end of scene; if target becomes Compromised, must resist with TN 5 Meditation (Void 3) or body is pulled into Void permanently</li></ul>","sightbeyondexistence":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per session, immediately after an action of great consequence, TN 2 Theology (Void), target that character at range 0-3</li><li>Scry for another outcome; return to the moment before the action; all effects undone; only you and target are aware. If you are the target, choose same or different action. If another character is the target, say up to five words before they act</li><li>Magnitude: 1+: see one consequence before end of scene; 2+: see consequence in next year; 3+: see consequence in decades</li></ul>","slipthecycle":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per session, Movement and Support action, TN 3 Theology (Void); can be made even if restrained, Incapacitated, Unconscious, dead, or nonexistent</li><li>Purify self; remove all conditions and persistent effects; fatigue and strife become 0; move to position at range 0-2 ignoring obstacles; if dead or nonexistent, return for 1 round</li><li>Magnitude: 1: return until end of scene; 2-3: return until end of session; 4+: return permanently (permanently increase TN by 1)</li></ul>","thelotusblooms":"<ul><li>Activation: Scheme and Support action, TN 3 Theology (Void), target one character at range 0-1</li><li>Augment and curse target; they keep dice up to Void Ring instead of ring used (must keep as many as possible); no strife from kept strife results, but receive 1 fatigue per strife instead; if Incapacitated this way, also gain Exhausted; persists until end of target&#x27;s next turn</li><li>Magnitude: 1-2: persists additional rounds; 3+: persists until end of scene</li></ul>","threeheartbeats":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 4 Theology (Void), target yourself</li><li>Receive 3 fatigue, then take an additional turn immediately; others count as unaware of you and cannot react, but still make checks to resist effects and defend against damage</li><li>Magnitude: 1+: take additional turns equal to magnitude; each additional turn beyond the first costs 3 more fatigue; if Incapacitated, suffer Dying [3 rounds] and Exhausted</li></ul>","unweave":"<ul><li>Activation: Attack and Scheme action, TN 4 Theology (Void), target one character or object silhouette 0-3 at range 0-2</li><li>Mundane object or Minion NPC ceases to exist (receive fatigue = silhouette + conflict rank). Mystical object gains Damaged/Destroyed. Adversary/PC suffers supernatural damage equal to Theology ranks ignoring all resistances</li><li>Magnitude: 1+: additional damage equal to magnitude; 2+: terrain within magnitude range bands loses all qualities; 2+: if target gets critical/Destroyed, ceases to exist; 3+: all characters with vigilance &lt;= magnitude become targets</li></ul>","whisperedblade":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 2 Theology (Void)</li><li>Summon a rift in reality usable as a knife that ignores all resistances; persists until end of scene</li><li>Magnitude: 1+: after Attack, rift echoes summoned at range 0 of target for magnitude rounds; in skirmish when they end, each character (not you) at range 0-1 suffers critical strike equal to deadliness times number of echoes; in other conflicts, targets treat all terrain as Dangerous while echoes persist</li></ul>","witnesstheend":"<ul><li>Activation: Scheme and Support action, Theology (Void), TN = target&#x27;s vigilance (or 2 for objects), target one character or object at range 0-1</li><li>Scry for the ways target can be undone; TN of next check to damage/sabotage/attack it becomes 1 (cannot be increased); persists until end of next turn</li><li>Magnitude: 1-3: persists additional rounds equal to magnitude; 2+: can also target metaphysical objects; 4+: persists until end of scene</li></ul>","amaterasusgaze":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 1 Theology (Fire), target one character or item silhouette 2 or lower at range 0-3</li><li>Summon pleasant sunlight that follows target, providing light at range 0-2 for 1 + bonus success rounds</li></ul>","armorofearth":"<ul><li>Earth is the Element of protection, as evidenced by this invocation. When a shugenja performs this invocation, shards of stone fly toward them, fastening around them to clad them in rocky armor.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Earth) check targeting yourself.</li><li>You summon and equip a suit of armor that grants physical resistance equal to your Earth Ring plus bonus successes and has the Cumbersome and Wargear qualities. Persists for rounds equal to your Earth Ring, then tumbles to the ground as loose stones.</li><li>Earth (op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li><li>Earth (op): The armor has the Durable quality.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): The armor has the Sacred quality.</li></ul>","armorofradiance":"<ul><li>By appealing to the fire kami that slumber within an object, a shugenja can turn a set of armor into a weapon. The fire kami’s creative energy expands rapidly as the incantation ends, causing shimmering radiance to burst forth into a halo of fire that encircles the armor and the wearer, searing their foes.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Fire) check targeting one set of armor at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment the target armor, enveloping it in blinding radiance and searing heat (that do not affect the wearer). When a character at range 0-1 of the wearer begins their turn, they suffer Burning and Dazed. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes.</li><li>Fire (op): The armor gains the Wargear quality.</li><li>Fire (op)(op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li></ul>","bindtheshadow":"<ul><li>When confronting a Tainted being, the shugenja can call forth the pure spirit of a small sanctified object to weaken or even paralyze the monster.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 3 Theology (Earth) check targeting one Otherworldly being at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, crackling arcs of jade light smite and purify your target; it must resist with a TN 4 Fitness (Air 2, Water 5) check or suffer Immobilized and Silenced. Persists for rounds equal to your Earth Ring.</li><li>Earth (op): Each target that fails is bound until end of the scene instead.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): Each target that fails is bound for one year instead.</li><li>Earth (op)(op)+: Increase TN of checks to resist by 1 per (op)(op) spent this way.</li><li>Earth (op)(op)(op): Each target that fails is bound for one hundred years instead.</li></ul>","bitingsteel":"<ul><li>Flame, passion, and ingenuity transform ore into steel, and steel into a sword. So too, then, can a shugenja wield flame to transform a sword into an even greater weapon, one with an impossible edge that parts nearly any substance in its ferocity. By drawing a pattern along the naked blade, a shugenja can wake the spirits of fire still sleeping within it.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Fire) check targeting one weapon at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment the weapon with blazing energy. Increase the weapon&#x27;s base damage by your Fire Ring. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes.</li><li>Fire (op): After performing this action, if you have the enhanced weapon readied, immediately perform a Strike action with it.</li><li>Fire +(op): While the effect persists, increase the weapon&#x27;s deadliness by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Fire (op)(op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li></ul>","blessedwind":"<ul><li>The shugenja recites a short chant, and the dust whips up, carried upon twisting currents of air that foil and deflect projectiles. Stones, arrows, and even larger missiles are knocked aside by buffeting winds, keeping the target safe from such attacks.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Air) check targeting one position at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a swirling wind at the target position. Any character at range 0-2 of the chosen position counts as being in Obscuring terrain for Attack actions targeting them. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</li><li>Air (op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li></ul>","boofwater":"<ul><li>A shugenja can invoke the spirits in a nearby pool or stream to take the form of a weapon. This weapon can change form at the bearer’s will, swirling from a staff into a blade in the blink of an eye, and back again.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Water) check to summon a staff made of water from a nearby pool, stream, or airborne vapor.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon and ready a Bō made of water. It has the Snaring quality. At the end of each round, you may transform this weapon into a different melee weapon. Persists until end of any turn in which it leaves your grip or until end of scene.</li><li>Water (op): The weapon can be any kind of melee or ranged weapon instead.</li><li>Water (op): You may immediately perform a Strike action using the weapon.</li><li>Water (op): When performing an Attack action with this weapon, treat its minimum or maximum range as 1 higher or lower.</li></ul>","bondoftherealms":"<ul><li>Activation: Attack and Scheme action, TN 2 Theology (Earth), target one character from another realm and name their realm of origin</li><li>If correct realm named, smite target; reduce endurance and composure by 3 (min 1) for 1 + bonus success rounds. If failed, suffer 3 strife, learn target&#x27;s realm, cannot reuse until end of scene</li></ul>","breathofthefiredragon":"<ul><li>“Fire begins with breath,” or so the Isawa have long said. Some shugenja make this practice literal, calling upon the fire kami to ignite the air they exhale, transforming it into a gout of charring flame. Besides burning foes, it also tends to ignite nearby flammable objects.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 4 Theology (Fire) check targeting one character at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you exhale searing flames that smite the target. The target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring plus two times your bonus successes and Burning. Each character at range 0-1 of the target must make a TN 3 Fitness check (Air 4, Water 1) or suffer supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring.</li></ul>","bythelightofthelordmoon":"<ul><li>When a shugenja performs this invocation, the light shifts to that of a moonlit night, unweaving the shadows to lay bare the things they conceal. Hidden objects glow faintly with silver light, while mystical illusions are revealed as translucent, gossamer forms.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a TN 2 Theology (Air) check targeting an area at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you scry for each hidden character and concealed object (secret compartments, trap doors, concealed weapons) in the targeted area, revealing it with a luminous outline only you can perceive. Only reveals mundane concealment.</li><li>Air +(op): Reveal up to one magically concealed object per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Air (op)(op)+: Choose one additional character at range 0-1 per (op)(op) spent this way who can also see the objects.</li></ul>","calluponthewind":"<ul><li>The shugenja whispers a breathless prayer and rises from the ground as gentle winds bear them aloft. Air spirits usually carry their charges gracefully, without dropping them to stumble the last few feet—usually.</li><li>As a Movement action, make a TN 4 Theology (Air) check targeting yourself.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment your movement with a gust of wind that carries you aloft. You may move vertically freely and ignore the effects of terrain while flying. Persists until end of the scene.</li><li>Air (op)(op)+: While flying, carry up to one additional willing character at range 0-2 per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","caressofearth":"<ul><li>The shugenja draws their hand across a broken item, calling upon the spirits of metal, wood, or stone to restore and fortify it. Splintered planks knit back together, metal glows and writhes before solidifying into a form like new, and stone congeals as liquid before freezing back into form.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 3 Theology (Earth) check targeting one item with Damaged or Destroyed at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you mend the target, removing the Damaged or Destroyed quality from it.</li><li>Earth (op): One target gains the Durable quality until end of the scene.</li></ul>","cloakofnight":"<ul><li>A sufficiently learned shugenja can call forth air kami to play one of their simplest and most effective tricks: enveloping an object or person in their embrace to hide it from sight.</li><li>As a Scheme and Support action, make a Theology (Air) check targeting one object or character at range 0-1. TN equals the target&#x27;s Silhouette.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment the target with an illusion that renders it invisible to the naked eye. The object is still physically present and can be touched, smelled, or sensed with any normal sense other than vision. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</li><li>Air (op)(op)+: Choose one additional target of the same silhouette or smaller per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","courageofseventhunders":"<ul><li>At the dawn of the Empire, the Seven Thunders stood against Fu Leng, and their clash resounded from the Shadowlands to every corner of Rokugan. Earth is the Element of recollection, and from the earth kami, a shugenja can unearth fragments of the memories of these heroes from across the ages and impart them to their comrades in arms. This invocation does not erase fear, but it reminds a samurai of the legacy they must uphold—that others stood against the darkness before and prevailed.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Earth) check targeting a number of characters up to your Earth Ring at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment each target with vigorous resolve; each target increases their composure by your Earth Ring. Persists until end of the scene.</li><li>Earth (op): Each target also increases their endurance by your Earth Ring while this effect persists.</li><li>Earth +(op): Each target removes 1 strife per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): This technique targets each friendly character in range instead.</li></ul>","danceofseasons":"<ul><li>A skilled shugenja can entreat the kami to change the world around them through a rite that seems as much performance as invocation. As the shugenja dances, the water kami mirror the movements and shift the moisture around them from water to ice to vapor and back again. A skilled shugenja might be able to use this to entrap the unwary, drenching them in the waters of a summer storm before plunging them into the frozen heart of winter.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 3 Theology (Water) check targeting one position containing water (pool, river, snow/ice, mist) at range 1-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon the essence of the seasons to freeze, thaw, or evaporate water at range 0-1 of the target position. Ice becomes solid Dangerous terrain. Vapor creates Obscuring terrain. Mud becomes Entangling terrain. Water within living beings is unaffected.</li><li>Water +(op): Choose one additional target position per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Water +(op): Attempt to encase in ice one character in the affected area per (op) spent this way. Each must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Earth 1, Fire 4) or suffer Immobilized and Disoriented.</li></ul>","dominionofsuijin":"<ul><li>A shugenja deeply attuned to the kami of water can see other places in watery reflections. Incredibly powerful practitioners can even use this reflection to transport themself and others to the desired place through the water—even if they arrive slightly damp.</li><li>As a Movement and Scheme action, make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check targeting one position containing a body of water at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you scry in the ripples. The target body of water displays an image of a second body of water of your choice and its surroundings as if the onlooker were just below the surface. The second body must be at range 0-6 and you must have concrete knowledge of it.</li><li>Water (op): You can also hear (very muffled) noises through the pool.</li><li>Water (op): Only you can see the vision; to others, the pool shows no images.</li><li>Water (op): The location can be any distance from you (but must still be familiar).</li><li>Water (op)(op): You may use clouds, fog banks, snow, or sheets of ice as bodies of water for this technique.</li><li>Water (op)(op)(op): You and a number of characters up to your Water Ring may pass through a temporary portal to the other location. One way only; you arrive soaked.</li></ul>","dreampainter":"<ul><li>Activation: Scheme action, TN 3 Theology (Air), target one Unconscious NPC at range 0-3</li><li>Scry into target&#x27;s subconscious; discover one piece of relevant information (ninjō, giri, biggest fear, opinion, pressing issue). If you fail, target wakes aware of meddling</li></ul>","earthbecomessky":"<ul><li>The shugenja makes a short incantation and stomps a foot on the ground, and the earth kami spray torrents of dirt, stones, and even boulders toward their foe.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 3 Theology (Earth) check targeting one character at range 1-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a boulder to smite your target. The target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Earth Ring plus bonus successes and must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Air 1, Water 4) or suffer Prone. If your target is already Prone, double the damage.</li></ul>","earthquake":"<ul><li>Earthquakes are common in some parts of Rokugan, and they are rightly feared—whole villages have been known to vanish when the earth spirits are set to turmoil. To intentionally raise their ire is dangerous, but it is one of the most powerful techniques a shugenja can wield. Ripples shoot across the ground around them as the earth bucks and tumbles. The shugenja’s foes plummet into chasms of darkness and sulfur, entombed forever beneath the ground they once walked.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 5 Theology (Earth) check targeting each other character at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon an earthquake. At the end of each of your turns, each target must resist with a TN 5 Fitness check (Air 3, Water 6) or suffer supernatural damage equal to twice your Earth Ring and Prone. Persists for rounds equal to your Earth Ring.</li><li>Earth (op): Persists until end of the scene, or you may dispel it at any time as an action.</li><li>Earth +(op): Summon a chasm beneath one character in range; that character and anyone at range 0-1 of them fall range bands equal to (op) spent this way into the earth.</li><li>Earth (op)(op)+: Destroy one building or fortification in range per (op)(op) spent this way. Each character inside must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Air 1, Water 4) to escape or suffer a Critical Strike with severity 10.</li></ul>","emboldenedsteed":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 3 Theology (Earth), target any number of mounts at range 0-4</li><li>Augment and mend targets; remove Exhausted condition and strife equal to bonus successes</li></ul>","embraceofkenrojijin":"<ul><li>The shugenja appeals to rumbling subterranean kami, offering the proper prayers to receive safe passage even across places humans were not meant to tread. The spirits shroud the shugenja, allowing them to stick to rocky surfaces or parting the ground to allow passage.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Earth) check targeting yourself.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment yourself with the ability to stick to earthen surfaces, traversing even vertical surfaces made of earth or stone. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes (or one minute in narrative).</li><li>Earth (op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li><li>Earth (op): You can pass through solid earth as if it was water when you move. Supernatural resistance against Earth invocations, kihō, and mahō equal to your Earth Ring.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): Effects also apply to metal. Physical resistance against metal weapons equal to your Earth Ring.</li></ul>","essenceofjade":"<ul><li>Type: Invocation</li><li>Subtype: Earth Invocation</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: As a Support action, make a TN 3 Theology (Earth) check targeting one position at range 0-2.</li><li>Purify the area and remove the Defiled terrain quality from an area extending range bands around target equal to your Earth Ring. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): Persists until end of scene. (op)(op): Terrain gains Hallowed (Earth). (op): Each Tainted being increases TN of checks to resist effects by 2. (op): Choose character instead of position; area follows them. (op): All damage in area gains Sacred quality.</li></ul>","everchangingwaves":"<ul><li>A shugenja might have lived as a bird, a wolf, a plant, and humans of various stations before being born into their current position in the Celestial Order. All of these existences are separate, and yet they are inexorably bound. By following the bond backward, a shugenja adept in communing with the water kami can reshape their own flesh to mirror a past form— albeit briefly—transforming into a natural animal or supernatural beast for a short time.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 4 Theology (Water) check targeting yourself.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment your body, transforming it into that of a natural animal of Silhouette 2. While in this form, use its ring values, derived attributes, abilities, and advantages with the physical or social type, but your own skill ranks and advantages with the mental or spiritual type. Persists until you choose to end it or are rendered Unconscious. Do not remove fatigue or strife when reverting; if this causes fatigue to exceed endurance (or strife to exceed composure), suffer a Critical Strike with severity 5 (or become Compromised).</li><li>Water (op): Transform into a different sentient species.</li><li>Water (op): Transform into an Otherworldly being, such as a supernatural beast.</li><li>Water +(op): Choose a new form of silhouette 1 higher or lower per (op) spent this way (min 0, max 6).</li></ul>","extinguish":"<ul><li>A shugenja who communes with the spirits of fire must learn to still them, lest the flames they conjure consume the shugenja. The trick is to stoke the kami&#x27;s wrath briefly but intensely, so that it is exhausted that much more quickly. With a few words and a rising gesture, the shugenja inhales, drawing the flames to a searing glow, then exhales, letting them settle to embers.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 3 Theology (Fire) check targeting up to three mundane sources of fire at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon the fire kami&#x27;s energy into yourself. Extinguish each target flame and remove 1 fatigue per target source of fire extinguished.</li><li>Fire (op)(op): Also end all persistent effects from other Fire invocations and flame-based supernatural effects in the area.</li></ul>","falserealmofthefoxspirits":"<ul><li>The kami are not bound so tightly to the Mortal Realm of Ningen-dō as mortals (even shugenja) are. They can see the ways in which the mortal and spiritual realms overlap and disconnect, and when beseeched by a shugenja, they can even draw visions of one realm into another, creating vast, nearly tangible falsehoods that fool all but the keenest observers.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a TN 5 Theology (Air) check targeting one position at range 0-4.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon illusory terrain at the target position extending range bands up to your Air Ring. A character unaware of its false nature must resist with a TN 4 Survival check (Earth 5, Fire 2) to realize its falsehood at a distance. Any physical contact reveals the lie (though the illusion stays in place). Persists for rounds equal to your Air Ring plus bonus successes (or that many minutes in narrative or downtime).</li><li>Air (op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li><li>Air +(op): The illusory terrain has one of the following terrain qualities per (op) spent this way: Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring.</li></ul>","firesofpurity":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 2 Theology (Fire), target one character at range 0-3</li><li>Augment target with sacred fire; Fire Ring range bands around target become Dangerous terrain for others; persists 1 + bonus success rounds</li></ul>","fluidshadows":"<ul><li>Activation: Movement and Scheme action, TN 2 Theology (Water), target shadowy position at range 1-3</li><li>Summon yourself instantly to target position</li></ul>","fukurokujinswit":"<ul><li>Shujenja are scholars at their heart, for their art is one of long hours of study and dedication to the refinement of the mind. Thus, many seek the blessing of Fukurokujin, keeper of knowledge and patron to scholars. A shugenja can call upon the guidance of this Fortune to sharpen their mind to a razor edge and vitalize their nerves.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Fire) check targeting yourself.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment your target&#x27;s wits and cunning. When making checks, the target adds a kept (ring) set to a (su) result. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes.</li><li>Fire (op): You may target another character at range 0-2 instead of yourself.</li></ul>","furyofosanowo":"<ul><li>The Fortune of Fire and Thunder, Osano-wo is the mythical son of the Kami Hida. With a sudden, harsh incantation and downward gesture, a shugenja can conjure a bolt of lightning to strike foes with a powerful blast.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 5 Theology (Fire) check targeting one character at range 0-4. Can only be performed outdoors. If the weather is already stormy, reduce TN by 1.</li><li>If you succeed, you call forth lightning to smite your target. The target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring plus three times your bonus successes. If a target is Incapacitated by this damage, they suffer a Critical Strike with severity 8.</li><li>Fire (op): The target and any other characters at range 0-2 must make a TN 3 Meditation check (Air 4, Water 1) or suffer Dazed and strife equal to three times your Fire Ring.</li><li>Fire +(op): Increase severity of any critical strikes inflicted as part of this action by 2 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","graspofearth":"<ul><li>With a harsh chant and a gesture of seizing, the shugenja calls upon the earth spirits to lay hold of someone, dragging them down and containing them. Usually, this invocation causes the target’s legs to sink into ground that has turned into sucking mud, quicksand, or a hole beneath them and entraps them.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 2 Theology (Earth) check targeting one character at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon cracks in the earth; each target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Earth Ring and must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 2, Water 5) or suffer Prone.</li><li>Earth (op): Each target that fails also suffers Immobilized.</li><li>Earth (op): Reduce the damage each target suffers to 0.</li></ul>","graspoftheairdragon":"<ul><li>Invocations are marked Shikajin&#x27;s Leap (Ancestral), Jikoju&#x27;s Journey with a stylized scroll () (Fortunist), The Wind&#x27;s Cradle (Foreign) in curriculum tables. The shugenja exhales a long breath at the end of the incantation and extends a hand. A stillness descends, the moment before the storm breaks. Then, the clouds high above twist and trail from the Heavens like festival streamers. The wind swoops toward the target and hurls them into the air—carrying them to safety or to their doom, depending on the will of the shugenja.</li><li>As an Attack action or a Support action, make a TN 4 Theology (Air) check targeting one character at range 3-5.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a gale-force wind to move the target range bands equal to your Air Ring plus bonus successes (max 6), ignoring intervening terrain. Set the target down gently (Support) or slam them into the ground (Attack).</li><li>Attack: Target must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Earth 5, Fire 2) or suffer the effects of a fall from range 3.</li><li>Air +(op): Treat the maximum range as 1 higher per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Air (op)(op)+: Increase the height of the fall the target suffers by 1 per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","guardianofthesecretgate":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 5 Theology (Earth), target unoccupied position at range 0-3; stake honor equal to honor rank</li><li>Summon ancestral spirit from Yomi; generally helpful but refuses dishonorable acts; uses NPC profile with combat and intrigue ranks up to your honor rank; persists until end of scene; attacks deal supernatural damage</li></ul>","handsofthetides":"<ul><li>Water binds all living beings, and by communing deeply with the vital spirits that flow through everything, a shugenja can master many arts. Using this esoteric invocation, a shugenja can exchange the positions of living beings near one another, throw enemies off-balance, or put allies in a position of advantage. While the Elemental Masters have been known to debate whether the water spirits shift the targets or reshape the world around them, the effect of the invocation—shuffling the positions of a number of individuals in a small radius as the shugenja sees fit—is easy to understand, if hard to comprehend.</li><li>As a Movement action, make a TN 5 Theology (Water) check targeting yourself and a number of other characters up to your Water Ring at range 1-4.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon the targets. You may cause them to exchange their positions in space. Each target&#x27;s original position must be occupied by a target, and each target must occupy a position.</li><li>Each target receives 2 strife.</li><li>Water +(op): Choose a new stance for one target per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","heartoftheladysun":"<ul><li>Activation: Attack and Support action, TN 5 Theology (Fire), target position at range 0-3</li><li>Summon orb of flame shedding brilliant light equal to Fire Ring range bands; smites Tainted beings for 3 fatigue per round and mends non-Tainted for 1 fatigue and 1 strife; persists 1 + bonus success rounds</li></ul>","heartofthewaterdragon":"<ul><li>The shugenja traces a gentle pattern on the target’s skin with purified water, calling upon the water kami in their body to protect and mend the flesh they call home. The target becomes extremely resistant to invocations, sorcery, and other supernatural abilities; summoned flames ripple off their skin harmlessly, and baleful maledictions pass over the targets.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 3 Theology (Water) check targeting one character at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment your target with spiritual fluidity. The target gains supernatural resistance equal to your Water Ring and removes 1 fatigue at the end of each round. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes. Each target cannot be affected by this invocation again until end of scene.</li><li>Water (op)(op): When the target succeeds on a check to resist the effect of a kihō, Mahō, or invocation, the character who used the technique must also make the check to resist that effect, or suffer the effect themself.</li></ul>","inarisblessing":"<ul><li>Water is life, and water kami can provide life-giving gifts of food and drink even from the most desolate environments. After the shugenja performs the invocation, the land nearby flourishes with life, delivering food to the shugenja, and pure water springs from the ground. This food is simple and nourishing, and it can be cooked or even packed away as rations for later if needed.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check targeting one position at range 1.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a meal at the target position that can feed a number of people up to your Water Ring plus bonus successes.</li><li>Water (op): The meal is particularly fortifying. Any character who partakes during downtime removes fatigue equal to your Water Ring.</li><li>Water +(op): The meal can feed people equal to your Water Ring plus bonus successes times (op) spent this way instead.</li></ul>","jadestrike":"<ul><li>Jade, said to be the tears of Amaterasu, is a sacred stone. It is anathema to creatures of darkness, and it is one of the few substances capable of harming the greater minions of Fu Leng, the fallen Kami. A shugenja can mimic its effects by entreating earth kami to punish evil before them. The shugenja’s hand is enveloped in the sacred green glow, which strikes forth, withering creatures of evil and humans under the sway of the Shadowlands’ insidious power.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 2 Theology (Earth) check targeting one character at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed and the target is an Otherworldly being, you smite and purify it with searing jade energy. It suffers a Critical Strike with severity equal to your Earth Ring plus bonus successes. The creature may spend (op)(op) from its check to resist to conceal that it has been affected, potentially concealing its Otherworldly nature (though it still suffers the effects).</li><li>If you succeed and the target is not Otherworldly, it suffers no ill effects.</li><li>Earth (op): Each Otherworldly target suffers Silenced and cannot use Mahō until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","jurojinsbalm":"<ul><li>Jurōjin, guardian of longevity, health, and physical wellbeing, is one of the most sought after of the Seven Fortunes—for whether one is a lord or a peasant, one is sure to pray for health sooner or later. A shugenja can impart spiritual fortification in this Fortune’s name, anointing the body of the target with sacred earth, healing plants such as ginseng or rhubarb, or stranger remedies still. While under the effects of this blessing, a character is much more resistant to poison, disease, and the effects of alcohol—which can be a boon or curse depending on one&#x27;s goals.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Earth) check targeting one character at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment your target&#x27;s fortitude. The target reduces TN of all checks to resist poison and disease by 2 (min 1). The target cannot become intoxicated via alcohol. Persists until end of the scene.</li><li>Earth (op): Target also reduces TN of checks to resist Mahō, Defiled terrain, and effects of Otherworldly beings by 2 (min 1).</li><li>Earth (op)(op): This effect persists for twenty-four hours instead.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): You also mend your target, removing current poisons, the Dying condition, and suppressing disease symptoms until end of scene.</li></ul>","katanaoffire":"<ul><li>The shugenja takes a kenjutsu posture, holding their hands aloft or in a guarded position, and a burst of fire swirls into existence in their grip in the shape of a sword. This blade weighs nearly nothing, but its edge cuts like fine steel, leaving blazing trails of light in the air behind it and scorching cuts through any flesh it crosses.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Fire) check to summon forth a blade of flame.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon and ready a Katana made of fire. It has the Wargear quality. Damage inflicted with this weapon is supernatural rather than physical. Persists until the end of any turn in which it leaves your grip or until end of scene.</li><li>Fire (op): The weapon can be any kind of melee weapon instead of a katana.</li><li>Fire (op): You may immediately perform a Strike action using the weapon.</li><li>Fire (op): You may summon and ready a pair of weapons instead.</li><li>Fire (op): After you perform an Attack action with the weapon, each target must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Air 4, Water 1) or suffer Burning.</li></ul>","maskofwind":"<ul><li>Deception is not the way of the samurai, but it is often the way of expedience. The shugenja asks the air kami to mask their features and even their voice, causing onlookers to perceive a different person.</li><li>As a Scheme and Support action, make a TN 3 Theology (Air) check targeting yourself.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment yourself with an illusion that makes you look like someone else. An observer must resist with a TN 4 Sentiment check (Earth 5, Fire 2) to notice something amiss from appearance alone; if they succeed, they may spend (op) to recognize you specifically. Persists until end of the scene.</li><li>Air (op): Alter your voice to sound like someone else. Separate TN 4 Sentiment check (Earth 5, Fire 2) to notice from voice alone; may spend (op) to recognize you.</li><li>Air (op)(op)+: This effect persists for one additional scene per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","matsusbattlecry":"<ul><li>The shugenja calls to kami of war and flame with an ancient chant, and the calamitous spirits of the battledin roar back, inciting fury within nearby targets. This can drive foes to rash acts, or inspire a dread bravery in allies.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a Theology (Fire) check targeting a number of characters up to your Fire Ring at range 0-2. TN equals the highest vigilance among your targets.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon an illusion of a hellish scene only the target can perceive. The target receives 1 strife plus additional strife equal to bonus successes, and must resist with a TN 3 Meditation check (Air 4, Water 1) or immediately suffer Enraged.</li></ul>","messengerofchikushodo":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 2 Theology (Air), target one character you know by name</li><li>Summon a small animal from Chikusho-do to deliver a message of 20 words or fewer; arrives within 8 hours regardless of distance</li></ul>","naturestouch":"<ul><li>To perform this rite, the shugenja seeks Chikushō-dō, the Realm of Animals, in the world around them and in their own heart. This allows the shugenja to communicate with (though not dominate) animals of the mortal realm.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Air) check targeting yourself.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment yourself with the ability to speak to animals of the natural world (not Otherworldly or Tainted beings). Animals understand you within their ability but are not compelled to obey. Persists until end of the scene.</li><li>Air (op): Until end of scene, you can understand animals&#x27; speech.</li><li>Air (op): The animal acts favorably toward you, fulfilling one request that does not put it in danger without subsequent checks.</li><li>Air (op)(op): You can communicate with an Otherworldly being this way, provided it has anything to say to you.</li></ul>","pathofbeasts":"<ul><li>Activation: Support action, TN 2 Theology (Water), target yourself</li><li>Augment self with one animal aspect: Eyes of the Falcon, Nose of the Fox, Ears of the Bat, Might of the Bear (silhouette 3), or Elegance of the Moth (silhouette 1); reroll up to 3 dice on relevant checks; persists 1 + bonus success rounds</li></ul>","pathtoinnerpeace":"<ul><li>By communing with the water kami that dwell within the body, a shugenja can right imbalances and correct the flow of ki, speeding the recovery of stamina dramatically.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check targeting yourself or another character at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you mend your target&#x27;s exhausted muscles. The target removes fatigue equal to your Water Ring plus bonus successes. Each target cannot be affected by this invocation again until end of scene.</li><li>Water (op): Choose one condition: Bleeding, Dazed, Disoriented, or Lightly Wounded. Remove that condition from each target.</li><li>Water (op): Your target also removes strife equal to your bonus successes.</li></ul>","poweroftheearthdragon":"<ul><li>The shugenja places a hand on the earth and a hand over the target’s heart. They recite a deep, reverberating prayer that thrums loudly through both, bringing the vitality and resilience of stone to the blessed.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 4 Theology (Earth) check targeting one character at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment your target&#x27;s resilience, increasing their endurance by your Earth Ring plus bonus successes. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes. Each target cannot be affected by this invocation again until end of scene.</li><li>Earth (op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li></ul>","rainoftenthousandlotuses":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per session, Support action, TN 2 Theology (Water), target position at range 0-4</li><li>Mend everyone at range 0-2 of target; each removes strife and fatigue equal to 1 + bonus successes</li></ul>","ravenousswarms":"<ul><li>The shugenja ignites a number of candles and hurls them into the air, and the flames leap forth, quickly devouring the tallow before subsiding into smaller fiery motes. These settle around the shugenja’s shoulders or near their feet, sputtering cheerily and spitting out sparks that seek to spread and multiply. In addition to providing a (dangerous) source of light, these flames can also leap onto anyone the shugenja attacks.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 3 Theology (Fire) check targeting one position containing a flammable object at range 0-1. The object is consumed.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon fiery motes equal to your Fire Ring plus the Silhouette of the object consumed. When you succeed at an Attack action, you may spend motes up to your school rank to add one bonus success per mote spent. Persists until end of scene.</li><li>After you perform a Fire invocation, you summon one additional fiery mote. Persists until end of scene.</li><li>Fire (op): The motes only set nearby objects on fire when you will them to, rather than haphazardly.</li><li>Fire (op): When you defend against damage, you may spend motes up to your Fire Ring to reduce damage by 1 per mote spent.</li></ul>","reflectionsofpanku":"<ul><li>Water kami are notoriously covetous, and things lost to the depths rarely resurface. Still, this avarice can offer advantages. A shugenja learned in this art can call forth water spirits to recognize an item by submerging it in sacred water. The water spirits often provide cryptic answers, but they usually can grant the shugenja a good idea of an item’s composition, whether it possesses any mystical properties, and the general disposition of these traits.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check targeting one item at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you scry to uncover all properties an item possesses, including its name, maker, mundane qualities, magical properties, curses, and sealed techniques (nemuranai).</li><li>Water (op): Gain knowledge of the item&#x27;s origin in broad strokes (where it was forged, the clan of the individual who carried it longest, or similar).</li><li>Water (op): Target a character instead. Identify one invocation, kihō, mahō, or supernatural ability or item they possess, along with its name and general qualities.</li></ul>","riseair":"<ul><li>A manifest air kami is a flickering, shifting thing, a whirlwind of power with lashing arms that screams with the voice of the storm. It towers above the tallest of humans, yet can find its way through the slightest of cracks. The slightest slip of concentration while guiding such a being can lead to untold devastation as the child of the tempest carves its way across the landscape.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 6 Theology (Air) check targeting one position at range 3-5.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a Manifest Air Kami to fight for you. It appears at the target position and obeys you for two rounds, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes, taking its turn immediately after yours each round. When this effect ends, it departs or, if stirred to ire, begins to follow its own directives (will not attack you unless provoked).</li><li>Air (op): The manifest air kami arrives in a cyclone. Each character at range 0-2 of the target position must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Earth 5, Fire 2) or suffer supernatural damage equal to your Air Ring and be pushed 2 range bands.</li></ul>","riseearth":"<ul><li>An earth kami bursts from the ground, manifesting as a guardian creature of living rock with veins of sapphire, ruby, or even jade. Earth kami can be cantankerous, but they hate anything tainted and strive to obliterate them.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 6 Theology (Earth) check targeting one position that includes dirt, clay, or stone at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a Manifest Earth Kami to fight for you, which bursts forth at the target position. It obeys you for three rounds, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes, taking its turn immediately after yours. When this effect ends, it departs or follows its own directives (will not attack you unless provoked).</li><li>Earth +(op): Increase the earth kami&#x27;s endurance by 2 per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Earth (op): The earth kami&#x27;s stone fists unarmed attack profile gains the Sacred quality.</li><li>Earth (op): The manifest earth kami creates a shockwave. Each character at range 0-2 of the chosen position must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 2, Water 5) or suffer physical or supernatural damage equal to your Earth Ring and Prone.</li></ul>","riseflame":"<ul><li>A humanoid form wrought of flame, garbed in a flowing robe of cinder and smoke, with hair of trailing sparks, a manifest fire kami is an alluring and terrible sight to behold. Where its gaze passes, flames arise, and only ash remains in its wake.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 6 Theology (Fire) check targeting one position containing flammable material at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a Manifest Fire Kami. It consumes the flammable material, appearing in its position. It obeys you for two rounds, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes, taking its turn immediately after yours. When this effect ends, it departs or follows its own directives (will not attack you unless provoked).</li><li>Fire (op): The fire kami bursts forth in searing flame. Each character at range 0-2 must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 5, Water 2) or suffer Burning and Dazed.</li><li>Fire +(op): The fire kami consumes one additional flammable source in range per (op) spent this way. Increase its endurance by the silhouettes of all consumed objects.</li><li>Fire (op): When the fire kami&#x27;s fatigue exceeds its endurance, it detonates. Each character at range 0-3 must resist with a TN 5 Fitness check (Air 6, Water 3) or suffer supernatural damage equal to two times your Fire Ring and Burning and Dazed.</li></ul>","risewater":"<ul><li>Water kami are nurturing, for water fosters all life. However, like all nature spirits, they are beings of destruction and creation; calling a water kami to take manifest form is to summon a potent force indeed. A manifest water kami often takes a humanoid form, rising from a nearby lake, river, or ocean and carried aloft on a crushing wave. As water splits into rivulets, so a manifest water kami can split into multiple smaller beings, each one surging forth to devastate the foe.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 6 Theology (Water) check targeting one position containing a large quantity of water at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a Manifest Water Kami to fight for you. It appears from the targeted body of water and obeys you for two rounds, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes, taking its turn immediately after yours. When this effect ends, it departs or follows its own directives (will not attack you unless provoked).</li><li>Water (op): The water kami attempts to swallow anyone inside it; each must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Earth 2, Fire 5) or be pulled in and begin suffocating. As an action, a trapped character may make a TN 3 Fitness check (Earth 1, Fire 4) to escape.</li><li>Water (op): Upon arrival, the water kami may move range bands up to your Water Ring.</li><li>Water +(op): Split the manifest water kami into smaller manifest water kami equal to (op) spent this way. Each has endurance equal to 12 divided by number of (op) spent (rounded up).</li></ul>","secretsonthewind":"<ul><li>The spirits of air need little prompting to gossip, even if their breathless murmurs are often incomprehensible to human ears. To make this clandestine invocation, the shugenja offers up incense of sandalwood and plum to convince the air kami to repeat what is said far away.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a TN 3 Theology (Air) check targeting one position at range 0.</li><li>If you succeed, you scry with whispering winds that eavesdrop on the chosen position. The air kami can overhear anything said within range bands equal to your Air Ring. Persists for twenty-four hours or until you designate a new area. While this effect persists, you may spend an action to hear anything being said at the moment in the designated area.</li><li>Air (op): You can also smell any scents in that area.</li><li>Air (op): If another character discovers your invocation, the effect immediately ends, preventing them from identifying it as your handiwork.</li><li>Air (op)(op)+: Persists for twenty-four additional hours per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","stridethewaves":"<ul><li>Guided by the spirits of water, the character can slide effortlessly across the surface of a stormy sea, ride a current of water out of the ocean, or even plunge beneath its depths, breathing the brine as though it were air.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check targeting one character at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a buoyant current. Even if the target cannot normally swim, they can control where they move in or on water. The target ignores negative effects of terrain while in water and does not suffocate while underwater. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","strikethetsunami":"<ul><li>Upending the contents of a water pouch or reaching into a nearby lake or stream, the shugenja pulls out an impossibly large torrent that slams into several foes nearby, pushing them back or dragging them forward as the shugenja wills.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 4 Theology (Water) check targeting a number of characters up to your Water Ring at range 0-3. Must have a source of water.</li><li>If you succeed, you smite your targets with a spray of water. Each target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Water Ring plus bonus successes. Each target must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Earth 1, Fire 4); you may move each target who fails range bands up to their shortfall in any direction.</li><li>Water (op): Each target who fails the check to resist also suffers Bleeding.</li></ul>","suijinsembrace":"<ul><li>A shugenja with the proper knowledge—and the will to wield it—can inflict a drowning death upon their enemy, transforming the air in their lungs into seawater and killing them as surely as throwing them off a pier while tied to a heavy stone.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 4 Theology (Water) check targeting one character at range 1-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you smite your target with lungfuls of seawater. The target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Water Ring plus two times bonus successes. If a target&#x27;s fatigue exceeds their endurance this way, the target begins to suffocate for rounds equal to your Water Ring plus bonus successes or until you release them as a Support action.</li></ul>","summonfog":"<ul><li>Tendrils of mist spill forth from the character’s robes or armor, billowing out before them and wrapping them in an ominous haze.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Air) check targeting one position at range 0-4.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a fog bank extending 1 range band around the target position. This fog bank counts as Obscuring terrain.</li><li>Air (op): Target a character instead of a position. The fog bank follows that character.</li><li>Air +(op): The fog bank encompasses 1 additional range band per (op) spent this way (max range 6).</li><li>Air (op)(op): The fog bank becomes a freezing ice storm, also counting as Dangerous terrain.</li></ul>","symbolofearth":"<ul><li>Earth spirits govern boundaries and domains. By inscribing an emblem in dirt, scratching it upon stone, or imprinting it upon sand, a shugenja can create a field that repels malevolent supernatural entities.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 3 Theology (Earth) check targeting one position at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a symbol that purifies the area at the target position. Each time an Otherworldly being attempts to move closer to the target, it suffers supernatural damage equal to your Earth Ring and must make a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 2, Water 5) or suffer Prone. Persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes.</li><li>Earth (op): Persists until end of the scene instead.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): Persists for twenty-four hours instead.</li></ul>","sympatheticenergies":"<ul><li>Water kami flow through all living beings, and a shugenja can use their winding channels to transfer boons and curses alike between individuals.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check to spread one chosen persistent invocation effect across a number of targets equal to your Water Ring at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment the spiritual power of one persistent invocation effect already affecting one target. Each other target counts as being affected by it as well. Persists as long as the original effect persists on the original target.</li><li>Water (op)(op): Choose a condition the target is suffering instead of a persistent invocation effect.</li></ul>","tempestofair":"<ul><li>The shugenja beseeches the air spirits to lash out all around them, calling buffeting winds to push foes backward or even hurl them to the ground.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 3 Theology (Air) check targeting each character at range 2-3.</li><li>If you succeed, blasts of wind smite each target. Each target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Air Ring and must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Earth 5, Fire 2) or suffer Disoriented.</li><li>Air +(op): Each target who fails their Fitness check is also pushed 1 range band away from you per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","tetsuboofearth":"<ul><li>The shugenja takes a steady stance and calls the spirits of earth. A pillar of stone rises from a nearby plot of soil, chunks cracking away to reveal the form of a studded club. Despite its great weight, the shugenja can heft it with ease, their might reinforced by the spirits of earth.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Earth) check targeting one position at range 0-1 that includes stone, dirt, or clay.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon and ready a Tetsubō made of stone. When you deal damage with an Attack action using this weapon, if a target is Prone, that target suffers additional damage equal to your Earth Ring. Persists until the end of any turn in which it leaves your grip or until end of scene.</li><li>Earth (op): The weapon can be any kind of melee weapon instead. It has the Durable quality.</li><li>Earth (op): After performing this action, immediately perform a Guard action using this weapon.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): The weapon has the Sacred quality.</li></ul>","thecleansingfire":"<ul><li>With a roared incantation, the shugenja spreads their hands wide and a circle of fire spills forth, rippling across the ground and searing everything in its path. These flames are indiscriminate, hungrily lapping at friend, foe, and inanimate object alike.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 1 Theology (Fire) check targeting each other character at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you smite each target with a roaring burst of fire. Each target suffers Dazed and must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Air 4, Water 1) or suffer supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring plus their shortfall and Burning.</li></ul>","thefadingdream":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene, Scheme action, TN 2 Theology (Air), target yourself</li><li>Cloak of dreams; NPCs with vigilance lower than 1 + bonus successes forget interactions with you at end of scene; ends if you attempt violence</li></ul>","thefiresfromwithin":"<ul><li>The incantation to call fire is guttural and raw. Even as the words echo, the shugenja’s hands snap open, and motes of flame trail from their fingertips, searing their way toward the objects of the shugenja’s ire. If the shugenja has the strength of will to maintain their focus, they can direct the motes with amazing precision and burn tiny, searing holes in their targets. However, if the shugenja lets their heart swell with wrath or fury, the motes bloom into tiny infernos that seek to consume anything they hit and leave only ash.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 3 Theology (Fire) check targeting a number of characters up to your Fire Ring at range 1-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you smite each target with a stream of fire. Each target suffers supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring plus bonus successes.</li><li>Fire +(op): Treat maximum range as 1 higher per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","therushingwave":"<ul><li>The shugenja calls the torrent as their steed and rides it, pulling a wave of water from a nearby lake, pond, river, or ocean to propel them forward at incredible speed.</li><li>As a Movement action, make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check targeting one character at range 0-1. Must have a large source of water nearby.</li><li>If you succeed during a skirmish, you summon a rushing waterspout that propels the target. The target may immediately move 1 range band, plus additional range bands equal to bonus successes.</li><li>If you succeed during a narrative or downtime scene, you summon a gentle current that doubles the target&#x27;s speed across or through water. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","thesoulsblade":"<ul><li>The shugenja extends a hand toward the sky and makes a dangerous appeal, calling for a heavenly weapon with which to vanquish their enemy. If the invocation is performed properly and the shugenja’s cause is judged worthy, the sky cracks and a thunderbolt descends from the heavens, blasting through anything in its path. It lands writhing in the shugenja&#x27;s hand, forming a weapon that appears in the shape pictured in the shugenja&#x27;s mind. Be it the hide of a great beast or the sorcerous ward of a mahō-tsukai, there is nothing this blade of judgment cannot pierce.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 4 Theology (Fire) check to summon forth a blade of pure energy.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon and ready a Katana or Naginata made of searing, crackling energy. Attacks made with this weapon inflict supernatural damage and ignore all forms of resistance. Persists until it leaves your grip or until end of scene.</li><li>Fire (op): The weapon can be any kind of melee weapon instead.</li><li>Fire (op): You may immediately perform a Strike action using the weapon.</li><li>Fire (op): You may summon and ready a pair of weapons instead.</li><li>Fire (op): One character you choose other than yourself may wield the weapon.</li><li>Fire (op)(op): After you perform an Attack action with the weapon, each target must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Air 5, Water 2) or suffer Dazed.</li></ul>","theworldisnotheavy":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Theology (Water) check targeting yourself or a living creature you are touching with your bare hands.</li><li>If you succeed, the target can carry items with maximum combined silhouette value equal to their own silhouette plus 1. Their armor loses the Cumbersome quality while worn. If the target is a steed, the maximum combined silhouette value of riders it can carry increases by 2 (no individual rider may exceed what the steed can normally carry). Persists for the duration of the scene.</li><li>Opportunities: Water (op)+: Increase max combined silhouette of items the target can carry by 1 per (op) spent. Water (op)(op): Another equipped item the target has loses the Cumbersome quality. Water (op)(op): Increase max combined silhouette of riders the steed can carry by an additional 2.</li></ul>","tokenofmemory":"<ul><li>After performing this invocation, the shugenja conjures an illusion from the air, a trick of the light captured in hand.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a TN 2 Theology (Air) check targeting one position at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon an illusion of one inanimate object at the target position. The illusory object&#x27;s Silhouette is up to your bonus successes (beginning at 0). The item appears real but cannot be used. Any character must resist with a TN 4 Artisan, Smithing, or Design check (Earth 5, Fire 2) using a Scholar skill approach to discern its illusory nature. Persists until end of the scene.</li><li>Air (op): The object can appear to be a creature or person (though it does not move).</li><li>Air +(op): Summon one additional illusory object in range per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Air (op)(op): Illusory objects you summon have mass and can be used as if real (still inanimate, do not move on their own). They vanish when the effect ends.</li></ul>","tombofjade":"<ul><li>One of the most powerful invocations of the spirits of earth, the rite the Kuni shugenja call the Tomb of Jade seals an entity suffused with the power of the Shadowlands within jade, transforming its blighted flesh into this sacred substance. However, if the prison of jade is cracked or broken, the spell weakens, and the being sealed within might be able to escape to wreak havoc once again. If it ever escapes, the shugenja who sealed it becomes aware of its escape, for the earth kami send a rumbling warning, shaking their current location to raise the alarm.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 6 Theology (Earth) check targeting one character at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed and the target is a Tainted being, you purify it, slowly transforming it into jade. At the beginning of each of the target&#x27;s turns, reduce the value of each of its rings by 1. Persists for rounds equal to your Earth Ring plus bonus successes. If any ring is reduced to 0, the target is turned entirely into jade — it can only be freed if the statue is damaged or destroyed. The jade statue causes area at range 0-2 to count as Hallowed (Earth) terrain.</li><li>If you succeed and the target is not Tainted, it suffers no ill effects.</li><li>Earth (op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li><li>Earth (op): At a later point, you may release the target from its jade prison as an action.</li><li>Earth +(op): Choose one condition per (op) spent: Dazed, Disoriented, Immobilized, or Prone. If the target is Otherworldly, it suffers the chosen conditions.</li></ul>","vaporofnightmares":"<ul><li>The shugenja murmurs an incantation half-heard by the target, and as the ominous chant fades and the scent cloud of incense parts, the object of the target’s fear strides forth as an illusive phantasm.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 4 Theology (Air) check targeting one character at range 2-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon an illusion of your target&#x27;s greatest fear. Target must resist with a TN 4 Meditation check (Earth 5, Fire 2); if they fail, they suffer strife equal to your Air Ring plus bonus successes, and must immediately unmask if they become Compromised this way. If they unmask in the presence of the phantasm, they focus their attentions on the phantasm (attacking it, fleeing from it, or unleashing harsh words upon it) rather than dealing with you or anyone else. The phantasm persists for rounds equal to your Air Ring.</li><li>Air (op): If a target fails the Meditation check, they also suffer Disoriented.</li><li>Air (op): The phantasm persists until end of the scene instead.</li></ul>","wallofearth":"<ul><li>For their part, earth kami are not too proud to shape walls, ditches, or even buildings along lines in the dirt that a shugenja traces or blesses with reagents like topaz and oak. Placing such a wall underneath someone is likely to hurl them to the ground, while placing one under a building could wreak havoc and cause considerable damage to the structure. The invoked construction endures as long as a mundane construction of the same material would. If it is merely dirt called into the desired shape, it begins to erode within a few days, while if the ground the shugenja raises is largely composed of stone, the construction might stand for centuries.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Earth) check targeting two positions at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a wall of earth between the two target points that is range 1 in thickness and range 3 in height. Each character standing where the wall erupts must resist with a TN 2 Fitness check (Air 1, Water 3) or suffer physical damage equal to your Earth Ring and Prone. The wall endures as long as a mundane construction of the same material.</li><li>Earth (op): The wall counts as terrain with one quality: Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring.</li><li>Earth +(op): Treat maximum range as 1 higher per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): Summon an Outpost fortification instead of a wall.</li><li>Earth (op)(op)(op): Summon a Fortress fortification instead.</li><li>Earth (op)(op)(op)(op): Summon a Castle fortification instead.</li></ul>","walloffire":"<ul><li>A roiling wall of fire sends a very specific message: approach and die in a manner most awful. Shugenja who commune with fire spirits can summon forth such blazing warnings with relative ease, brushing oil or powder across the ground and then igniting it with a word of invocation. The wall of fire sparks to life with great force and extends up a few yards for several moments, but it maintains its intensity only so long as it has fuel.</li><li>As an Attack and Support action, make a TN 4 Theology (Fire) check targeting two positions at range 2-4.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a wall of flame between the target points that extends to range 1 in thickness and range 3 in height; this area counts as Dangerous terrain. Persists for one round plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes. Any character standing where the wall erupts suffers Dazed and must resist with a TN 2 Fitness check (Air 3, Water 1) or suffer supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring and Burning.</li><li>Fire (op): The wall of fire also counts as Entangling or Obscuring terrain (choose one).</li></ul>","wingsofthephoenix":"<ul><li>The shugenja leaps into the air, and fiery wings burst forth behind them, carrying them into the sky. Small motes of flame fall in the wake of the shugenja’s passing, igniting the ground cover before fading into delicate feathers of ash.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 4 Theology (Fire) check targeting yourself.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment yourself with wings of flame. These flames do not harm you. You can move vertically and horizontally freely and ignore terrain while flying. Persists one round, plus additional rounds equal to bonus successes. While persisting, any terrain you fly over at range 0-3 is ignited and becomes Dangerous terrain until the beginning of your next turn; each character within suffers Dazed and must resist with a TN 2 Fitness check (Air 3, Water 1) or suffer supernatural damage equal to your Fire Ring and Burning.</li><li>Fire +(op): While flying, carry up to one additional willing character at range 0-2 per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Fire (op)(op): This effect persists until end of the scene instead.</li></ul>","wrathofkazenokami":"<ul><li>When stirred to wrath through the deepest secrets of the shugenja’s art, the spirits of the wind become a howling tornado, spinning around the priest and raising them from the ground while devastating everything in reach; uprooting trees, shattering buildings, and crushing foes.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 5 Theology (Air) check targeting each character at range 2-4.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a hurricane that buffets all characters in range. At the end of each of your turns, each target in range must resist with a TN 4 Fitness check (Earth 5, Fire 2) or suffer supernatural damage equal to your Air Ring and Disoriented. The hurricane persists for rounds equal to your Air Ring and can destroy objects or structures at GM&#x27;s discretion.</li><li>Air (op): You may end the hurricane at any time as an action.</li><li>Air +(op): Each target who fails the Fitness check is hurled range bands away from you equal to (op) spent this way. Upon landing, each target hurled suffers the effects of falling the number of range bands they moved.</li><li>Air (op)(op): While within the hurricane, you can fly, moving vertically and ignoring the effects of terrain.</li></ul>","yariofair":"<ul><li>The shugenja adopts a spear-fighting stance, and a swirling, darting mass ripples into being in their hand. It weighs almost nothing and yet strikes with the force of a thunderclap.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 1 Theology (Air) check to summon a spear made of swirling wind into your hand.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon and ready a Yari made of wind, visible only by a wispy outline. It has the Concealable quality. When you make an Attack or Support action check using the invisible spear, during Step 5: Choose Kept Dice, add a kept (ring) set to an (ex)(st) result. The spear persists until the end of any turn in which it leaves your grip or until the end of the encounter.</li><li>Air (op): The weapon you summon can be any kind of melee or ranged weapon instead of a spear.</li><li>Air (op): After performing this action, you may immediately perform a Guard action using the weapon you summoned.</li><li>Air (op)(op): You may summon a pair of weapons instead of a single weapon.</li></ul>","balancingsalveqamaristregion":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Support action using an alchemy kit, make a TN 2 Medicine (Air) check targeting one character with the Dying or Afflicted condition.</li><li>If you succeed, remove Dying or Afflicted condition from target. Target suffers Unconscious condition and cannot be awakened until end of scene.</li></ul>","beseechakodosjudgment":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: Once per game session as a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Tactics (Void) check targeting one terrain feature on the battlefield (or one battle zone, if using the rules for battle zones)</li><li>If you succeed, increase your army&#x27;s discipline by your glory rank plus your ranks in Command as long as your army has at least one cohort occupying the chosen terrain feature. This effect persists until your army has no cohort occupying that feature, or until the end of the scene.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: If you succeed and designate a fortification, while your army occupies that fortification, increase that fortification&#x27;s difficulty level by 1 per (op) spent this way. (op)(op)+: Each time your army suffers panic from battle fatigue during this scene, it suffers 1 less per (op) spent this way (to a minimum of 1).</li></ul>","beseechbayushisabsolution":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: Once per game session as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Sentiment (Air) check targeting yourself</li><li>If you succeed, the next time you would receive strife or fatigue, reduce the amount you receive by your focus. This effect persists until the end of the next scene.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you succeed, the next time you would forfeit honor, reduce the amount you forfeit by half (rounded up).</li></ul>","beseechdojiswisdom":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: Once per game session as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Composition check to transcribe a historical event you witnessed to paper</li><li>You write from the heart to create a record of the event that rings as a genuine account and omits no details of significance. Readers with vigilance lower than your honor rank trust the events to be true, or at least recorded in good faith.</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op): If you succeed, each character awarded glory from the event receives that much glory plus your ranks in Culture. Earth (op): If you succeed, the text gains the Durable quality. Air (op)+: If you succeed, you may omit one detail of significance per (op) spent without creating contradictions. Water (op): If you succeed, reduce the TN of any check to copy the text by 2. Void (op)(op): The text gains the Sacred item quality.</li></ul>","beseechhidasmight":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: Once per game session as a downtime activity or Support action, you may make a TN 2 Meditation (Fire) check targeting an area encompassing 3 range bands around yourself</li><li>If you succeed, this area becomes an arena. When a character makes a Martial Arts check in the arena during the event and does not gain strife from the check, that character reduces the TN of their next check by 1 (to a minimum of 1). This effect persists until the end of the next scene.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you succeed, the arena gains the Hallowed (Fire) terrain quality until the end of the scene. (op)+: If you succeed, increase the Endurance and Composure of each character fighting a duel in the arena by 1 per (op) spent this way. (op)+: Reduce the TN of checks to remove the Bleeding and Dying conditions from characters within the arena by 1 per (op) spent this way (to a minimum of 1).</li></ul>","beseechshibascalm":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: Once per game session after participating in a Mass Battle or as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Theology (Void) check targeting an area upon which a mass battle was fought earlier that day</li><li>If you succeed, remove the Defiled terrain quality from the area.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): Remove one Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain quality gained during the battle. (op)(op): Remove the Imbalanced terrain quality from the area. (op)(op): Non-Tainted beings reduce Theology check TNs in this area by 1; Tainted beings increase all check TNs by 1. (op)+: Reduce the TN of any Fitness or Meditation checks that characters in your army need to make at the end of a scene by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","beseechshinjosempathy":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: Once per session as a downtime activity or Support action, you may make a Survival (Water) check targeting a friendly animal at range 0-1. TN equals the animal&#x27;s conflict rank. If bonded, reduce TN by 2 (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, your target removes 3 fatigue, plus 1 additional fatigue per bonus success.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): You and the target each remove 1 strife per bonus success. (op): If you succeed, target removes additional fatigue equal to your ranks in Medicine. (op): Remove the Bleeding condition. (op)(op): Remove the Lightly Wounded condition, or reduce Severely Wounded to Lightly Wounded. (op)(op): Remove the Dying condition. (op)(op)+: Choose one additional friendly animal of the same conflict rank or lower per (op) spent.</li></ul>","beseechtogashisvision":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: Once per game session as a downtime activity or as a Scheme and Support action during a Mass Battle, you may make a TN 3 Meditation (Void) check targeting a character you can perceive (or a leader or commander of an enemy army)</li><li>If you succeed, you assess another character&#x27;s strategy. Once before the end of the next scene, after that character performs an action, you may reveal that you were prepared for this and immediately perform one action.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you succeed and you are the commander of an army, you may choose a leader in your army to perform the action instead. (op): While you perform the prepared action, reduce the TN by your ranks in Tactics.</li></ul>","blessedunion":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 1 Theology (Air), target people entering a union</li><li>Determine whether each target has good intentions for the union; may formalize the union legally</li></ul>","blessingoffertilefields":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 2 Theology (Earth) or Survival (Earth), target settlement fields</li><li>All fields protected from pests and excessive flooding and heat until next harvest</li></ul>","blessingofsteelartisan":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Subtype: Artisan Ritual</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, make a TN 2 Smithing check using any ring.</li><li>Apply one effect based on ring used: Air: +1 deadliness. Earth: Remove Damaged or gain Durable. Fire: Gain one logical quality (GM approval). Water: +1 damage/-1 deadliness, or +1 supernatural resistance/-1 physical resistance. Void: Reduce TN of next check with item by 1. Only one effect per item. Persists until end of next scene in which item is used.</li></ul>","blessingofthedance":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 2 Performance (Water), target everyone in scene</li><li>Each target removes 3 strife and 3 fatigue</li></ul>","centertheworld":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Survival (Air) check to find a path to civilization through impenetrable desert, dense forest, or treacherous mountains. On the ocean, use Seafaring instead of Survival.</li><li>If you succeed, you find a sign of the nearest habitation of humans or other sentient beings and can determine the direction to reach it.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op)+: Learn one key detail about the inhabitants per (op)(op) spent: culture/national affiliation, means of subsistence, commonly used technologies, or time since they last passed your location. (op)(op): Reduce TN of checks using the Analyze approach by 1 until end of next scene.</li></ul>","chikushodosguile":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 1 Survival (Air) to tap into Chikusho-do and Sakkaku, shrouding yourself in human form.</li><li>Transform into a human form derived from your true form. You are functionally human and cannot use techniques requiring aspects of true form. Observers with vigilance lower than or equal to Performance ranks do not detect flaws. Key features (feather/fur color, scars) persist across forms. If Compromised, disguise slips. As Support action, transform back.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): Choose a form of another creature of silhouette 2. (op)(op): Choose a form of a creature of silhouette 1 or 3.</li></ul>","cleansingofcoralandgoldivorykingdomsregion":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity using a small piece of coral and one koku&#x27;s worth of gold, make a TN 3 Theology (Void) check targeting food and water sufficient for one person for a day. Does not consume coral or gold.</li><li>If you succeed, food and water are cleansed of Unholy quality and are safe to consume for 24 hours.</li></ul>","cleansingrite":"<ul><li>The ritualist sanctifies a person or group, anointing them with sacred substances that drive out unholy presences and malign sorcery.</li><li>As a downtime activity, make a TN 3 Theology (Void) check targeting up to five characters to remove spiritual contaminants from the targets before they spread. Note: this cannot remove a Shadowlands Taint disadvantage once it has taken hold, but it can prevent this spiritual contamination from taking root after a character is exposed.</li><li>If you succeed, remove the Afflicted condition from the target.</li><li>Void (op)(op): If one or more targets is an Otherworldly being, you become aware of it after completing the ritual — but you do not know which target.</li><li>Void (op)+: Choose one additional target per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Void (op)+: Instead of targeting characters, you may target an area encompassing a number of range bands around you equal to (op) spent this way. Remove the Defiled terrain quality from this area. If it is a deeply unhallowed place that has long been the domain of evil, the Defiled quality returns after one day, plus additional days equal to your bonus successes.</li></ul>","communewiththespirits":"<ul><li>The ritualist centers their mind on one of the Elements, appealing to the spirits in their environment and seeking their counsel or boon. Priests and laypeople are able to use this ritual to receive less specific guidance from the spirits, such as a leaf that falls to the ground pointing in the direction of the person or thing they are seeking.</li><li>As a downtime activity or Support action, make a TN 1 Theology check using Air, Earth, Fire, Water, or Void to appeal to nearby spirits of that Element (appeal to the departed, such as ancestor spirits, and other non-elemental supernatural presences if using Void) for aid.</li><li>If you succeed, choose and receive one of the following boons: (1) Sense the Kami — Detect all spirits and uses of their magic by shugenja within a number of range bands equal to the ring you used plus your bonus successes. (2) Spiritual Knowledge — Learn one fact the spirits know about the area. (3) Elemental Gift — The kami deliver a small amount of the Element in question to you (e.g., rain from water kami, sparks from fire kami, a gust from air kami, a stone from earth kami, or a found ancestor&#x27;s belonging from Void).</li><li>(op): Reduce the TN of your next check to interact with or appeal to kami or supernatural presences of this Element by 1.</li><li>(op)+: If you succeed, receive one additional boon per (op) spent this way. Each boon can only be received one time per activation.</li></ul>","craftshikigamishugenja":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Subtype: Shugenja Ritual</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity using a consecrated vessel of silhouette 0 or smaller, make an Artisan skill (Void) check. You choose the TN (minimum 1).</li><li>Choose a number of invocations you know up to the TN. Create a shikigami with those invocations sealed within it. While shikigami exists, you cannot use those invocations but it can. Maximum one shikigami at a time (Yogo Preserver school ability modifies this).</li><li>Opportunities: (op): Add one of your advantages and one disadvantage to shikigami. (op): Shikigami has different form of same silhouette. (op)+: Increase silhouette by 1 per (op). (op)+: Choose one skill; shikigami has ranks equal to (op) spent. (op)+: Increase endurance or composure by 2 per (op).</li></ul>","culturalexchange":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 2 Culture (Fire) check to establish cultural fundamentals with someone from an unfamiliar culture. A number of characters up to your ranks in Culture can participate.</li><li>If you succeed, each participant learns something of value about the culture of each other participant. Even without a shared language, participants establish basic communication through gestures and learned words.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): Reduce TN of checks using the Theorize approach by 1 until end of next scene.</li></ul>","cunningsnares":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 1 Survival (Air) to create and set traps at range 0-5.</li><li>Set one trap, plus one additional per 2 bonus successes. Each trap triggers when a character moves to range 0. Choose from: Deadfall Trap (TN 5 Fitness [Water 3, Fire 6], physical damage 2x shortfall), Pitfall Trap (TN 4 Fitness [Earth 2, Water 5], 6 physical damage + Dazed + Disoriented), Rope Snare (TN 5 [Fire 3, Earth 6], physical damage equal to shortfall ignoring physical resistance + Immobilized). Trap deadliness is 7.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Increase trap resist TN by 1, plus 1 per additional (op)(op). (op): If trap inflicts damage, increase by Skulduggery ranks; if critical strike, increase severity by same. (op): If trap inflicts damage, target also suffers Bleeding. (op)(op): Use poison doses on traps equal to number made.</li></ul>","divination":"<ul><li>The ritualist peers into a character’s future, ascertaining their fate from the patterns of the stars, the char marks upon animal bones, the placement of cast shells, or other omens they can read.</li><li>As a downtime activity, make a TN 2 Theology (Void) check targeting one character to see glimpses of their future.</li><li>If you succeed, choose one of the following omens in the target&#x27;s near future: (1) Omen of the Azure Dragon — The next time the target performs a check using an Artisan skill this game session, the target adds a kept (ring) set to an (su)(st) result. (2) Omen of the Black Tortoise — Same for a Scholar skill check. (3) Omen of the White Tiger — Same for a Martial skill check. (4) Omen of the Vermilion Bird — Same for a Social skill check. (5) Omen of the Weaver and the Cowherd — Same for a Trade skill check. If you fail, the GM chooses one of the above omens instead. The target cannot receive another divination until the next game session.</li><li>(op): If you fail, an additional omen appears to you after the first. Choose one of the above omens in addition to the one the GM chose.</li></ul>","elixirofrecoveryqamaristregion":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity using an alchemy kit, make a TN 3 Medicine (Water) check targeting one character.</li><li>If you succeed, target removes twice as much fatigue when resting and reduces TN of checks to remove conditions by 2. Persists until end of game session.</li></ul>","formalteaceremony":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 5</li><li>Activation: Once per game session, as a downtime activity using a ceremonial tea set</li><li>Check: TN 5 Performance (Void) targeting yourself and up to your ranks in Culture other participants</li><li>Each participant removes 6 strife plus additional strife equal to bonus successes. If you succeed, each participant gains 1 Void point.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): If you succeed, reduce TN of each participant&#x27;s next check by 2. (op)+: Each participant removes 2 fatigue plus 1 per (op) spent. (op)(op): If you succeed, gain 1 glory per participant of higher status than yourself.</li></ul>","fortitudedraughtqamaristregion":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity using an alchemy kit, make a TN 4 Medicine (Earth) check targeting one character.</li><li>If you succeed, target adds one bonus success to successful checks to resist critical strikes, plus one per two bonus successes on the Medicine check. Persists until end of next scene.</li></ul>","guardagainsttheelements":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 3 Survival check using Air, Earth, Fire, or Water, targeting up to Survival ranks characters at range 0-3.</li><li>Targets are prepared for harsh weather/environment of a type based on ring chosen (Air: pressure/noxious gasses; Earth: altitude/lack of oxygen; Fire: extreme cold; Water: extreme heat). Reduce TN of checks to resist by 1. First time affected by matching terrain quality each scene, ignore its effects. Persists until end of game session.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Choose one additional target per (op). (op)(op)(op): If you succeed, choose one additional weather type; targets are also protected against it.</li></ul>","huntersexpertise":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 5 Survival check using Air, Earth, Fire, Water, or Void, targeting one previously encountered character. Reduce TN by 1 per known advantage or disadvantage of target.</li><li>If target matches ring&#x27;s creature type (Air: ethereal Otherworldly spirits/ghosts; Earth: living Tainted; Fire: undead corporeal; Water: wild animals; Void: non-Tainted sentient beings), prepare one weapon with increased deadliness 3, plus 1 per 2 bonus successes.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): Choose additional weapons to prepare equal to Smithing ranks (minimum 1). (op): If minion NPC, increased deadliness applies to all minions with same profile. (op)(op): Instead of increasing deadliness, weapons ignore points of target&#x27;s physical resistance equal to Survival ranks.</li></ul>","imbuethunder":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: Once per session as a downtime activity with proper ingredients (10 koku, rarity 6), you may make a TN 4 Medicine check to create blasting powder</li><li>If you succeed, you create ten brilliant flares, plus ten per two bonus successes, or one blasting powder charge, plus one per two bonus successes.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): When used in a skirmish, the charge inflicts the Dazed condition on all characters at range 0-4. Air (op)(op): Increase the charge&#x27;s range band by 1. Earth (op)(op)+: When used, the charge inflicts 2 additional damage (or attrition) per (op)(op) spent. Fire (op)(op)+: When used, the charge inflicts 2 additional strife (or panic) per (op)(op) spent. Water (op)(op): Inflicts the Bleeding condition on all characters at range 0-2. Void (op)(op): The area becomes Imbalanced (All Elements) terrain for 1 day.</li></ul>","prayerofprotection":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 3 Theology (Fire), target one infant not previously targeted</li><li>Bless child until age four; decrease TN of checks to resist harmful effects by 4 (min 1)</li></ul>","protectionoftheflock":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 2 Survival (Fire) check targeting a number of animals up to your ranks in Survival.</li><li>If you succeed, you fortify targets against disease and hardship. Until end of next scene, they use your ranks in Medicine for any checks they make to resist effects.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): Target an additional number of animals equal to your ranks in Medicine. (op): If you succeed, each target gains the Emboldened condition.</li></ul>","restorativetransmutationqamaristregion":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity using an alchemy kit, make a TN 6 Medicine (Void) check targeting one character who suffered a critical strike of severity 7-8 Permanent Injury or 9-11 Maiming Blow in the previous scene. Must have severed limb if applicable.</li><li>If you succeed, remove any disadvantage received from the critical strike. Character gains the Horrible Scar adversity instead.</li></ul>","riteofthewheel":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 1 Theology (Void), target one corpse</li><li>Corpse gains Sacred item quality; Tainted beings interacting with it receive 5 strife</li></ul>","shadowofdays":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Culture (Earth) check to calculate distance between two locations. You must have knowledge of stars visible at each location or shadow lengths at certain hours. If you have visited both locations, TN is 2 instead.</li><li>If you succeed, you determine the distance between the two locations as the crow flies in li, from which you can estimate travel days. Does not necessarily account for all obstacles.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you succeed and have access to a map, create a more accurate estimate accounting for known obstacles. (op)(op): Reduce TN of checks using the Recall approach by 1 until end of next scene. (op)(op)(op): Accurately predict a future celestial phenomenon in one or both locations.</li></ul>","spiritualsurvey":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Survival (Void) check to learn about local spirits and supernatural entities.</li><li>If you succeed, you learn the nature of spirits inhabiting the region around you (extends 6 range bands). You learn their elemental affinities, otherworldly realms of origin, preferred offerings, and general inclinations toward humans. The spirits become aware someone extended senses toward them, but not your specific location.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): The spirits do not become aware that anyone searched for them. (op)(op): Reduce TN of checks using the Sense approach by 1 until end of next scene. (op)(op)(op): If you are a practitioner of meishōdō, you learn the true name of one spirit you detected.</li></ul>","teaceremony":"<ul><li>When Lady Doji served tea for the very first Emperor, the tea ceremony was born. Ceremony styles vary among the clans, from the gilded tea rooms of the Phoenix to the imperfect tea bowls of the Dragon, the early morning gatherings of the Crane to the snow- and moon-viewing ceremonies of the Scorpion. However, at its core the tea ceremony is fundamentally an appreciation of tea and, if done well, a spiritual moment for its participants. The tea represents all five elements: the fire used to heat the water, the earth from which the tea is grown, and the air that carries the aroma of the tea. Finally, void holds all four elements together, and brings in the mysterious fifth element, the moment of harmony and tranquility as one sips the tea.</li><li>Once per game session, as a downtime activity using a tea set, make a TN 2 Performance (Void) check targeting yourself and a number of other characters up to your ranks in Culture, who are also participants. Up to one other participant may assist (see Assistance).</li><li>Each target removes 3 strife, plus additional strife equal to your bonus successes.</li><li>(op): Reduce the TN of each target&#x27;s next check by 1.</li><li>(op)+: Each target removes 1 fatigue, plus 1 fatigue per (op) spent this way.</li><li>(op)(op): If you succeed, each target gains 1 Void point.</li></ul>","thetiesthatbind":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity</li><li>Check: TN 3 Sentiment (Void) targeting one character</li><li>If you succeed, learn of a character who would be a particularly fortuitous match for your target. Provides valuable clues about this person. If using Bond rules, target and identified character may decrease cost of forming a Bond to 1 XP.</li><li>Opportunities: Void (op)(op)+: Learn one likely future consequence of a relationship per (op)(op) spent. Void (op)(op)(op)(op): Learn of another character who would be an inauspicious match and one likely future consequence.</li></ul>","thresholdbarrier":"<ul><li>The ritualist wards an entryway against beings of a certain sort, causing them to fail to observe the entryway or making them mentally repulsed by their efforts to enter it.</li><li>As a downtime activity, make a TN 2 Theology check using Air, Earth, Fire, Water, or Void targeting a threshold, gate, or other entryway at range 0-1.</li><li>If you succeed, the threshold is barred against a particular entity type based on the ring chosen for one hour, plus additional hours equal to your bonus successes. When an entity of that type attempts to enter, it must resist with a TN 3 Meditation (Void) check or be repelled. Whether it succeeds or fails, you immediately become aware of its attempted entry. Entity types by ring: Air — Ethereal Otherworldly beings such as spirits and ghosts. Earth — Living Tainted beings. Fire — Undead beings with corporeal form. Water — Wild animals. Void — Humans.</li><li>(op): Instead of protecting a threshold, you may protect the entirety of a sealed area extending a number of range bands around you no greater than your bonus successes.</li><li>(op): If any beings of the type you are sealing the threshold against have passed through the threshold within the last twenty-four hours, you become aware of their passage.</li></ul>","tranceoflivespast":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity, TN 4 Meditation (Void) targeting a place, object, or individual from one of your past lives. Reduce TN by 2 if all three are true: you have items from past life, you are in a place important to it, and you interacted with an individual from it within 24 hours.</li><li>If you succeed, GM reveals a specific memory related to your target. GM may ask you to help determine specifics, then offer modifications.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Reduce TN of next check related to target by 1. (op)(op)(op)(op): If you fail, become possessed by past self until end of scene (use NPC profile determined by GM). You control actions but character has no memory of events.</li></ul>","travelersexperience":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity in a place of habitation where you are unfamiliar with the laws and customs, you may make a TN 2 Culture (Earth) check.</li><li>If you succeed, you ascertain the laws and cultural norms of the place you are visiting. You can logically discern whether a proposed course of action is legal or illegal, rude or polite.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): Reduce TN of checks using the Recall approach by 1 until end of next scene. (op)(op): Through study and use of common language roots, you can make yourself understood in the common language of the place (intelligible but not fluent).</li></ul>","treatysigning":"<ul><li>Type: Ritual</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: Once per game session as a downtime activity</li><li>Check: TN 2 Composition (Fire) to write agreement, then TN 3 Government (Air) targeting participants</li><li>If you succeed, agreement has no loopholes. Each participant stakes 10 honor on upholding the agreement. Anyone who later breaks it loses staked honor unless another participant broke it first.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: All participants stake 1 additional honor plus 1 per (op) spent. (op)(op)(op): If you succeed, you need only stake half the honor other participants stake.</li></ul>","wayfarerspath":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per game session as a downtime activity at a crossroads or in the wilderness, make a TN 3 Meditation check.</li><li>If you succeed, encounter a sign based on ring used: Earth (direction of someone with whom you share a bond), Water (direction of opportunity to make money), Fire (direction of nearest large-scale conflict), Air (direction of a person related to your past or desire), Void (direction in which you are needed most).</li></ul>","wayfindersinstincts":"<ul><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 2 Survival (Water) check to seek a crucial survival resource. On the ocean, use Seafaring instead of Survival.</li><li>If you succeed, choose one resource: potable water, food, or shelter. You find a sign of the nearest source and can determine the direction to reach it.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you succeed, determine the distance (in days journeyed) to the resource. (op)(op): Reduce TN of checks using the Survey approach by 1 until end of next scene.</li></ul>","whisperstothemoonmooncultist":"<ul><li>Activation: Downtime activity or Scheme action, TN 2 Theology (Water), target one character at range 0-4</li><li>Augment target&#x27;s mind with chaos of Onnotangu; target receives strife equal to Water Ring and must make TN 4 Meditation (Earth 5, Fire 2) check or suffer Disoriented, Exhausted, Silenced and reduce TN of next Scholar check by Water Ring (min 1). If you fail, receive strife equal to Water Ring and become Silenced and Immobilized for 1 + shortfall rounds</li></ul>","asamuraisfate":"<ul><li>A leader asks their warriors for the final service all samurai must someday render to their lord: to lay down their lives that others might live. Even as they fall in battle, their shed blood waters the fields that will grow a thousand victories.</li><li>As an action, make a TN 5 Command (Void) check targeting any number of characters (or your cohort, during a mass battle).</li><li>If you succeed during a skirmish, each target ignores any critical strikes with severity lower than your Void Ring plus your bonus successes. This effect persists until the end of the scene (at which point the injuries take effect). If you succeed during a mass battle, your army counts as having the Fearless Army ability: at the end of each round, your army removes panic equal to your glory rank. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li></ul>","allartsareone":"<ul><li>Just as the four elements are bound together by Void, certain underlying principles, including aesthetics, logic, and discipline, unite all forms of art. By meditating on these similarities, a courtier is able to more easily grasp the fundamentals of any subject.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 4 Martial skill (Void), Games (Void), or Performance (Void) check to rapidly absorb information on a new activity covered by that skill.</li><li>If you succeed, you immediately intuit how to wield a new weapon, play a new game, use a new instrument, or perform a new song, dance, or other task. You do not apply any TN increase that might be associated with dealing with something new to you.</li><li>Void (op): Choose a ring. Reduce the TN of your next check using that ring for the chosen skill by 1. This effect persists until the end of your next turn (or until the end of the scene during a narrative scene).</li></ul>","allinjest":"<ul><li>Veteran courtiers sometimes play off missteps as jokes. This underhanded but effective tactic puts the other person in a difficult position: press the issue and seem stubborn, or let it slide and give the courtier a pass.</li><li>When you make a Commerce (Water), Courtesy (Water), or Performance (Water) check, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Water (op)+: If you forfeited honor as part of the check in order to say something rude or appeal to your target&#x27;s base desires (greed, lust, laziness, etc.), regain 1 honor per (op) spent this way (see Forfeiting Social Attributes).</li></ul>","allshallfearme":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Fire Shūji</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: As a Scheme action</li><li>Check: TN 4 Command or Performance (Fire) targeting any number of characters in the scene</li><li>If you succeed, each target receives 2 strife when they choose you as target for a Social skill check. Persists until end of scene. If you fail, receive 4 strife.</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op)(op)+: If you succeed, all targets suffer 1 additional strife per (op)(op) spent whenever they target you.</li></ul>","ancestryunearthed":"<ul><li>A samurai’s ancestry often reveals a great deal about their political opportunities, assets, and probable allies in the Emerald Empire, for the rigid social strata allow little divergence. Any courtier can likely dredge up another samurai’s lineage from the dark corners of their mind, but some can recall it in an instant.</li><li>When you make a Scholar skill (Earth) or Social skill (Earth) check targeting a character, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Earth (op): You know one sworn oath the character&#x27;s family took in the past, and whether or not they have broken or bent it.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): You know one secret of the character&#x27;s family that they would prefer be forgotten, and have perhaps even worked to bury.</li><li>Earth (op)(op)(op): You know something the character does not even know about their own ancestry.</li></ul>","appreciatethescenery":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a Support action check targeting another character, if you and the target are in Dangerous, Entangling, Hallowed, Imbalanced, or Obscuring terrain, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Earth or Water (op): You and your target each remove strife equal to your ranks in Composition. Air or Fire (op): You and your target gain the Emboldened condition. Void (op): You and your target gain the Centered condition.</li></ul>","artisansappraisal":"<ul><li>The courtier looks at an object but sees its maker. Each thumbprint tells a story about the hand that crafted the piece; every subtle choice reveals something about the desires that linger in the artist’s mind.</li><li>When assessing an object or performance with an Artisan skill (Air), Performance (Air), or Games (Air) check, you may spend (op) in the following ways:</li><li>Air (op): Choose a ring; learn the value of that ring for the creator or performer and all advantages and disadvantages attached to that ring that are not of the curse type.</li><li>Air (op): If the creator or performer is an NPC, learn their demeanor.</li></ul>","assessstrengths":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Air Shūji</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: As a Scheme action</li><li>Check: Games (Air) check targeting one opponent in a game. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, learn target&#x27;s ranks in Games, Tactics, or any one Martial Arts skill. Choose one additional skill per bonus success.</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op)(op): Learn all target&#x27;s Mental advantages and disadvantages.</li></ul>","aweofheavenimperial":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Void Shūji (Imperial)</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: Once per scene, as an Attack and Scheme action</li><li>Check: Command (Void) check targeting any number of characters in the scene. TN equals the highest status rank among targets.</li><li>If you succeed, each target suffers the Silenced condition.</li></ul>","battleofnoescape":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Void Shūji</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Support action, you may make a TN 5 Command (Void) check targeting your cohort or a number of characters who can hear you up to your ranks in Meditation. Reduce TN to 2 if all targets are in Confining or Entangling terrain.</li><li>If you succeed during a mass battle, your army does not suffer morale collapse if its panic exceeds its discipline, and continues to function normally. Persists for one round, plus one round for every three bonus successes. If you succeed during an intrigue, duel, or skirmish, each target ignores the effects of the Compromised condition. Persists for one round, plus one round for every two bonus successes.</li><li>Opportunities: Void (op)+ (Intrigue, Duel, or Skirmish): Choose one additional target per (op) spent. Void (op)(op) (Intrigue, Duel, or Skirmish): If you succeed, each target also ignores the effects of the Incapacitated condition for one round, plus one round for every two bonus successes.</li></ul>","bellowofresolve":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Support action, make a TN 2 Command (Earth) check targeting one Compromised or Incapacitated character.</li><li>If you succeed and target is Compromised, they remove strife until strife equals composure minus 1. If target is Incapacitated, they remove fatigue until fatigue equals endurance minus 1.</li></ul>","bendwiththestorm":"<ul><li>When faced with a much more powerful foe, a cunning courtier often feigns a position of weakness. In this way, they can lead the opponent where they desire by offering chances the foe cannot pass up.</li><li>When you make a Social skill (Air) check targeting another character, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Air (op): Choose an advantage or disadvantage. The target comes to believe that you possess that advantage or disadvantage without your having to expend noticeable effort or state it directly. Further, the target believes that you do not know you have given this advantage or disadvantage away. If you do anything that could call this misconception into question, any character may resist with a TN 5 Sentiment check (Earth 6, Fire 3) to discern that the advantage or disadvantage is not real. This effect persists until the target is faced with incontrovertible evidence or succeeds on the check to resist.</li></ul>","bewarethesmallestmouse":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Water Shūji</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: When you make a Social skill (Water) check targeting one or more characters</li><li>Opportunities: Water (op)(op)+: While interacting with you, the target treats their vigilance as 1 lower per (op)(op) spent and decreases TN of social checks targeting you by 1. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","bondofheroes":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per game session as a Support action, make a TN 5 Performance (Void) check targeting each character who shares a bond with you in the scene.</li><li>If you succeed, each target removes 5 strife and 5 fatigue, plus 1 per two bonus successes.</li></ul>","borrowedcourage":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Air Shūji</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Performance (Air) check targeting an army or a number of characters who can hear you up to your ranks in Sentiment. You may stake up to 3 honor to reduce the TN by that amount (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, you spread a powerful rumor. The first time your target receives panic or strife during the next scene, they reduce the amount by your ranks in Performance, to a minimum of 0. Whether you succeed or fail, if your side loses the battle, you lose your staked honor.</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op): If you fail, nobody remembers what you said, so no narrative social consequences. Air (op): Add 1 kept (ring) set to (op) to the first Scheme action check you make during the next mass battle.</li></ul>","bravado":"<ul><li>Glory is half reputation and half poise. The courtier displays a confident mien, speaking more informally than propriety should allow. Their words and posture carry a tinge of arrogance, making them harder to ignore.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a Games (Fire) or Performance (Fire) check targeting any number of characters in the scene. The TN of this check is equal to the highest vigilance among your targets.</li><li>If you succeed, each target behaves as though your glory is 10 higher or lower than its actual value, plus or minus an additional 10 for each bonus success (to a maximum glory value of 100 or a minimum glory value of 0). If you do anything that could call your glory into question, any character may resist with a TN 4 Sentiment check (Air 5, Water 2) to determine your actual glory attribute. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Fire (op): Choose a character in the scene. Learn if their glory is higher or lower than yours (the actual value).</li></ul>","buoyantarrival":"<ul><li>Some people have the ability to blend in with any social environment, fluidly adapting to the rough atmosphere of the humblest tavern one day, while walking among the rulers of the Empire the next.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a Courtesy (Water) check targeting a number of characters up to your Water Ring. The TN of the check is equal to the vigilance of the character with the highest status among your targets.</li><li>If you succeed, you may enter or leave the conversation gracefully. You need not forfeit honor or glory for interrupting, suddenly departing, or preempting someone else, regardless of the respective status of the participants.</li></ul>","cadence":"<ul><li>In courtly situations, it can be advantageous for courtiers of the same clan to be able to communicate wordlessly.</li><li>When you make a Social skill (Air) check, you may spend (op) in the following ways:</li><li>Air (op): Convey a secret message that alters the meaning of what you are saying outwardly (or has nothing to do with it at all) to one character observing you who possesses this technique.</li><li>Air (op)(op): Convey a secret message that alters the meaning of what you are saying outwardly (or has nothing to do with it at all) to one character observing you who does not possess this technique.</li></ul>","callthewild":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Fire Shūji</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a Survival (Fire) check targeting one friendly animal or manifest kami at range 0-2. TN equals the animal or kami&#x27;s conflict rank.</li><li>If you succeed, increase the damage and deadliness of the animal or kami&#x27;s weapon profiles by 1, plus 1 for every two bonus successes. Persists until end of scene.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Target one additional friendly animal or manifest kami per (op) spent. (op)+: The target removes 1 fatigue per (op) spent. (op): The animal gains the Enraged condition, then removes all strife.</li></ul>","calltoride":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Support action, you can make a TN 1 Survival (Water) check targeting your mount or animal companion, provided it is within range 5 of you.</li><li>If you succeed, your mount or animal companion immediately moves up to 2 range bands toward you, plus 1 additional per two bonus successes. If it is a mount and ends at range 0, you can immediately mount it.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): Increase TN of Attack action checks targeting you and your mount/companion by 1 until end of your next turn. (op)(op): If you perform a Maneuver action after mounting, you may move up to 2 range bands instead of 1.</li></ul>","citethefacts":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Scheme action check, you may make a Scholar skill (Earth) check targeting another character using a relevant Scholar skill. TN equals target&#x27;s focus minus their current strife (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, your target suffers the Silenced condition unless they choose to gain strife equal to your ranks in Command, plus one for every bonus success.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If you succeed, add one bonus success for each reserved die you have. (op)(op)+: Choose one additional target with a focus lower than the original target&#x27;s per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","civilityforemost":"<ul><li>Samurai are warriors, but there are many contexts in which violence is inappropriate. Many strictures exist around the times weapons can and cannot be drawn. A courtier who has memorized the rules of such engagements can articulate why fighting would be improper or profane in nearly any situation.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a Command or Courtesy (Earth) check targeting one character to claim protection for an individual of your choice by rights of honor. The TN of the check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, the target must forfeit honor equal to your Earth Ring plus your bonus successes and suffer that much strife to perform an Attack or Scheme action targeting the chosen individual. This effect persists until the end of the scene, or until the target performs an Attack or Scheme action.</li><li>Earth (op)+: Choose one additional target with vigilance lower than or equal to your first target&#x27;s vigilance per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","cloudspartedbysteel":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Air Shūji</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: When you make a check to perform a Strike action or an Assault action</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op)+: If your target&#x27;s vigilance is lower than your ranks in Sentiment plus (op) spent this way, choose one of the advantage/disadvantage types: interpersonal, mental, or physical. If your target has one or more advantages or disadvantages of that type, you learn what they are.</li></ul>","complementaryexperience":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Command (Water) check targeting one other character in the scene.</li><li>If you succeed, your target has your assistance on the next check they make (persists until end of your next turn). If you succeed, your target may grant you assistance on the next check you make (persists until end of your next turn).</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): Choose one skill in which you have 0 ranks and your target has 1 or more ranks. When you grant assistance, you count as being trained in that skill until end of scene.</li></ul>","coursingmarchchant":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Water Shūji</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Performance (Water) check targeting an army or a number of characters traveling with you up to your ranks in Command. You may expend an additional day&#x27;s rations to reduce the TN by 2 (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, you and your targets can march twice the distance they normally could in that time.</li><li>Opportunities: Water (op): Army removes attrition up to your ranks in Medicine. Water (op): Army removes panic up to your ranks in Culture. Water (op)+: One individual target per (op) spent removes fatigue up to your ranks in Medicine. Water (op)+: One individual target per (op) spent removes strife up to your ranks in Culture. Water (op)(op)+: Choose one mundane terrain quality per (op)(op) spent; each target ignores it during the march.</li></ul>","courtiersresolve":"<ul><li>Warriors do battle with their bodies, and courtiers do battle with their minds. To maintain one’s composure while surrounded by the challenges of court, one must be able to clear and organize one’s mind, returning focus to the most vital tasks.</li><li>Once per scene as a Support action, you may spend 1 Void point to recover from strife.</li><li>Remove strife equal to your glory rank.</li></ul>","cracklinglaughter":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Fire Shūji</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: Once per game session as a Scheme action</li><li>Check: TN 3 Performance (Fire) targeting up to your Fire Ring characters</li><li>If you succeed, each target receives 2 strife and must make TN 5 Meditation (Air 6, Water 3) check or receive additional strife equal to shortfall. If you fail, receive 3 strife.</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op)(op): For each character who suffers Compromised condition, gain 1 glory.</li></ul>","cunningomission":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Scheme action, you may make a Sentiment (Air) check targeting another character. TN equals target&#x27;s focus minus their current strife (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, your target slips up and admits something they were concealing from you. If your target was not concealing anything, you know this fact with certainty.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op)+: If you succeed, your target receives 2 strife per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","dazzlingperformance":"<ul><li>Performing a great feat can win a character renown, but performing a great feat and then telling the story of it draws far greater accolades. A courtier building a reputation in the competitive courts of Rokugan must master not just excellence, but also capture the imagination.</li><li>When making an Artisan skill (Fire), Games (Fire), or Performance (Fire) check, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Fire (op)+: The next time you receive a glory award this scene, increase the amount you receive by 1. If there is a character of higher status in the scene, increase it by 1 per (op) spent this way instead.</li></ul>","ebbandflow":"<ul><li>Just as hardest ice and the gentlest mist are composed of the same water, seasoned courtiers know that all it takes is time and work to transform strength into weakness and weakness into strength. The courtier manipulates a person&#x27;s perceptions with ease, keeping their allies confident and their foes uneasy.</li><li>As a Scheme or Support action, make a Courtesy (Water), Command (Water), or Games (Water) check targeting one character. The TN of this check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed (and chose Scheme action), choose one of the target&#x27;s advantages that you know; whenever it applies, invert it. This effect persists until the end of the scene. If you succeed (and chose Support action), choose one of the target&#x27;s disadvantages you know; whenever it applies, invert it. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Water (op): Choose one additional advantage or disadvantage and apply the effect to it.</li><li>Water (op)(op)+: Choose one additional target with vigilance lower than or equal to your first target&#x27;s vigilance per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","enticewithfalsehoods":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Air Shūji</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: Once per scene during a mass battle as a Scheme action targeting the commander of the enemy army, you may make a Tactics (Air) check. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance. If not your army&#x27;s commander, stake 5 honor and 5 glory. If your cohort is in Obscuring terrain, reduce TN by 2.</li><li>If you succeed, you immediately change your army&#x27;s current strategic goal to a new goal of your choice. Momentum points from the previous goal apply to this new goal. If you fail and are not the commander, you lose staked honor and glory.</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op): Your target remains unaware of your machinations. Air (op): Gain 1 momentum point. Air (op)+: All characters in the scene with vigilance lower than or equal to (op) spent are unaware of your machinations.</li></ul>","enticewithofferings":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 3 Commerce (Air) check targeting another character. You must give up something the target wants: a physical object or a concession that adds 2 momentum points to the target&#x27;s current objective.</li><li>If you succeed, you distract your target for one round; they cannot add momentum to their social objectives. Persists for one round plus one additional round for every two bonus successes.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): Instead of being unable to add momentum, when the target would add momentum to their social objectives, those points are added to one of your social objectives instead. Target is unaware.</li></ul>","everyonehasaprice":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Scheme action, you may make a Sentiment (Water) check targeting another character. TN equals the target&#x27;s honor rank. You must offer a bribe with koku value equal to the target&#x27;s intrigue threat rating. Does not work on mindless or inscrutable Otherworldly creatures (GM discretion).</li><li>If you succeed and target is a Minion NPC, they accept the bribe and leave the scene. If target is not a Minion NPC, they must accept the bribe unless they receive strife equal to your ranks in Courtesy. If they accept, they must leave the scene, stop opposing you, or seek terms in negotiation.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If your target is a Minion NPC, they join your side instead of departing.</li></ul>","eyesup":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per game session at start of scene, or as a Support action, make a TN 2 Scholar skill (Water) check targeting one character.</li><li>If you succeed, target treats focus as 2 lower (minimum 1) and vigilance as 2 higher. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","fanningtheflames":"<ul><li>Inciting people to act foolishly or to flinch at the crucial moment is a key skill of a courtier, for words are their weapons. Inducing unchecked emotion is another tool in the courtier’s arsenal, and most become quite adept in the art of manipulating people into feeling certain things that are advantageous for the courtier. The courtier stings their target’s pride with needling comments or makes a flirtatious remark to draw their attention, pulling the target’s emotions to the surface and making them easier to predict.</li><li>When making a Social skill (Fire) check targeting one or more characters, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Fire (op)+: One target gains the Dazed condition per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Fire (op)(op)+: One target gains the Enraged condition per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","feignedopening":"<ul><li>A wise leader creates the impression of weakness to disguise strength, or strength to conceal weakness.</li><li>As a Movement and Scheme action, make a Performance (Air) check targeting one character in the scene who is observing you. The TN is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance. This technique can only be used during skirmish and mass battle conflicts.</li><li>If you succeed, reduce the TN of the next Attack checks against each target (or their cohort, in a mass battle) by 1 plus your bonus successes. This effect persists until the end of your next turn.</li><li>Air (op)+: Choose one additional target with vigilance lower than or equal to the original target&#x27;s per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Air (op)+: In a mass battle, increase the TN of Attack checks targeting your cohort by 1, plus 1 per additional (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","floweringdeceptions":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Scheme and Support action, make a Courtesy (Air) or Tactics (Air) check targeting two other characters who are not hostile to each other. TN equals highest vigilance among targets.</li><li>If you succeed, choose one target and increase TN of their next check by 2. Decrease TN of other target&#x27;s next check by 2. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","fluentbargaining":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a Commerce (Water) check to negotiate payment for a job, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Water (op)+: If you succeed, also convince client to pay 10% of fee up front per (op) spent.</li></ul>","foreseenneed":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Void Shūji</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: As a Support action</li><li>Check: TN 1 Artisan (Void)</li><li>If you succeed, recall that you foresaw the need for an item with rarity equal to 1 plus bonus successes. Spend one Void point to instantly reveal an item you could have crafted (must be reasonable).</li><li>Opportunities: Void (op): Double the rarity of the target item, but the item must be perishable or of sentimental value only.</li></ul>","fortressofnecessity":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Earth Shūji</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity or a Support action during a mass battle, using adequate supplies and a suitable area, you may make a TN 3 Command (Earth) check targeting a position you can reach</li><li>If you succeed, you erect a defensive structure. In a mass battle, this structure is treated as a fortification with difficulty value equal to your ranks in Labor plus your bonus successes, which reduces attrition suffered by the cohort occupying it by 2. In a skirmish, treated as Obscuring terrain by anyone attacking from outside. Temporary; degrades in a few days without maintenance.</li><li>Opportunities: Earth (op): When you perform the Reinforce action in this fortification, treat the TN as reduced by 1 (minimum 1). Earth (op)(op)+: Add one terrain quality per (op)(op) spent to range 1-3 around the building: Dangerous, Entangling, Obscuring, or Recessed.</li></ul>","funandgames":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Water Shūji</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: When you make a Games (Water) check</li><li>Opportunities: Water (op)+: Choose one participant or observer, remove 1 strife per (op) spent. Water (op)(op)(op): Remove 1 strife from each participant and observer instead.</li></ul>","gloriousentrance":"<ul><li>Activation: When you enter a scene, you may make a Performance (Fire) check. TN equals the difference between the glory rank of the character in the scene with the highest glory and your glory rank (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, reduce the TN of Scheme and Support action checks you make by 1. Persists for one round plus one additional round for every two bonus successes.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op)+: When you receive a glory award, increase the amount by 1 plus 1 per additional (op)(op) spent this way. (op)(op): You gain the Emboldened condition.</li></ul>","goadingtaunt":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Scheme action, make a Performance (Fire) or Tactics (Fire) check targeting one character. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>In intrigue/duel: target receives strife equal to honor rank unless they forfeit that much honor. In skirmish: target must move 2 range bands toward you or receive 3 strife plus 1 per 2 bonus successes. In mass battle: target must target your cohort with Assault or Challenge next turn or receive 3 strife plus 1 per 2 bonus successes. Succeed or fail, reduce TN of target&#x27;s next check by 1.</li></ul>","greatanvilsmeasure":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Earth Shūji</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: When you make a check to perform a Guard action or a Reinforce action</li><li>Opportunities: Earth (op)+ (Guard): Choose any number of characters with focus lower than or equal to your ranks in Performance plus 2 per (op) spent. Each must receive strife equal to your ranks in Performance to perform an Attack or Scheme action targeting anyone other than you. Persists until end of your next turn. Earth (op)+ (Reinforce): Choose any number of enemy leaders with focus lower than or equal to your ranks in Performance plus 2 per (op) spent. The enemy army receives panic equal to your ranks in Performance each time any of those leaders targets any cohort other than yours. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","hiddeninsmoke":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Air Shūji</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Scheme action</li><li>Check: Social (Air) check targeting one character. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, hide your true goal or objective. Any ability that would reveal your true intentions reveals a false, narratively appropriate goal instead. Persists until end of scene. During intrigue, gain 1 momentum point.</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op)(op)+: Choose one additional target per (op)(op) spent. Air (op)(op)+: Gain 1 additional momentum point per (op)(op) spent.</li></ul>","honestassessment":"<ul><li>Honesty is a virtue of Bushidō, but direct honesty is often seen as rudeness among the samurai—instead, one is expected to find a polite way to imply one’s meaning to spare the feelings of the other involved. As a result, directness can be something of a rare and valuable commodity.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Courtesy (Earth) check to appraise the weaknesses of a character.</li><li>If you succeed, choose one of the target&#x27;s known disadvantages. The target does not apply that disadvantage to their checks until the end of the scene.</li><li>Earth (op)+: Choose one additional disadvantage per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): Reduce the TN of the target&#x27;s next skill check using the ring the disadvantage is attached to by 2.</li></ul>","horsewhisperer":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a Courtesy (Water) or Survival (Water) check targeting a horse or other equine creature that can see or hear you and trusts you. TN equals target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, you make a wordless request to the target which they comprehend and are compelled to fulfill. If what they do is helpful to an action, that action counts as having assistance. Cannot request the impossible. If the horse becomes injured or harmed, it breaks the trust and becomes immune to this shūji.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): Give the target the Loyal Steed ability (it can be ridden by a silhouette 2 or lower rider) until end of scene.</li></ul>","illuminatetheway":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per session at start of scene, or as a Support action, make a TN 2 Scholar skill (Fire) check targeting one character.</li><li>If you succeed, target treats vigilance as 2 lower (minimum 1) and focus as 2 higher. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","incitewrath":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a Scheme or Support action check while riding a mount or while you have an animal companion at range 0-1, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op)(op)+: Your mount or animal companion immediately performs a Strike action targeting one character within range of one of its readied weapons. The damage it deals increases by 1 per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","ladydojisdecreecrane":"<ul><li>Propriety, grace, and eloquence were of great importance to the founder of the Crane Clan. With a word, she was said to defuse the most dangerous situations. Crane Clan courtiers follow in her footsteps, forcing bystanders to listen with a single striking comment.</li><li>Once per game session as an action, make a Courtesy (Void) check targeting a number of characters up to your school rank. The TN of this check is equal to the vigilance of the character with the highest status among your targets.</li><li>If you succeed, your targets cannot perform Attack actions targeting you. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes, or until you perform an Attack action.</li><li>Void (op)+: Choose one additional target with status lower than your first target per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Void (op)(op): Your targets also cannot perform Scheme actions targeting you.</li></ul>","ladyshinjosspeedunicorn":"<ul><li>The Kami Shinjo carried within her a curiosity that could never be fully satisfied. Her passion extends to her clan, who still feel the call of the unexplored. Peerless riders, the Unicorn Clan finds their way across unfamiliar terrain with ease, as Shinjo taught them centuries ago.</li><li>As a downtime activity, if you have a steed available, make a TN 2 Survival (Void) check to reach a destination with extreme swiftness.</li><li>If you succeed, you reach the destination in half the time it would normally require. If you so desire, one character may ride along with you.</li><li>Void (op): You may lead a number of willing characters with mounts of their own up to your school rank.</li></ul>","lightningraid":"<ul><li>The Unicorn Clan is famous for its quick strikes, smashing down upon its enemies with cavalry to sow chaos in their ranks and leave them vulnerable to the rest of the army. Other clans employ similar tactics, usually by ambushing exposed cities or supply trains in the field. The leader rouses their troops for a swift attack to leave the enemy in a state of disarray.</li><li>Once per scene, as an Attack and Movement action, make a TN 3 Command (Fire) check targeting any number of characters in the scene (or one cohort in a mass battle).</li><li>If you succeed during a skirmish, each character increases their initiative by your Fire Ring plus your bonus successes at the beginning of the next round. If you succeed during a mass battle, one enemy leader&#x27;s cohort suffers panic equal to your Fire Ring plus your bonus successes.</li><li>Fire (op): During a skirmish, immediately perform a Strike action.</li><li>Fire (op): During a mass battle, immediately perform an Assault action against the chosen enemy cohort&#x27;s leader.</li></ul>","lookout":"<ul><li>Activation: When you make a check to resist an effect, you may spend opportunities.</li><li>Earth (op)+: One character per (op) spent may immediately switch to a stance of their choice.</li></ul>","lordakodosroarlion":"<ul><li>The Kami Akodo One-Eye, who founded the Lion Clan, was the greatest tactician in the Empire. His victories rested not upon the strength of his arm, but upon his keen mind and his faith in the people he rallied behind him. The true general never stands alone, for they are always bolstered by the united will of their followers. With a roar that echoes through the ranks, chilling their foes and heartening their comrades, the leader charges as Akodo himself once did.</li><li>Once per game session as an action, make a TN 1 Command (Void) check targeting each hostile character within a number of range bands equal to your school rank.</li><li>If you succeed, each target suffers the Dazed condition.</li><li>Void (op)(op)+: After you perform this action, one other friendly character per (op)(op) spent this way at range 0-3 may immediately perform a Strike action targeting a Dazed character.</li></ul>","lordbayushiswhispersscorpion":"<ul><li>The Kami Bayushi, self-appointed villain of the Emperor Hantei and master of duplicity, founded the Scorpion Clan with a simple purpose: to dishonor themselves so that others could live honorably. Bayushi maintained vast networks of spies and informants, and he was extremely skilled at turning assets others used to try to spy on him. The Scorpion Clan has carried on this tradition with an efficiency that would surely make Bayushi proud. Hardly a town exists in the Empire without an agent of the Scorpion.</li><li>Once per game session, during a narrative scene or as a downtime activity, make a TN 2 Skulduggery (Void) check to uncover an informant who can give you information about a subject.</li><li>If you succeed, you reveal one informant who can give you information about a topic of your choice. If the informant&#x27;s profile is required, use an appropriate NPC of the GM&#x27;s choice.</li><li>Void (op): If you succeed, choose one skill. The informant has a number of ranks in that skill equal to your school rank and can perform checks with that skill to assist you until the end of the scene.</li></ul>","lordtogashisinsightdragon":"<ul><li>The enigmatic Kami Togashi was said to have the ability to see the future, by which provenance he excused himself from the Tournament of the Kami. Occasionally he appears to his descendants, the members of the Dragon Clan, in flashes of visions or sudden, unexplained bursts of insight. Whether those who hear the voice of Togashi himself are truly in contact with their progenitor, channeling his essence across the ages, or are letting their imaginations run a bit too wild is a topic of discussion among the Dragon’s scholars.</li><li>Once per game session as an action, make a TN 2 Meditation (Void) check to seek cosmic wisdom regarding a quandary in front of you.</li><li>If you succeed, you receive a brief vision or hear the voice of Togashi providing a hint regarding one way you might proceed (which the GM should furnish). This hint should not be the full answer, but it should help you move forward toward a solution or at least formulate a plan of action.</li><li>Void (op): Reduce the TN of your first check to overcome the problem you are facing by your school rank (to a minimum of 1).</li></ul>","malleableformation":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Movement and Support action, make a TN 2 Command (Water) check targeting two willing characters at range 0-2 who could reach each other&#x27;s positions.</li><li>If you succeed, targets immediately move to switch places. If they do, each may select a new stance.</li></ul>","mentorsguidance":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Support action, make a TN 4 Command (Earth) or TN 4 Performance (Earth) check targeting one character.</li><li>If you succeed, choose one of your kata, ninjutsu, or shūji techniques. Your target may use that technique as if they knew it. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","momentofglory":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Void Shūji</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Movement and Support action during a mass battle, you may make a TN 4 Meditation (Void) check. Reduce TN to 2 if your cohort is in Confining or Obscuring terrain.</li><li>If you succeed, whenever your cohort is targeted with an Attack action check, reduce any attrition it inflicts on your army to 0, and receive that much fatigue yourself instead. If fatigue received causes you to suffer a critical strike, the severity is 16. Persists until start of your next turn.</li><li>Opportunities: Void (op)+: While this effect persists, reduce any fatigue you receive by 1 per (op) spent (minimum 0). Void (op)(op): If you suffer a critical strike this way, it is not applied until the end of the scene. Void (op): If you succeed and survive, double any glory you are awarded.</li></ul>","offendthesensibilities":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Fire Shūji</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: When you make an Artisan (Fire) check to craft an item</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op)(op): Choose one individual known to you. When they first see the item, they receive 2 strife. If this causes Compromised condition, target also suffers Dazed, Enraged, or Silenced (your choice). Anyone else seeing the item knows it could be very offensive.</li></ul>","osanowosboastmantis":"<p>Activation: Once per game session as a Support action, make a TN 2 Command or Performance (Fire) check to boast of a deed you will attempt.</p>","packgambit":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Scheme action, make a TN 3 Social skill (Air) check targeting one character.</li><li>If you succeed, each character who performs an Attack or Scheme action targeting that character counts as having your assistance. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","pillarofcalm":"<ul><li>The character calls for reason to prevail and swords to be sheathed, appealing to a common ideal or greater threat that stands before the belligerent parties.</li><li>As a Scheme and Support action, make a Command (Earth) check targeting a number of characters up to your Earth Ring times your school rank. The TN of this check is equal to the highest strife among the targets.</li><li>If you succeed while targeting all of the leaders involved in a conflict, you may de-escalate the conflict one level (from a mass battle to a skirmish, a skirmish to a duel, or a duel to an intrigue).</li><li>Earth (op)(op)+: You may de-escalate the conflict by one additional level per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","preservestrength":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Water Shūji</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Support action or as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Medicine (Water) check targeting a friendly army or a number of characters at range 0-3 up to your ranks in Command</li><li>If you succeed during a mass battle, your target removes 5 casualties, plus 1 for every two bonus successes. If you succeed during a skirmish, each target reduces the TN of their next Medicine check by 2, plus 1 for every two bonus successes (minimum 1).</li><li>Opportunities: Water (op)(op) (Mass Battle): Choose a friendly leader; remove Bleeding, Burning, or Dying condition. Water (op)(op) (Skirmish): Each target may immediately move 1 range band, or 2 range bands toward a character who is Bleeding, Burning, or Dying.</li></ul>","preyontheweak":"<ul><li>Court is not a kind place, and a harsh word is no less cruel for being spoken softly and with perfect etiquette.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a TN 1 Courtesy (Air) check targeting a Compromised character.</li><li>If you succeed, your target must choose one of the following: (1) Immediately unmask in a manner of their choosing based on the circumstances. (2) Forfeit glory equal to your Air Ring plus your bonus successes to leave the scene.</li><li>Air (op)+: If the target chooses to unmask, you learn one of their disadvantages of their choice per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Air (op)(op): If the target chooses to leave the scene, you notice their destination from the direction of their departure or overhear from the crowd where they will retreat.</li></ul>","rallyingcry":"<ul><li>The leader roars, calling their troops to battle, and the voice of an army echoes around them as the single cry is joined by many. As one, the troops surge forward to claim victory or perish in the attempt.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Command (Fire) or Performance (Fire) check targeting any number of characters in the scene (or one cohort in a mass battle).</li><li>If you succeed, the targets are energized and excited by your rhetoric. After Step 5: Choose Kept Dice, each target adds a kept (ring) set to an (su)(st) result. This effect persists until the end of your next turn.</li><li>Fire (op)+: In a skirmish, each enemy in the scene suffers 1 strife per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Fire (op)+: In a mass battle, the enemy army suffers 1 panic per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","regalbearing":"<ul><li>Courtiers train in the art of carrying themselves no matter what clothing they wear, gaining impeccable control over their posture, tone, and choice of words to project exactly the social standing they desire others to see.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a Command (Water) or Performance (Water) check targeting any number of characters in the scene. The TN of this check is equal to the highest vigilance among your targets.</li><li>If you succeed, each target treats your status as being 10 higher or lower (to a maximum status of 100 or a minimum status of 0), plus or minus an additional 10 per bonus success. If you do anything that could call your status into question, any character may resist with a TN 4 Sentiment check (Earth 2, Fire 5) to determine your actual status attribute. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Water (op): Choose a character in the scene. Learn if their status is higher or lower than yours (the actual value).</li></ul>","righteousexample":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Fire Shūji</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: As an Attack and Support action during a mass battle, you may make a TN 3 Martial Arts (Fire) check targeting an enemy leader&#x27;s cohort</li><li>If you succeed, the enemy army suffers attrition and panic equal to 1 plus your bonus successes. Other leaders in your army reduce the TN of their Attack action checks by 1 until end of your next turn. If you fail, reduce the TN of Attack and Scheme action checks targeting your cohort by 1 until end of your next turn.</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op)(op): If you are both the commander and a leader, your army gains 1 momentum point toward its current strategic objective.</li></ul>","roarofencouragement":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Support action, make a TN 3 Command (Fire) check targeting a friendly character.</li><li>In skirmish: target may immediately perform a Strike action with your assistance. In mass battle: target&#x27;s cohort may immediately perform an Assault action with your assistance.</li></ul>","rousethesoul":"<ul><li>Many things can cloud the soul, but words can awaken it. The courtier speaks honestly and without pretension, calling upon their allies to overcome earthly circumstances and reach a mutual goal.</li><li>When making a Social skill (Void) or Theology (Void) check targeting one or more characters, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Void (op)+: Remove one of the following conditions from one target per (op) spent this way: Afflicted, Enraged, Exhausted, Intoxicated, or Unconscious.</li></ul>","ruseofthemoonsreflection":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Scheme action, make a Command (Air) check targeting any number of characters not hostile to each other. TN equals highest vigilance. In mass battle, must target all commanders.</li><li>In intrigue/skirmish/duel: exchange initiative values of any number of targets. In mass battle: reveal that two leaders of the same army have exchanged cohorts and positions.</li></ul>","rustlingofleaves":"<ul><li>If everyone has heard a scandalous story, but it has no clear source, what can it be but true? The courtier cleverly spreads stories so none see them as the source.</li><li>When you make a Social skill (Air) check to spread a rumor, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Air (op)+: Increase the TN of any check to trace the rumor back to you by 2 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","searthewound":"<ul><li>Many courtiers cannot resist the opportunity to twist the knife after delivering a stabbing remark, but the wise use this power judiciously. Though somewhat cruel, the technique of bringing a rival’s weakness to the forefront of their mind to burn away at their resolve is often effective.</li><li>When making a Social skill (Fire) check targeting one or more characters, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Fire (op)+: Choose a known disadvantage of one of your targets per (op) spent this way. That disadvantage applies to all of the target&#x27;s checks until the end of the scene.</li></ul>","sensationaldistraction":"<ul><li>Standing out in court requires a great deal of both cunning and flair, and standing out on purpose can be even harder. Courtiers train for much of their lives to learn to control the perceptions of others at court. The best courtiers know when to draw attention to themselves with a display of rhetorical prowess or another social feat and when to avoid attention. Drawing attention to oneself can give collaborators the chance to work unnoticed as well, and thus it is an extremely valuable tool in the courtier’s arsenal.</li><li>When making a Social skill (Fire) check targeting one or more characters, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Fire (op)+: When interacting with other characters, the target treats their vigilance as 1 lower per (op) spent this way; when interacting with you, the target treats their vigilance as 1 higher per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li></ul>","shallowwaters":"<ul><li>A good courtier learns how to read the desires of those around them from the subtle cues of their responses in conversation, as well as how to probe for details without revealing their intentions.</li><li>When you make a Social skill (Water) check targeting a character, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Water (op): Learn of one material item or worldly experience the target desires.</li><li>Water (op)(op): Learn the target&#x27;s Ninjō.</li></ul>","slipperymaneuvers":"<ul><li>The leader makes several signals and calls out a command—often a code word—to their troops; suddenly, the formation shifts in unison to take advantage of the terrain around them.</li><li>As a Movement and Support action, make a TN 2 Command (Water) check targeting any number of friendly characters in the scene (or your cohort during a mass battle). This technique can only be used during a skirmish or mass battle.</li><li>If you succeed during a skirmish, choose a position containing terrain that you can see. Each target may immediately move 1 range band toward it. Attack checks targeting any of your targets inside the terrain treat the terrain as having the Obscuring terrain quality. This effect persists until the end of the scene. If you succeed during a mass battle, choose a piece of terrain you can see. You and your cohort may immediately move to occupy it if it is unoccupied. Attack action checks targeting you and your cohort while you are inside the terrain treat the terrain as having the Obscuring terrain quality. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Water (op): Each target is able to leverage Obscuring terrain to better effect; Attack action checks targeting them have their TN increased by 2 instead of 1. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li></ul>","solidifygratitude":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Courtesy (Earth) check targeting another character. Can only target a character who has accepted a gift from you this scene or has completed a social objective to which you contributed momentum.</li><li>If you succeed, you gain the Ally (Target&#x27;s Name) [Water] advantage unless your target chooses to forfeit glory equal to the rarity of the gift you gave or the number of momentum points you contributed to their objective.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): You learn your target&#x27;s reason for pursuing their social objective. (op)(op): You gain your target&#x27;s assistance on the next check you make until end of scene.</li></ul>","spinthewebkolat":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Air Shūji (Kolat)</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: Once per game session, during a narrative scene or as a downtime activity</li><li>Check: TN 2 Skulduggery (Air)</li><li>If you succeed, recruit a minor or previously unknown NPC (GM discretion) as a Kolat asset. Record them under your Relationships. Once per game session you may call on one asset you can reasonably contact. The NPC aids you during a single scene or conducts a single downtime activity.</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op): If you succeed, choose one skill. The NPC has ranks in that skill equal to your school rank and can perform checks with that skill to assist you.</li></ul>","spitefulloss":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Fire Shūji</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: When you make a Games (Fire) check while playing a game</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op): If you fail, forfeit 1 glory. Then each participant receives strife equal to 1 plus the shortfall.</li></ul>","stingofwarriorspride":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Fire Shūji</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Performance (Fire) check targeting an army or one character who can hear you. You may stake up to 3 glory to reduce the TN by that amount (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, you spur your target to greater courage. The first time your target is dealt attrition or damage during the next scene, they reduce the amount by your ranks in Performance, to a minimum of 0. Whether you succeed or fail, if observed acting in a cowardly manner by your target, you lose any staked glory.</li></ul>","stirringtheembers":"<ul><li>A good leader does not just compensate for the weaknesses of comrades, but also fosters their innate strengths. The courtier reminds an ally of one of their finer qualities, sparking their pride to get them to fight more fiercely or speak with greater conviction.</li><li>When making a Social skill (Fire) check targeting one or more characters, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Fire (op)+: Choose a target and one of their known distinctions per (op) spent this way. Until the end of the scene, when that advantage applies to a check, the target may reroll up to three dice (instead of two).</li></ul>","stonewalltactics":"<ul><li>The courtier makes themself impossible for the target to ignore, raising a pressing concern that must be addressed first or even physically planting themself between a rival and their allies.</li><li>When making a Social skill (Earth) or Martial skill (Earth) check targeting a character, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Earth (op)+: Increase the TN of any check the target makes that does not target you by 1 per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the beginning of your next turn.</li></ul>","theimmovablehandofpeace":"<ul><li>The courtier calls for the warriors in the field to lay down their arms and withdraw with such unquestionable conviction that even the fires of hate are temporarily smothered.</li><li>Once per game session as a Scheme action, during a duel or skirmish, make a TN 5 Command (Earth) check targeting every character in the scene.</li><li>If you succeed, the scene becomes an intrigue between you and the other principal characters. This effect persists for one round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes. If you have not achieved a peaceful resolution by the time this effect ends, the scene returns to its previous state.</li><li>Earth (op): You may also perform this action during a mass battle or other form of conflict (other than an intrigue).</li></ul>","thewindblowsbothways":"<ul><li>A word in the right ear at the right time can enhance the accomplishment of another, or a cutting slight can diminish their success in the eyes of those who matter.</li><li>When you make a Courtesy or Performance (Air) check targeting another character, you may spend (op) in the following ways:</li><li>Air (op)+: The next time the target receives a glory award, increase the glory they gain by 1 per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Air (op)+: The next time the target forfeits or stakes glory, increase the glory they must forfeit or stake by 1 per (op) spent this way. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li></ul>","tosmashtheheart":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Fire Shūji</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: Once per scene, after a character in the scene (or enemy leader, in a mass battle) becomes Compromised or is killed, you may immediately make a TN 4 Tactics (Fire) check targeting that character</li><li>If you succeed in an intrigue, skirmish, or duel, each character allied with your target who has lower status receives strife equal to your bonus successes plus your ranks in Sentiment. If you succeed in a mass battle, the enemy army receives panic equal to your bonus successes plus your ranks in Sentiment.</li></ul>","tonightiamyouropponent":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per game session as a Scheme and Support action, make a TN 3 Social skill (Void) check targeting one character currently fighting in a duel or clash.</li><li>If you succeed, immediately replace target in the duel or clash, staking your own honor and glory. Target forfeits half their staked honor and glory. If you share a bond with the character you are replacing or their adversary, no character must forfeit honor or glory.</li></ul>","touchstoneofcourage":"<ul><li>Armies are rarely routed in the field; instead, most collapse when morale becomes impossible to maintain. As panic rises in the ranks, soldiers look to leaders to set an example. The character does just this, speaking to the importance of duty to bring their troops back from the edge of chaos.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 4 Command (Earth) check targeting any number of characters (or your cohort during a mass battle).</li><li>If you succeed during an intrigue, duel, or skirmish conflict, each target increases their composure by your Earth Ring. This effect persists until the end of the scene. If you succeed during a mass battle, increase your army&#x27;s discipline by your Earth Ring plus your bonus successes. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): During an intrigue, duel, or skirmish, each target removes strife equal to your Earth Ring.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): During a mass battle, your army removes panic equal to your Earth Ring.</li></ul>","tradersintuition":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Scheme action, you may make a Commerce (Air) check targeting an object you can observe. TN is 2, or 4 if the object has the Forbidden item quality.</li><li>If you succeed, you assess the target, learning its monetary value and rarity.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): You know a place (which you have visited) where you could sell the object for more money than it is worth in your current location.</li></ul>","tributariesoftrade":"<ul><li>Gift giving is an important cultural practice in Rokugan (as is the art of gift refusal, which any potential recipient must repeat at least twice before accepting the third offer). While some courtiers have a gift prepared for any possible contingency, many simply get acquainted with the art of explaining why a gift could only have been intended for its current recipient (even if they originally procured it for a different purpose). The ability to quickly acquire an item is valued among all courtiers, as a gift demands reciprocity in some kind, whether that be in favors, esteem, or subsequent gifts.</li><li>Once per scene as a Scheme and Support action, make a TN 1 Commerce (Water) skill check to establish that you acquired a chosen item earlier. From a narrative standpoint, you procured this gift during your last opportunity (or sent an attendant to retrieve it) but are only revealing it now.</li><li>If you succeed, you produce an item with a rarity less than or equal to 1 plus your bonus successes. You must still pay the price of the item.</li><li>Water (op)+: Reduce the price you must pay for the item by one-quarter per (op) spent this way (to a minimum of one-quarter of the original price).</li></ul>","truthburnsthroughlies":"<ul><li>The courtier rapidly extrapolates, imagining the ramifications of a story and conjecturing what might have gone unsaid. If a loose thread exists in the account, they can find it, and that first thread can become the unraveling of the most cunning duplicity.</li><li>When making a Scholar skill (Fire) check to assess a character&#x27;s story, you may spend (op) in the following way:</li><li>Fire (op): If there is a single statement upon which the character&#x27;s story hinges, you determine what it is and what you would need to do to verify or disprove it.</li></ul>","unyieldingterms":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Earth Shūji</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Scheme action when determining duel method and stakes</li><li>Check: TN 4 Culture (Earth)</li><li>You select either the method of battle, or the stakes for victory.</li></ul>","victorywithoutasword":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Void Shūji</li><li>Rank: 6</li><li>Activation: As an Attack, Movement, Scheme, and Support action during a mass battle, you may make a TN 6 Tactics (Void) check targeting the enemy commander. Reduce TN to 4 if all enemy cohorts are in Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain. Can only be attempted once per army per scene.</li><li>If you succeed, the enemy commander immediately resists with a TN 5 Command check (Void 3), adding 1 to the TN for every 10 strength your army has in excess of theirs. If the enemy commander fails, the enemy army suffers 10 panic for each point of their shortfall. If the enemy army collapses this way, its forces surrender. If you fail, reduce the TN of Attack action checks targeting the cohorts of leaders in your army by 2 (minimum 1) until end of scene.</li></ul>","wanderersresolve":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Support action, if you are in a Void stance, focus on protecting what is important to you.</li><li>Remove 3 fatigue and 3 strife, plus 3 fatigue and 3 strife for each Compromised or Incapacitated character in the scene with whom you share a bond.</li></ul>","watchmyback":"<ul><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Movement and Support action, if you are in a Water stance, call for a character at range 0-2 to cover you.</li><li>Chosen character may immediately perform a Guard action targeting you, ignoring range restrictions. If they succeed, you may move up to 2 range bands. Reduce TN of your next action check this turn by 1.</li></ul>","weightofduty":"<ul><li>All samurai know the pressure of expectation in countless forms. An observant courtier can read this when engaging with another character, learning their beliefs and in what ways they fear they might not live up to their own expectations.</li><li>When you make a Social skill (Earth) check targeting a character, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Earth (op): Learn one way the target fears failing as a samurai.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): Learn the target&#x27;s Giri.</li></ul>","wellofdesire":"<ul><li>Bribery is considered to be corruption in Rokugan, yet gift exchanges and gift giving is a time-honored tradition. The shrewdest courtiers can engineer scenarios in which their targets cannot refuse their gifts without tarnishing their reputations. Thus, the recipient of such a poisoned gift might find it preferable to owe the courtier a favor than to be shamed in public.</li><li>When you make a Courtesy (Water) check to present a gift to a target, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>Water (op): To refuse your gift, your target must forfeit glory equal to your Water Ring. Additionally, if the gift is something that the target desires, the target also must suffer strife equal to its rarity to refuse it. If your target accepts the gift, reduce the TN of your next Social skill check targeting them by the rarity of the item (to a minimum of 1).</li></ul>","whispersofcourt":"<ul><li>Rumors are the currency of court, and when such news is in short supply, many courtiers simply spin it themselves. They use cunning schemes and plausible half-truths to bait their webs of intrigue.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a Courtesy (Air) check targeting each character in the scene. The TN of this check is equal to the lowest vigilance among your targets.</li><li>If you succeed, you create a rumor that sweeps across the room like a storm. Everyone in the scene hears it, and characters with vigilance lower than your bonus successes even come to give it some credence. If spreading a rumor is your social objective in an intrigue, you score rhetorical points equal to your Air Ring plus your bonus successes.</li><li>Air (op): Learn one other rumor that is spreading in the current scene.</li></ul>","wolfsproposal":"<ul><li>Being honorable is of the same value to a courtier as appearing honorable. True honor cannot be faked, but fortunately for many, the appearance of respectability can be fabricated.</li><li>As a Scheme action, make a Courtesy or Performance (Air) check targeting any number of characters in the scene. The TN of this check is equal to the highest vigilance among your targets.</li><li>If you succeed, each target behaves as though your honor is 10 higher or lower than its actual value, plus or minus an additional 10 for each bonus success (to a maximum honor value of 100 or a minimum honor value of 0). If you do anything that could call your perceived honor into question, any target may resist with a TN 4 Sentiment check (Earth 5, Fire 2) to determine your actual honor attribute. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Air (op): Choose a character in the scene. Learn if their honor is higher or lower than yours (the actual value).</li></ul>","yourenemysarrows":"<ul><li>Type: Shūji</li><li>Subtype: Water Shūji</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: Once per scene as a Scheme action targeting another character who can perceive you or your cohort, you may make a Tactics (Water) check. TN equals target&#x27;s focus. You may stake up to 3 glory to reduce TN by that amount.</li><li>If you succeed, the next time your target accrues momentum points toward an objective, add those momentum points to your objective instead. If you fail, you lose the glory you staked.</li><li>Opportunities: Water (op): Your target remains unaware of your machinations. If you failed, regain your staked glory. Water (op): Gain 1 momentum point. Water (op)+: All characters in the scene with vigilance lower than or equal to (op) spent are unaware of your machinations.</li></ul>","accursedsummoning":"<ul><li>Rank: 1</li><li>The mahō-tsukai spills blood and recites a foul prayer to summon a chosen oni and bind it to their will. The oni appears caught in an invisible prison, unable to act except at the summoner&#x27;s direction.</li><li>XP Cost: 3</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity action, you may make a Theology (Void) check with TN equal to the oni&#x27;s Intrigue rank.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon the desired oni and bind it to your will, unable to act without your consent. If you fail, you summon the desired oni (or a different one, at the GM&#x27;s discretion) but it breaks free of your control and curses you, causing you to suffer the Afflicted condition. If you have 3 or more kept (ring) results, the summoned oni scries and learns your name.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: The sight of the oni instills primal terror in any onlookers. Each character who can see the oni and is within range 3 suffers a number of strife equal to (op) spent this way. (op)(op): The oni instills a Shadowlands Taint disadvantage of your choice upon anyone within a range equal to the number of your rings with the Shadowlands Taint disadvantage attached.</li></ul>","bindtheundead":"<ul><li>Rank: 2</li><li>The mahō-tsukai draws on the power of Jigoku to extend their will over the animated dead (such as skeletons or zombies). These undead then act as the mahō-tsukai commands, mimicking gestures or following simple instructions. They can attack a target or follow the mahō-tsukai like a squad of troops follows their leader. A smaller number of undead allows the practitioner greater control, and a single undead being can act naturally enough to infiltrate a town or castle, if the practitioner remains nearby and sustains the necessary concentration.</li><li>Activation: As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (Fire) check targeting a number of undead creatures up to your Earth Ring at range 0–4. You can only choose undead creatures with combat rank 3 or lower this way.</li><li>If you succeed, you bind each target to your will. They can now act only under your control, via simple voice commands. You can issue straightforward commands with your allocated five words per turn, or you can issue more complex commands if you dedicate your action to giving a command. If you are killed or become Unconscious due to a critical strike, all bound undead under your control cease to function, slumping to the ground as inanimate corpses. Whether you succeed or fail, an area encompassing 1 range band around each target&#x27;s position gains the Defiled terrain quality.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): One undead creature you choose becomes a revenant (see page 18) in addition to becoming bound. (op)+: Treat the maximum range of the technique as 1 higher per (op) spent this way. (op)+: Treat the maximum combat rank of an undead creature you can bind as 1 higher per (op) spent this way. If you bind an intelligent undead creature this way and later lose control of it, it reverts to its own goals instead of becoming inanimate.</li></ul>","communewithevil":"<ul><li>The practitioner detects any malevolent supernatural entities in the area, senses their desires, and makes a bargain for an unholy blessing.</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity action, you may make a TN 1 Theology (Void) check.</li><li>If you succeed, you scry for the presence of any Otherworldly or Tainted beings at range 0–6.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If there are any such beings, they accept your offering, and they augment you with an unholy blessing that increases the value of the ring you used for the check by 1. You can only have one unholy blessing at a time, and it persists until the end of the next scene. (op)(op)(op)+: If you receive an unholy blessing, it temporarily increases the ring&#x27;s value by an additional 1 per (op)(op)(op) spent this way. (op)+: If you receive an unholy blessing, it persists for 1 additional scene per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","darkreflection":"<ul><li>Rank: 1</li><li>The mahō-tsukai must obtain an obsidian mirror, pool of Tainted water, or other corrupted reflective surface. By appealing to kansen, the practitioner makes the object become a divinatory tool for a time. The practitioner can receive visual answers to questions or spy on a person or area. Kansen are willing to play this &quot;game,&quot; but the accuracy of images may not be reliable.</li><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check targeting a person, object, or location you have encountered before.</li><li>If you succeed, you scry upon a chosen person or location. However, the image is distorted: one minor detail within it, of the GM&#x27;s choosing, is always incorrect, reflecting instead the fears or desires of the mahō-tsukai.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op)(op): You bind the kansen within the object permanently. The object gains the Unholy quality and retains its divinatory properties after the initial use. As a Support action, a character may give the object an offering of blood to show the chosen object, person, or location again.</li></ul>","entreattheshadowsteed":"<ul><li>Rank: 2</li><li>The mahō-tsukai compels the kansen to fetch a suitable mount. The onikage rises from the ground as a skeletal mount, or an undead horse with decaying flesh comes galloping across the Shadowlands.</li><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (Earth) check. This technique can be used only in the Shadowlands, or near a place where the corpse of a horse might be found, such as an ancient or recent battlefield.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon an onikage (see page 23) and bind it to your will. It obeys your commands, allowing you to ride it as per the Mounts and Riding rules on page 326 of the core rulebook. It reacts violently if others try to ride it.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): The equine creature retains enough flesh to pass as a living horse; characters with vigilance 3 or lower do not notice its undead status. (op)(op)(op): Other characters whom you designate can also ride the onikage. (op)(op)+: Summon one additional onikage per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","fiendsretreat":"<ul><li>This technique allows its user to exchange positions with an unsuspecting character, leaving them to meet a miserable end. The blade descends, but the sorcerer&#x27;s flesh twists like wax and melts to foul muck, revealing some unfortunate whom the mahō-tsukai left to meet the judgment they so richly deserve.</li><li>Activation: Once per scene, as an Attack and Movement action or as an out-of-turn action when you are targeted by an attack, you may make a Theology (Air) check targeting one character at range 2–3. The target must be Incapacitated or a minion NPC, and the TN of the check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, you curse the target, forcing them to exchange physical locations with you. The target becomes the target of any attacks that were targeting you.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Choose one additional character at range 0–1 to move and one additional target per (op) spent this way. (op)+: Increase the maximum range by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","gripofanguish":"<ul><li>The mahō-tsukai calls for the kansen afflicting their victim to wreak sickness and agony upon them. The victim is tormented by nausea, pain, and feverish delusions.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a Theology (Water) check targeting one living being at range 0-2. The TN of the check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, you curse your target, causing them to suffer supernatural damage equal to your Water Ring plus the number of your rings with a Shadowlands Taint disadvantage attached.</li><li>Water (op): One target must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Earth 1, Fire 4) or suffer one of the following conditions of your choice: Dazed, Disoriented, Silenced.</li><li>Water (op)+: Treat the maximum range of the technique as 1 higher per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Water (op)+: Choose one additional target per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Water (op)(op): One target must resist with a TN 3 Fitness check (Earth 1, Fire 4) or suffer one of the following conditions of your choice: Bleeding, Immobilized, or Lightly Wounded.</li></ul>","incitehaunting":"<ul><li>Kansen are kami twisted by the power of Fu Leng, and they need little prompting to cause harm. Directing them toward a target with a vile rite and profane words that seem to warp the air, the mahō-tsukai afflicts a poor soul with a spiritual malady that can fester and bloom, fueling darker curses still. Spiritualists can perceive kansen as wretched, ghostly figures, clinging to their victim and dragging them inexorably toward a wretched end wrought by their worst nature.</li><li>As an Attack and Scheme action, make a Theology check targeting one character at range 0-1. This check uses any ring of your choice, and the TN of the check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, you curse your target, causing them to suffer the Afflicted condition. If you fail, the target rebuffs your efforts. If your shortfall is 2 or higher, the target also becomes aware of your attempted malediction.</li><li>(op)+: Treat the maximum range of the technique as 1 higher per (op) spent this way.</li><li>(op)+: Choose one additional target per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","markofdesecration":"<ul><li>The mahō-tsukai performs the rite upon a corpse or group of corpses, placing ominous masks over their faces and whispering dark words into their dead ears. The dead are dragged to their feet by the kansen possessing them, moving with the jerking, unnatural gait of an ill-made puppet.</li><li>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Theology (Earth) check targeting a number of corpses up to your Earth Ring at range 0-3.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a Zombie Peasant from each target. You also curse an area encompassing 1 range band around each target&#x27;s position, which gains the Defiled terrain quality.</li><li>Earth (op)+: Choose one additional target per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Earth (op)+: Increase each zombie&#x27;s endurance by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li><li>Earth (op)(op): Once per round, one zombie may use your skill ranks instead of its own for a check.</li><li>Earth (op)(op)+: One target who was a warrior in life per (op)(op) spent this way rises as a Bushi Skeleton instead.</li></ul>","shapetheflesh":"<ul><li>Rank: 4</li><li>The mahō-tsukai transforms their body, taking on a demonic aspect. Ragged wings or a glistening carapace sprouts from their flesh, or their form flows like befouled water, extending unnaturally. They might even fade into living shadow, becoming a creature of pure obscurity that shrugs off even the holiest of talismans and prayers.</li><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a TN 4 Theology check.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment and curse yourself in one of the following ways, depending on the ring you used: Talons and Fangs (Fire): The damage and deadliness of your Unarmed profile become 6, and it gains the Unholy quality. Thick Hide (Earth): Your physical resistance becomes 7. Wings (Air): You gain flight; you can move vertically and ignore the negative effects of terrain. Malleable Form (Water): The maximum range of your unarmed and melee attacks becomes 3. Shadowy Form (Void): Your supernatural resistance becomes 7. You count as an Otherworldly being.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): Once before the end of the scene, as an action, you may perform this technique again with a different ring and maintain both effects.</li></ul>","sinfulwhispers":"<ul><li>The kansen assail the victim’s mind, murmuring dark things that slowly erode their concentration, making them more receptive to the words of the mahō-tsukai and less able to think coherently.</li><li>As an Attack and Scheme action, make a Theology (Air) check targeting one character with the Afflicted condition at range 0-4. The TN of the check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, you curse your target, sapping their will; they must answer your questions honestly (and find doing so unremarkable at the time). This effect persists for a number of rounds equal to your Air Ring.</li><li>Air (op): The target does not remember what you asked, even if prompted to think about the conversation later.</li><li>Air (op)(op)(op): You may give the target a single simple order. The target may ignore that order, but receives 2 strife at the end of each scene in which they disregard it. When the target becomes Compromised, they must unmask and attempt to fulfill the order until the end of the scene.</li></ul>","spiritualshackles":"<ul><li>Mahō-tsukai deal constantly with powerful, dangerous beings, and those who live long enough learn that kansen can only be trusted to be untrustworthy—but deceit can be repaid in kind. Other spirits might also seek to wreak vengeance upon mahō-tsukai, from the hungering ghosts called gaki to wrathful ancestor spirits, and it pays to have protection against such beings. The mahō-tsukai uses trickery and sheer will on a kansen or other spirit, sealing it within an object.</li><li>Activation: As an Attack and Scheme action, you may make a Theology (Air) check targeting one Otherworldly being at range 0–1. The TN of this check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance and is reduced by 2 if the target is also a Tainted being.</li><li>If you succeed, you bind the spirit inside an object of silhouette 1 or less at range 0–2. If the being you bound is Tainted, the object gains the Unholy quality. If you fail, the spirit curses you, and you suffer the Afflicted condition.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): The object gains one other quality of your choice from the following list: Concealable, Durable, Resplendent, Subtle. (op): As an action, the holder of the object may release the bound being to importune one mahō (or invocation, if you have bound an elemental spirit) without paying the usual costs or making the usual TN adjustments (see Importune Invocations on page 189 and Importune Mahō on page 225 of the core rulebook).</li></ul>","spreadcorruption":"<ul><li>Rank: 2</li><li>The practitioner channels their inner corruption into their skin, so that their touch becomes contagious. Anyone or anything they touch is assailed by the foul influence of the Shadowlands, which seeks any gap in their spiritual fortitude that it can grasp.</li><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (Fire) check.</li><li>If you succeed, you augment your touch with a corrupting influence. Anyone whose skin you touch (such as with an unarmed attack) is cursed, and they must resist with a TN 4 Fitness or Meditation check (Earth 2, Fire 5) or suffer fatigue equal to their shortfall and the Afflicted condition. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): After you touch someone, the effect is delayed for three rounds, or about a minute in narrative time. (op): While this effect persists, any ground you walk on becomes Defiled terrain (see Terrain on page 267 of the core rulebook). (op)(op): Increase the severity of any critical strike you inflict with your unarmed attack profiles by 2 for each of your rings with the Shadowlands Taint disadvantage.</li></ul>","swordofblood":"<ul><li>Rank: 2</li><li>The mahō-tsukai draws blood from an open wound, the vital fluid swirling up to their outstretched palm and congealing into a deadly weapon.</li><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a TN 2 Theology (Water) check. Performing this technique requires a source of blood, such as a corpse or nearby foe with the Bleeding condition. If the mahō-tsukai uses their own blood, they receive 3 fatigue.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon a weapon of your choosing made of blood. It has the Unholy quality (see page 241 of the core rulebook).</li><li>Opportunities: (op): You may summon a pair of identical weapons instead of a single weapon. (op): At the end of each of your turns, you may transform the weapon into a different weapon. (op)(op): You may immediately perform a Strike action using the weapon you summoned. (op)(op): After you inflict a critical strike on another character with this weapon, remove fatigue from yourself equal to the severity of the critical strike (after the check to resist).</li></ul>","twistedsummons":"<ul><li>Rank: 3</li><li>The mahō-tsukai calls forth an abomination from Jigoku, giving it a temporary cage of flesh from which to wreak carnage upon the Mortal Realm. The being that comes forth is a fused horror, an agglomeration of multiple corpses twisted into unnatural form.</li><li>Activation: As an Intrigue and Support action, you may make a TN 3 Theology (Earth) check to call upon a foul spirit to target a number of corpses at range 0–2, reshaping them into an abominable body for its use.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon an Undead Horror (see page 19) and bind it to your will. However, the summoned creature is one not easily kept shackled; if you become Compromised or Incapacitated, it breaks the binding and sets off on its own to devour the living and absorb the dead. Whether you succeed or fail, an area at range 0–2 of your target becomes Defiled terrain.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: The Undead Horror absorbs up to two additional corpses at range 0–2 for each (op) spent this way. Increase its endurance by 2 for each corpse it absorbs. For every five corpses the monster absorbs this way, increase its silhouette by 1.</li></ul>","unholyfervor":"<ul><li>The kansen bite and tear the flesh of the victim, wracking them with pain that transforms into mindless fury.</li><li>As a Support action, make a Theology (Fire) check targeting one character at range 0-3. The TN of this check is equal to the target&#x27;s vigilance.</li><li>If you succeed, you curse the target with blinding fury; they suffer the Enraged condition. You also augment the target&#x27;s corruption; they may treat each of their Shadowlands Taint disadvantages as an advantage that applies to any checks using its ring. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</li><li>Fire (op): Each target receives strife equal to your Fire Ring and removes that much fatigue.</li><li>Fire (op)+: Choose one additional target per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","artfulalibi":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: When you make a Skulduggery check to surveil or engage in clandestine activities during downtime</li><li>Opportunities: Air or Water (op)+: If you succeed, you also count as having made a successful downtime Composition or Design check to refine (Air) or adapt (Water) an item, with one bonus success per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","cunningdistraction":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: As a Scheme action during a duel or clash</li><li>Check: TN 2 Skulduggery check targeting one character engaged in the duel or clash</li><li>Performing this action is cheating. Any character with vigilance of 2 or higher spots the cheating. If you succeed, during the next round both characters engaged swap their initiative order.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: The vigilance required to spot the cheating is increased by 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","deadlysting":"<ul><li>Poison is not a weapon an honorable samurai would choose, but it is tremendously effective, and like its namesake, the Scorpion Clan is not above envenoming its weapons to defeat foes it otherwise could not best.</li><li>As an Attack action, you may use one dose of a poison and make a TN 3 Martial Arts (Air) check using a readied Concealable weapon targeting one character within the weapon&#x27;s range.</li><li>If you succeed, apply the chosen poison to your weapon (see Poison). Then, the target suffers physical damage equal to the deadliness of your weapon plus your bonus successes.</li><li>Air (op): Move 1 range band.</li><li>Air (op)+: If you succeed, the target suffers a critical strike with severity 2, plus 1 per (op) spent this way.</li></ul>","deceitfulstrike":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: When you make a Martial Arts check during a duel or clash</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Each observer with vigilance equal to or less than one plus (op) spent this way believes your attack was not meant to be lethal.</li></ul>","employterriblethunder":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: As a Movement and Support action, you may make a TN 4 Skulduggery check and expend 1 charge of blasting powder to place it at a target position at range 0-1. You must forfeit honor equal to half your honor rank (rounded up).</li><li>If you succeed, the blasting powder explodes at the end of the next round. (Mass Battle) Nearby cohort&#x27;s army receives 5 attrition and 5 panic, plus 1 per bonus success. If placed inside a fortification, reduce its difficulty value by 1 plus 1 per bonus success. One affected cohort leader suffers Immobilized and Lightly Wounded. (Other Scene) Each character at range 0-2 suffers 10 physical damage plus 1 per bonus success, suffers Dazed, and receives 5 strife. Items at range 0-2 gain Damaged. Structures at range 0-1 gain Damaged.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): Any item or structure damaged gains the Destroyed quality instead. (op)(op): Area at range 0-2 gains Dangerous and Obscuring terrain qualities. (op)+: The blasting powder does not detonate for one additional round per (op) spent.</li></ul>","likeaghost":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: As a Movement and Scheme action</li><li>Check: TN 2 Fitness (Air or Water)</li><li>If you succeed, you may move one range band, plus one additional range band per two bonus successes. This movement ignores terrain effects. You may move up or down vertical surfaces or across jumpable gaps.</li><li>Opportunities: (op)(op): Your footfalls are completely silent.</li></ul>","noxiouscloud":"<ul><li>Volatile concoctions are an important weapon in many shinobi’s arsenals, allowing them to create choking smoke into which they can escape or even poison unprepared foes to weaken them for a killing blow.</li><li>As an Attack action, you may use two doses of any single poison and make a TN 2 Medicine (Air) check targeting each other character at range 0-2.</li><li>If you succeed, each target suffers 3 physical damage, ignoring their resistance. This damage counts as being inflicted by a weapon envenomed with the poison you chose (see Poison).</li><li>Air (op): Move 1 range band.</li><li>Air (op)+: Until the end of the scene, the area at range 0-2 becomes Obscuring and Dangerous terrain.</li><li>Air (op)(op)+: If you succeed, one target per (op)(op) spent this way suffers a critical strike with severity 2.</li></ul>","silencingstroke":"<ul><li>Shinobi must often eliminate targets without raising an alarm, and so they often train in the art of disabling with a single strike. A shuriken to the trachea or a swift blow to occlude the carotid artery can leave a target unable to scream while the shinobi finishes their unsavory work.</li><li>As an Attack action, make a TN 4 Martial Arts (Air) check using a readied weapon targeting one character within the weapon&#x27;s range.</li><li>If you succeed, the target suffers physical damage equal to your weapon&#x27;s base damage and suffers the Silenced condition. Other characters beyond range 0-2 of the target do not notice that they have been struck for 1 round, plus additional rounds equal to your bonus successes.</li><li>Air (op)+: If you succeed, the target suffers a critical strike with severity equal to the deadliness of your weapon plus 1 per (op) spent this way beyond the first.</li></ul>","silentelimination":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action using one readied melee or unarmed weapon with Snaring quality</li><li>Check: TN 3 Martial Arts [Melee or Unarmed] targeting one living character of silhouette 0-2 in range. TN reduced by 2 (minimum 1) if performed against same target as previous round.</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers Immobilized and Silenced conditions, pulled to range 0. Target limited to Martial Arts [Unarmed] checks targeting you with TN increased by 1.</li><li>Opportunities: (op): If succeed and target is minion, they suffer Unconscious condition. (op)+: Target suffers 2 fatigue and 2 strife per (op). (op)(op): You and target move one range band.</li></ul>","skulk":"<ul><li>Shinobi are known for walking silently from shadow to shadow, moving like phantoms. Some of this relies upon agility and speed, of course, but veterans in the art of stealth know that using a crowd or another visual distraction to walk unnoticed can be as effective as the most complex acrobatics.</li><li>When you perform an Initiative or Attack check using Air, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op): If you are in Obscuring terrain, a crowd, or otherwise concealed from sight, one character with vigilance lower than or equal to your ranks in Skulduggery loses sight of you.</li></ul>","slicingwindkick":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action using one readied polearm</li><li>Check: TN 3 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Air) with unarmed kick profile targeting one character at range 1-2</li><li>If you succeed, the target suffers physical damage equal to unarmed kick base damage plus bonus successes and the Disoriented condition.</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op): Move 1 range band. Air (op)(op): One target suffers Prone condition. Air (op)(op)+: Choose one additional target per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","stillnessofdeath":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 5</li><li>Activation: When you perform a check to use a Ninjutsu technique</li><li>Opportunities: (op)+: Increase TN of the next check a character makes to resist a critical strike you inflict by 1 per (op) spent this way. Persists until end of your next turn.</li></ul>","swiftscouting":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 1</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, or once per scene as a Movement and Support action, you may make a TN 3 Survival (Water) check to scout the terrain. In urban environments use Skulduggery; on the ocean use Seafaring.</li><li>If you succeed, you discover all terrain qualities of the area around you (several miles during downtime, or entire scene area), as well as any fortifications. Characters with vigilance lower than your Air Ring plus bonus successes do not detect you.</li><li>Opportunities: Water (op)(op) (Downtime or Mass Battle): Choose one area and add one terrain quality: Confining, Dangerous, Entangling, Obscuring. Water (op)(op) (Other Scene): Choose a position; up to three range bands surrounding it gain one terrain quality. Water (op)+: Discover location and composition of enemy forces led by characters with Air Ring lower than your vigilance plus (op) spent. Water (op)(op)(op): During your next turn, if you target an enemy cohort, ignore any fortification it is occupying.</li></ul>","thepatientviper":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Fitness (Earth) check targeting your cohort or yourself and a number of characters up to your ranks in Command who are within Dangerous, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain</li><li>If you succeed, all targets become hidden and are not noticed by characters with vigilance lower than or equal to your Earth Ring plus bonus successes. Hidden characters cannot be targeted by Attack actions. Persists until end of your next turn, or until any target performs an Attack or Movement action.</li><li>Opportunities: Earth (op)+: Persists for one additional round per (op) spent. Earth (op)+: Reduce the TN of the first Attack action check one of your targets makes against another character in the terrain by 1 per (op) spent.</li></ul>","tofloatorsink":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: When you make a Martial skill (Water or Earth) check</li><li>Opportunities: Water or Earth (op)+: Remove one existing Disoriented or Prone condition from yourself. Water or Earth (op): Do not suffer the Disoriented and Prone conditions if the check would cause you to suffer them.</li></ul>","vanishintheshadows":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 3</li><li>Activation: As a downtime activity or once per scene as a Movement and Support action, you may make a TN 5 Survival (Air) check targeting your cohort or yourself and a number of characters up to your ranks in Command who are within Confining, Entangling, or Obscuring terrain. In urban environments use Skulduggery; on the ocean use Seafaring.</li><li>If you succeed, all targets become hidden and are not noticed by characters with vigilance lower than or equal to your Air Ring plus bonus successes. Hidden characters cannot be targeted by or perform Attack actions. Persists until end of your next turn, or until any target performs an Attack action.</li><li>Opportunities: Air (op)+ (Mass Battle): If you succeed, enemy army receives 1 panic per (op) spent. Air (op)+ (Other Scene): Each non-targeted character within the terrain receives 1 strife per (op) spent. Air (op)(op)(op): If you failed, increase the TN of Attack action checks targeting each of your targets by 2. Persists until any target performs an Attack action or leaves the terrain.</li></ul>","whatsyoursismine":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 2</li><li>Activation: As an Attack and Movement action using one readied weapon without Cumbersome</li><li>Check: TN 3 Martial Arts [Melee] (Fire) targeting one character at range 0-1</li><li>If you succeed, target suffers physical damage equal to weapon&#x27;s base damage. If you succeed and target is Dazed, you may steal one item from their person (GM approval). Stealing a readied weapon requires target to resist with TN 3 Fitness check.</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op): Target suffers Dazed condition. Fire (op)+: Move 1 range band plus one additional per (op)(op) beyond first. Fire (op)(op)+: Steal one additional item per (op)(op) spent this way.</li></ul>","wreakhavoc":"<ul><li>Type: Ninjutsu</li><li>Rank: 4</li><li>Activation: Once per game session as an Attack and Movement action during a mass battle, you may make a Skulduggery (Fire) check targeting one enemy leader&#x27;s cohort. TN equals that leader&#x27;s vigilance. You may expend 1 charge of blasting powder and forfeit honor equal to half your honor rank (rounded up) to reduce TN by 2 (minimum 1).</li><li>If you succeed, achieve one: reduce a fortification&#x27;s difficulty value by 4 plus bonus successes (destroying it if reduced to 0 or lower); remove Confining and Entangling terrain but add Dangerous and Obscuring; or remove one cohort ability from the target cohort. Additionally, the target leader must resist with TN 5 Command check (Air 6, Water 3) or their army suffers panic equal to your ranks in Performance plus their shortfall.</li><li>Opportunities: Fire (op): Target cohort&#x27;s leader suffers a critical strike with severity equal to 6 plus bonus successes. Fire (op)(op): Target cohort&#x27;s leader suffers Dazed. Fire (op)+: Expend additional charges of blasting powder up to (op) spent to add two bonus successes per charge expended.</li></ul>","counteringmantra":"<ul><li>Activation: When a character you can perceive makes a check to use a celestial implement, if you have a readied implement of your own, immediately make a TN 5 Theology check. If your implement&#x27;s element matches the counter element, TN is 2 instead.</li><li>If you succeed, target&#x27;s implement is dispelled. Target counts as having failed with shortfall equal to your ranks in Theology, and does not apply boons.</li></ul>","summoningmantra":"<ul><li>Activation: As a Support action, you may make a TN 4 Theology check to call forth one celestial implement. The ring of the check is determined by the divinity whose implement you are summoning.</li><li>If you succeed, you summon and augment one readied item that becomes the celestial implement. Then, you must stake honor equal to two times your honor rank on upholding the implement&#x27;s restriction while you have the implement (see page 99). The implement persists until the end of the scene or until it is dispelled, at which point the blessing ends. If you break the implement&#x27;s restriction during this time, you lose your staked honor and the implement is dispelled. You cannot summon this implement again this scene.</li></ul>","agrainoftruth":"<p>Once per scene after you succeed on a Social skill check, you may choose a kihō with a prerequisite up to your school rank (whether you know it or not). You gain the benefits of its Enhancement Effect as if you had successfully activated it. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</p>","akilahsteachings":"<p>Once per round after an Attack action check against you fails, if you have a shield readied and the attack is at range 0-1, you may shield bash. If you do, the target suffers physical damage equal to your ranks in Fitness plus your school rank.</p>","architectoftranquility":"<p>Once per scene after you succeed at an Artisan skill check, you may choose a number of characters in the scene equal to your school rank. Each chosen character removes 3 strife.</p>","badgershold":"<p>After you succeed at an Attack action check using the Martial Arts [Unarmed] skill, if the target is Immobilized or Prone, they also receive fatigue equal to your school rank.</p>","bendperception":"<p>When you choose this school, determine what illusion your character has perfected with your GM. You can seamlessly switch between your true form and this alternate form within seconds. You can still use your true form&#x27;s features such as your tail while in your alternate form. A character must make a TN 6 Theology or Survival (Void 5) check to see beyond your illusion. Additionally, increase the damage dealt by your tail by your school rank.</p>","blazingtearsofladysun":"<p>Damage inflicted by your Fire invocations is treated as having the Sacred item quality. Items you augment or summon with Fire invocations have the Sacred quality. When you affect a non-Tainted human with a Fire invocation, it does not deal damage or inflict negative conditions. Instead, the character removes fatigue equal to your school rank plus the damage you would have dealt. Each character can only benefit once per scene.</p>","blessingofthefortunes":"<p>You have gained the goodwill of a Fortune who grants you invocations. When making a check to use an invocation learned this way, add additional bonus successes equal to your school rank. Select a Fortune as the primary object of your veneration and choose one appropriate invocation for which you meet the rank prerequisite. You learn that invocation without paying its XP cost. Each time your school rank increases, you gain one additional invocation this way.</p>","bloodofthekami":"<p>You have one mystical tattoo that empowers your kihō, and gain more as your school rank increases. When you make a check to activate a kihō linked to one of your mystical tattoos, if you succeed, add additional bonus successes equal to your school rank. Select a natural motif for your first tattoo and choose one kihō for which you meet the prerequisites that are linked to the tattoo. If you have not learned it, you learn that kihō (without paying its XP cost). You cannot choose the same kihō multiple times this way. Each time your school rank increases, you gain one additional tattoo this way.</p>","borninthesaddle":"<p>Once per scene, before rolling dice, you may declare that you are directing your horse (who must be present) to aid in a task and describe how its efforts help in those circumstances. Reduce the TN of the check by your school rank.</p>","calmcounsel":"<p>After a friendly character at range 0-4 receives strife, you may impose the Centered condition on that character. You can use this ability a number of times per scene up to your school rank.</p>","celestialalignment":"<p>As a Support action, make a TN 2 Meditation (Void) check to draw one of the Spirit Realms closer to your location. A number of range bands around your position up to your school rank become a place of power of the realm you choose. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</p>","clawsofthecrab":"<p>When you make a check to perform the Guard action, you may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: If you succeed, you may guard one additional character in range per (op) spent this way. Maximum (op) equal to your school rank.</p>","creativeexecution":"<p>When making a check to perform a ritual, you may receive fatigue up to your school rank to add that many kept (ring) set to (op) results.</p>","disarmingdemeanor":"<p>When you perform a Support action check, you may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: Choose one character in the scene with vigilance lower than your school ranks plus (op) spent this way. You treat that character&#x27;s focus and vigilance each as 1 lower until end of scene.</p>","discipleofdarkness":"<p>When you perform a check to hide, move stealthily, or deceive others as to your true identity, you may suffer a number of strife up to your school rank to choose that many characters targeted by the check. Treat each chosen character&#x27;s vigilance as 1 lower while resolving the check.</p>","drilledprecision":"<p>When making an Attack or Movement action check, you may remove an amount of strife from yourself up to your school rank. For each strife you remove this way, add one kept (ring) set to (op) to the check and receive 1 fatigue.</p>","dunestrider":"<p>At start of each scene, choose one terrain quality: Dangerous, Entangling, Imbalanced, or Obscuring. Each friendly character within a number of range bands equal to your school rank ignores negative effects of that terrain quality.</p>","effortlessaim":"<p>When making a check using a bow, add a number of kept ring dice set to an Opportunity result equal to your school rank.</p>","elementalinspiration":"<p>Choose one: Air, Earth, Water, or Fire. This is your inspired element. When making a check to activate an invocation of your inspired element, add a number of rolled (ring) set to (op) results equal to your school rank. When making a check to activate an invocation of your inspired element, you trigger spiritual backlash only if you keep four or more dice containing (st) symbols (instead of three or more). When making a check to activate an invocation not of your inspired element, you trigger spiritual backlash if you keep two or more dice containing (st) symbols (instead of three or more).</p>","elementaltransmutation":"<p>When performing an invocation, you may choose a different ring with which to make the check. While using this school ability, you cannot activate (op) of the original Element of the invocation, but you can activate (op) for the new Element. You can use this school ability a number of times per game session up to your school rank.</p>","embracethevoid":"<p>When you spend a Void point to Seize the Moment, you may also treat your ranks in the skill you are using as being equal to your school rank. If your ranks in the skill are equal to or higher than your school rank, or if you have 5 ranks in the skill, you may add one kept (ring) set to an (op) result instead.</p>","everystoneserves":"<p>Reduce the TN of checks for downtime activities that alter your environment by your school rank (to a minimum of 1). When you succeed, choose mundane terrain qualities equal to your school rank and add or remove those terrain qualities from the area you affect.</p>","evolutionofthewilds":"<p>When you make a check to employ an unconventional solution (subject to GM discretion) reduce the TN of that check by your school rank.</p>","explosivearrival":"<p>After you perform an Attack action against a target who is Dazed or unaware of your presence, that target receives strife equal to your school rank. If your target is an enemy leader&#x27;s cohort in a mass battle, the enemy army also receives that much panic.</p>","eyeofthestorm":"<p>When an invocation technique you perform would affect &quot;each character&quot; or &quot;each other character&quot; at a specified range, you may exclude a number of characters up to your school rank from all effects of the invocation except for spiritual backlash (see page 190 of the core rulebook).</p>","eyesofyotogi":"<p>Otherworldly beings treat your vigilance as being increased by your school rank. When you make a check to search for Otherworldly beings, or make an Initiative check in a conflict against them, if you succeed, add bonus successes equal to your school rank.</p>","favoroftheancestors":"<p>Once per scene, you may importune one invocation (see Importune Invocations, on page 189) with a school rank prerequisite up to your school rank without making the sacrifices usually required and without the usual TN increase.</p>","fieldmedicine":"<p>When you perform a Medicine check to remove fatigue or a condition from a friendly character, that character removes additional fatigue up to your school rank.</p>","fleshoftheelements":"<p>You can have a number of additional potions with prepared invocations equal to your school rank. When you spend a downtime activity creating a potion, you may make supplemental checks after the first equal to your school rank, but each must be for a different invocation.</p>","flickeringflameskirmisher":"<p>After performing an Attack action, you may change your stance. If you do, increase the TN of Attack checks by creatures of silhouette 3 or larger targeting you by your school rank until the start of your next turn.</p>","flurryofsteel":"<p>Once per scene when performing an Attack action, you may choose a number of additional enemies up to your school rank in range of your weapon as targets for that Attack action.</p>","foxspirit":"<p>Your true form is that of a large fox with up to eight tails if you are a full-blooded kitsune, or a human with certain vulpine traits if you possess human ancestry as well. As a Scheme and Support action, you may transform between your human and true forms, or into another silhouette 1 or 2 natural creature at the GM’s discretion (you cannot mimic specific individuals). Observers with vigilance lower than or equal to your school rank plus your ranks in Performance do not detect any flaws in your façade. However, certain key features persist across all of your forms. If you become Compromised, your disguise slips, subtly revealing your true tails, ears, feet, or shadow.</p>","gazeintoshadow":"<p>Once per round, when you make a check targeting or involving a Tainted being, you may choose a number of your kept dice up to your school rank containing (st) symbols. Set each of these dice to a (su) result. You cannot use this ability if you are unsure if a being is Tainted or not.</p>","giftofinnerpower":"<p>After you perform a check to activate one of your kihō, you can receive fatigue up to your school rank and choose another character at range 0-1. If you do, that character gains the enhancement effect of your kihō in your stead (you may still resolve the burst effect, if able). This effect persists a number of rounds equal to the amount of fatigue you received plus your ranks in Meditation. Only one character can benefit from your kihō at a time.</p>","giftofmusubinokami":"<p>You may perform The Ties that Bind ritual as an action, instead of as a downtime activity. When you make a check to perform this ritual, you may add kept (ring) set to (op) results equal to your school rank.</p>","handsofearthandsky":"<p>When you perform an invocation that targets at least one other character, if you succeed, you may nourish or drain: Nourish: receive fatigue up to your school rank. One target removes fatigue equal to amount received. Drain: remove fatigue up to your school rank. One target receives fatigue equal to amount removed.</p>","heartofthelion":"<p>Once per scene, after you perform a check using a Social skill that targets one or more characters, you may agitate or console: If you agitate, transfer strife up to twice your school rank from yourself to your targets (divided among them as you choose). If you console, transfer strife up to twice your school rank from your targets (divided among them as you choose) to yourself.</p>","heroiccharge":"<ul><li>When you succeed at an Attack action check, add bonus successes equal to the number of range bands you have moved this round, to a maximum of your school rank.</li><li>During a duel or mass battle, if you are mounted on your steed, you always count as having moved a number of range bands equal to your school rank this turn.</li></ul>","hideofiron":"<p>Once per game session when you make a check to craft, improve, or maintain a weapon or set of armor, you may receive an amount of fatigue up to your school rank to reroll that many dice.</p>","incisiveinsight":"<p>Once per scene, when making a check for a Scheme action targeting another character, you may receive a number of strife up to your school rank to reduce the TN by that amount (to a minimum of 1).</p>","justaspredicted":"<p>At the beginning of a game session or as a downtime activity, make a TN 1 Theology check using any ring. If you succeed, choose a number of kept dice up to your school rank to reserve. Until end of session or next downtime scene, when any character makes a skill check using the chosen ring, you may replace one or more kept dice with the same number of reserved dice of the same type.</p>","keensenses":"<p>When you make a check to perceive or investigate your surroundings, decrease the TN of that check by a number equal to your school rank (to a minimum of 1).</p>","kitsukismethod":"<p>When performing a check to investigate with any skill (see The Art of Investigation, on page 170), you may treat your ranks in the skill you are using as being equal to your school rank. If your ranks in the skill are equal to or higher than your school rank, or if you have 5 ranks in the skill, you may add a kept (ring) set to an (op) result instead.</p>","laughtermakesthehome":"<p>The first time you make a successful Social check against another character in a scene, you may reduce the TN of all subsequent Social checks against that character by 1 (to a minimum of 1) for the remainder of the scene. This effect does not stack with itself, but can be used on multiple characters.</p>","masterfulbuilder":"<p>Once per scene, when making a check to use an item you personally crafted, you may add a number of kept (ring) set to (op) results equal to your school rank.</p>","matsusfury":"<p>After you suffer a critical strike or unmask, you may suffer the Enraged condition to remove an amount of fatigue from yourself equal to your school rank.</p>","maythespiritsshowthepath":"<p>Once per scene if you would fail a Social check, you may immediately make a TN 5 Theology check, with the TN being reduced by a number equal to your school rank (to a minimum of 1). If you succeed, you may change any kept (ring) on that Social check to (su) results instead.</p>","mazokusauthority":"<p>When you perform an Attack or Scheme action check targeting an Otherworldly being, if you succeed, add a number of bonus successes equal to your school rank.</p>","methodicalobservation":"<p>Once per scene when you make a Scholar skill check, you may reserve a number of dropped dice up to your school rank. Until end of scene, when you make a non- Scholar skill check, after choosing dice, you may add up to one reserved die as a kept die.</p>","mindofcalm":"<p>Once per scene you may make a TN 6 Meditation check to study someone else&#x27;s technique of a category and rank you have available to you. This check is reduced by your school rank, to a minimum of 1. If you succeed, you can replicate that technique until the end of the scene.</p>","momentofcertainty":"<p>Once per scene after you defend against damage, you may roll a number of skill dice equal to the fatigue you received this way. Choose a number of those dice up to your school rank and reserve them. Until end of scene, when you perform an Attack action check, after choosing kept dice, you may add one reserved die as an additional kept die.</p>","moveasthewind":"<p>When you make a Movement action check or check to travel at speed in narrative time, if you succeed, you may suffer up to 2 fatigue to add that many bonus successes. After you remove fatigue at end of scene, you may remove additional fatigue up to your school rank.</p>","mysticalscript":"<p>You can have a number of additional wards with prepared invocations (see page 190) up to your school rank. Decoding or using one of your wards requires any other character to make a Theology (Void) check with TN equal to your school rank.</p>","naturalbalance":"<p>When you succeed on a check to activate an invocation, if it is the first invocation of that element you have activated this scene, you may add bonus successes or kept dice set to (op) equal to your school rank.</p>","naturallyattuned":"<p>As a downtime activity, you may select any number of invocations with total school rank prerequisites equal to double your school rank. You can perform these invocations as if you knew them. While making a check to activate an invocation, if you become Compromised, you suffer spiritual backlash.</p>","necessaryactions":"<p>You never forfeit honor or glory in order to lie or deceive for the good of the Emperor and Empire (in your opinion). However, you must forfeit twice as much honor or glory to lie for your personal gain (again, in your opinion). When a character stakes or forfeits an amount of honor or glory in order to act against your desires, you may force them to increase that amount by your school rank.</p>","oathofsacrifice":"<p>Once per scene, after you defend against damage or suffer a critical strike, you may unleash your current kihō. Immediately end its enhancement effect, then resolve its burst effect as if you had a number of bonus successes equal to your school rank plus the amount of fatigue you received or the severity of the critical strike you suffered. If the burst effect has one or more targets, you may choose appropriate targets in range. If you have used this ability already this scene, you may spend 1 Void point to use it again this scene (you can do this any number of times, provided you have Void points to spend).</p>","onewiththeelements":"<p>Once per scene when making the check to activate an invocation technique, before rolling dice, you may reduce the TN of the check by your school rank.</p>","onewiththepride":"<p>Increase each of your bonded animals&#x27; endurance, composure, and ranks in Martial skill group by an amount equal to your school rank (its skill ranks still cannot exceed 5). If a bonded animal is a minion, it becomes an adversary instead.</p>","piercinginsight":"<p>Once per round, in a skirmish, when you inflict a critical strike on a character at range 2-5 or a character at range 2-5 inflicts a critical strike on you, you may increase or decrease the severity by your school rank.</p>","procedureandprotocol":"<p>When you cause a character to receive strife as a result of a check using a social approach, that character suffers additional strife equal to your school rank.</p>","professionalsaboteur":"<p>Once per game session at the beginning of a scene, you may reveal that an NPC in that scene is the target of your current assignment. The GM then decides what your assignment entails, such as sabotaging the target’s current activities, framing them for a crime, killing them, or even making sure they survive to play their part in a long and sinister plot. Until the end of the session, when you make a skill check targeting the chosen NPC, you may reroll a number of dice up to your school rank.</p>","resourcefulartistry":"<p>Once per game session when performing a downtime activity to craft, you may scavenge supplies for your craft worth an amount of koku equal to your school rank.</p>","riskandreward":"<p>You have an uncanny sense for dangerous situations. Your vigilance and focus are increased by your school rank, unless you are Compromised.</p>","sacredarrows":"<p>As an action, you may augment one of your arrows with a prayer to the kami. Make the check to perform one invocation you know, reducing the TN by your school rank, and record the result. The arrow gains the Sacred quality, and remains infused with the invocation until the end of the scene. After you perform an Attack action using the arrow (or fire it at a location, at the GM&#x27;s discretion), you may resolve the effects of the invocation from the place the arrow landed. You may spend (op)+ to delay resolving the effects of the invocation for 1 round per (op) spent this way, and may spend (op) (op) from a failed check to affect one target of the attack that you missed.</p>","sacredartofsteel":"<p>Once per game session when you make a check to craft, improve, or maintain a weapon, you may add a number of kept (ring) set to (op) results equal to your school rank.</p>","sailorsfortune":"<p>Once per round when making a Trade skill check, if you are not Compromised, you may receive a number of strife up to your school rank to reroll that many rolled dice.</p>","schoolofwaves":"<ul><li>Choose one bonus curriculum skill; this skill henceforth counts as part of the Worldly Rōnin Path curriculum for you at all ranks. Each time your school rank increases, choose one additional bonus curriculum skill this way.</li><li>When you make a check using one of your bonus curriculum skills, you may negate 1 (st) symbol.</li></ul>","seerofthelordsofdeath":"<p>You can channel rituals in the same way as invocations. Once per scene, when you channel you may receive fatigue up to your school rank. If you do, you may immediately make another check to perform an invocation of the same element using the reserved dice from your channel. For each fatigue received this way, you may add one kept die set to an (op) result.</p>","sharpenedki":"<p>Your kihō that affect your unarmed attack profiles also apply to weapons you wield in a one-handed grip. When you succeed on a check to activate a kihō that affects your unarmed attack profiles or a weapon you wield in a one-handed grip, add bonus successes equal to your school rank.</p>","signatureweapon":"<p>Choose a signature weapon category (or unarmed) with GM approval. When using a weapon from this category for an Attack action or Performance check, roll one additional skill die. Additionally, when making such a check you may suffer fatigue up to your school rank to alter that many results of your kept dice to (op) results.</p>","soulofceremony":"<p>When you make a check to perform a ritual, you may add kept ring dice set to opportunity results equal to your school rank. You may spend these opportunity as if the ritual were also a Social skill check of your choice.</p>","speakinginsilence":"<p>Once per scene when making a check to persuade or influence someone, you may add a number of kept (ring) set to a (op) results equal to your school rank.</p>","speedofheaven":"<p>When you succeed on an Initiative check during a skirmish or duel, add bonus successes equal to your school rank.</p>","spiritualartisan":"<p>When making a check to mystically summon an illusion or to summon, augment, or awaken an object, you may add a number of kept (ring) set to (op) results equal to your school rank.</p>","standasthemountain":"<p>After you channel an invocation, increase your physical and supernatural resistances by an amount equal to the number of dice you reserved, to a maximum of your school rank. This effect persists until the start of your next turn.</p>","steedofthekami":"<p>When you make a check to handle, calm, or instruct an animal, negate strife results up to your school rank. Once per scene as a Support action, make a TN 2 Survival (Water) or Theology (Water) check. If you succeed, discover a ridable animal of combat rank 3 or lower appropriate to the environment. It is friendly and grants mount benefits, with Water Ring increased by bonus successes (max 6).</p>","suddennightfall":"<p>You do not suffer ill effects of Obscuring terrain from darkness. When you perform an Attack or Scheme action against a target in darkness-Obscuring terrain, reduce the TN by your school rank (minimum 1). As a Support action, summon supernatural darkness at range 0-2; area extending Air Ring range bands becomes Obscuring, persisting a number of rounds equal to school rank.</p>","suppressingblows":"<p>When you perform an Attack action check using Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Unarmed], you may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: One character per (op) spent this way who is in range of the weapon you used suffers the Silenced condition. Maximum (op) equal to your school rank.</p>","swirlingdesertwind":"<ul><li>When performing an Attack action during a skirmish or mass battle, you may spend (op) as follows:</li><li>(op): Choose an enemy other than your target whom you can perceive. Increase the TN of that enemy&#x27;s Attack checks targeting you by your school rank until the start of your next turn.</li></ul>","sympatheticbearing":"<p>After you make a check for Initiative (or enter the scene, for a narrative scene), you may choose another character in the scene. That character removes strife equal to your school rank, and you reduce the TN of your next Social skill check targeting that character by 2.</p>","tacticalcover":"<p>While you are in Obscuring terrain, you may treat your physical resistance as increased by your school rank.</p>","thebodyisashrine":"<p>In the presence of a kami, make a TN 4 Courtesy check using the kami&#x27;s element. If you succeed, the kami uses your body as a vessel: reroll dice up to school rank on checks using its element, but increase TN by 1 and add kept ring set to opportunity+strife on opposing element checks. If you unmask, the kami is released.</p>","thehorselordsfavor":"<p>When you make a check to craft, improve, or maintain an item, you may imprint it with the Horse Lord&#x27;s Favor, giving it one of your advantages or disadvantages. If the item is a meishōdō talisman, you may give it an advantage or disadvantage from its sealed spirit. While an item with your Favor adorns a horse or Loyal Steed creature, the creature is Otherworldly and possesses the chosen trait. If a meishōdō talisman, the creature may perform any techniques it contains. Sustain up to school rank items. Additionally, Medicine checks to remove fatigue or conditions from equine creatures add bonus successes equal to school rank.</p>","thekamiswhisper":"<p>While you are performing an invocation technique or channeling, characters with a vigilance lower than or equal to your school rank plus one cannot detect any physical sign that you are in the act of invoking the spirits. They can still observe effects of the invocation, however. Increase the TN of Theology checks to detect or study your supernatural activities by your school rank.</p>","thepathofshadows":"<p>While performing an Attack action against a target who is Compromised, Incapacitated, Unconscious, or unaware of your presence, treat the damage and deadliness of your weapon as being increased by your school rank.</p>","thewayofnames":"<ul><li>As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 2 Design check using any ring to bind a spirit to an inanimate vessel, creating a meishōdō talisman for one invocation of that Element that you have learned. While you have the talisman in your possession, reduce the TN of checks to activate that invocation by 1. You can give the talisman to another shugenja, allowing them to perform that invocation even if they have not learned it and reducing the TN to activate it by 1, but the talisman ceases to function after a number of uses equal to your school rank.</li><li>You can sustain a number of meishōdō talismans up to your school rank. You can only have one meishōdō talisman for any single invocation.</li></ul>","thunderouscourage":"<p>Once per scene after you perform a Support action, you may choose any number of characters within a number of range bands equal to your ranks in Command. Each chosen character treats their composure as increased by your school rank. This effect persists until the end of the scene. During a mass battle, if you are a leader, your army treats its discipline as increased by your school rank.</p>","tracesofpassage":"<p>Once per scene as a Support action, you may scry to detect any supernatural abilities used at range 0-3 in the last day (such as invocations, mahō, and kihō). Reduce the TN of your checks to investigate this phenomenon by your school rank.</p>","typhooninthebamboogrove":"<p>When making a Martial Arts [Melee] or Fitness check, you may spend (op)(op) to cause a number of characters no greater than your school rank and within range of your readied weapon to suffer the Dazed condition.</p>","unexpectedwisdom":"<p>You may dispense wisdom a number of times per game session equal to your school rank. On your turn or at any appropriate time during a narrative scene, you may give a small bit of wisdom to a character who can hear you and has not benefitted from this ability this scene. The next time that character employs that wisdom they may reduce the TN of that check by 1 and may negate a number of strife up to your ranks in Sentiment or Theology.</p>","unityofhorseandrider":"<p>When you spend Void to seize the moment during a check using a bow, you may negate (st) symbols up to your school rank. If you succeed, gain bonus successes equal to the number of (st) negated. While riding your steed, all Martial Arts [Ranged] and Performance checks have unskilled assistance.</p>","vendorofstrangewares":"<ul><li>Ignore the Forbidden quality when acquiring and handling items.</li><li>When acquiring, selling, or gifting an item, you may treat its rarity as reduced or increased by your school rank.</li></ul>","victorybeforehonor":"<p>Once per scene when performing a check, you may stake an amount of honor no greater than your school rank to re-roll a number of dice equal to twice the amount of honor staked. For each re-rolled die result that does not contain a (su) or (ex), you forfeit one staked honor.</p>","vigilanceofmind":"<p>Once per round, when another character within range of one of your readied melee weapons would suffer physical damage, you may intercept. If you do, you may suffer fatigue up to your school rank to reduce the damage the target suffers by twice that amount.</p>","voiceoftheemperor":"<p>Once per round, after a character at range 0-4 succeeds on an Attack or Scheme action check, you may cause them to receive strife equal to your school rank.</p>","wardedshikigami":"<p>You can have a number of additional shikigami (see page 115) up to your school rank. Once per scene, after you perform an action, you may instruct one of your shikigami to perform an action, for which it benefits from your assistance.</p>","wardenofthefivewinds":"<p>When you make a check to perform the Guard action, you gain a bonus success if you or your target is mounted on a steed. When you succeed on a Guard action check, you may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: Give a target at range 0-3 the Emboldened condition. Maximum (op) spent this way up to your school rank.</p>","wayofthecarp":"<p>As a downtime activity, if you have access to a market, you may acquire a number of items up to your school rank of rarity 4 or lower, or a single item of up to rarity 4 plus your school rank. You do not need to make a check or expend money to acquire these items, nor do you need to forfeit or stake honor or glory for the act of acquiring them, even if they are not befitting of your station or Forbidden (though displaying them openly later is a different matter). The GM can still apply rarity adjustments as usual based on the specifics of the market available.</p>","wayofthecrab":"<ul><li>Ignore the Cumbersome quality of armor you wear.</li><li>Once per round, before making a check to resist a critical strike, you may reduce the severity of that critical strike by the physical resistance of your armor plus your school rank (to a minimum of 0).</li></ul>","wayofthecrane":"<p>Once per round, you may increase or decrease the severity of a critical strike you inflict by an amount up to your school rank.</p>","wayofthedragon":"<p>Once per round during a duel or skirmish when you are targeted by an Attack check with a melee weapon, you may use one of your weapons readied in a one-handed grip (or one of your hands, if it is empty) to ward or trap. If you ward, the attacker must reroll dice containing (su) or (ex) up to your school rank. If you trap, reduce the TN of your next Attack check against the attacker this scene by your school rank (to a minimum of 1). You cannot choose this weapon for Attack actions until the end of your next turn.</p>","wayofthelion":"<p>When you succeed at an Attack or Support action check, you may remove an amount of strife from yourself up to your school rank. For each strife you remove this way, add that one bonus success to the check and receive 1 fatigue.</p>","wayofthephoenix":"<p>Once per scene, when a character at range 0-3 makes a check that contains 1 or more (st) symbols, you may negate all of those (st) symbols. Then, that character removes strife and fatigue equal to your school rank.</p>","wayofthescorpion":"<p>When you exploit a target&#x27;s disadvantage as part of an Initiative check for a duel or an Attack action, you do not need to spend a Void point, and you may reroll additional dice up to your school rank.</p>","wayofthetortoise":"<ul><li>You never need to stake glory to publicly use a Trade skill, so long as you are doing so as part of your duty to your clan.</li><li>Once per scene, you may add a number of kept ring dice set to Opportunity results equal to your school rank to a check to interact with one or more gaijin, peasants, merchants, burakumin, or any other character with status of 20 or lower.</li></ul>","wayofthevoid":"<p>When you make a check using your Void Ring, after rolling dice, you may receive fatigue up to your school rank. If you push, choose that many blank dice and alter each to a non-blank result of your choice. If you pull, choose that many non-blank dice and alter each to blank.</p>","weaknessismystrength":"<p>When you exploit a target&#x27;s disadvantage (see Turning Advantages and Disadvantages, page 100) as part of a Scheme action, you do not need to spend a Void point, and you may reroll additional dice up to your school rank.</p>","welltraveled":"<p>You always know which way is north, and you are always able to find a landmark useful for navigation. When making a check to recall or ascertain geographical, political, or societal information, you may add a number of kept (ring) set to (op) or (su) results equal to your school rank.</p>","wisdomoftheages":"<p>When performing a Scholar skill check, you may treat your ranks in the skill as being equal to your school rank. If your ranks in that Scholar skill are equal to or higher than your school rank, or if you have 5 ranks in the skill, you may add one kept (ring) set to an (op) result instead.</p>","abottomlessocean":"<p>You can increase your bonus curriculum skills to rank 6 (paying 12 XP per skill raised from rank 5 to rank 6 this way).</p>","afriendineverycity":"<p>As a downtime activity in any place of human habitation, you may make a TN 4 Commerce (Water) check to find a merchant with whom you (or your relatives) have done business. If you succeed, you find this individual and gain the Ally advantage for them (see page 101), which predisposes them to assist you in various ways.</p>","agiftoffate":"<p>Once per game session on your turn, you may choose one ritual for which you meet the prerequisites (does not need to be purchased). You may immediately perform that ritual as a single action instead of a downtime activity.</p>","amasterofstudy":"<p>Choose one technique category your school does not already have available to it. That technique type is now available to you.</p>","akodosfinallesson":"<p>Once per game session during a skirmish or mass battle, after you fail a check, you may attempt the check again, treating the TN as 1.</p>","allpartoftheplan":"<p>Once per scene when you make a check to resist, you may spend 1 Void Point to automatically succeed. If you do, you may immediately perform an action.</p>","anarrowloosed":"<p>Once per game session, before making a check with a bow, you may declare your confidence in a shot and stake up to 6 glory upon hitting your mark. Reduce the TN of the check by that amount. If you succeed, you recover your staked glory. If succeeding in the shot would cause you to receive a glory award (such as if you were competing with another skilled archer, or felled a dangerous beast on the hunt), you receive that amount of glory plus 3 instead. If you fail, you lose your staked glory.</p>","ashidakasmethod":"<p>When you create a new weapon, you may apply two different patterns that you know to it (instead of one).</p>","attunedinvocation":"<p>Once per scene, when making a check to activate an invocation of your inspired element, you may spend 1 Void point. If you do, you may keep any number of your rolled dice (instead of a number up to your ring value).</p>","blessingsoftheemperor":"<p>Once per scene as a Scheme action, you may make a TN 4 Command (Air) check targeting a number of characters in the scene up to your glory rank. If you succeed, until the end of the scene, the targets must forfeit honor equal to twice their honor rank and glory equal to twice their glory rank before choosing you as the target of an Attack action, and increase the TN of their Attack actions targeting you by 2. This effect persists until the end of the scene, or until you attack an affected character or their allies. (op)+: Choose one ally per (op) spent this way. The effects of this ability also apply to targets’ attacks against the chosen allies.</p>","bloodofthedragon":"<p>Once per scene, while you are benefiting from the enhancement effect of a kihō linked to one of your tattoos, when you activate a different kihō, you may spend 1 Void point. If you do, you may maintain both enhancement effects until the end of the scene or until you activate another kihō.</p>","borntosurvive":"<p>Once per scene when you would suffer an amount of damage that would cause you to exceed your endurance threshold, you may instead suffer that amount of strife instead.</p>","boundinink":"<p>Once per scene, when you are targeted by an invocation or mahō technique, you may resist with a TN 4 Composition check. If you succeed, you absorb the invocation or mahō, nullifying all of its effects and creating a ward containing it (see page 190).</p>","coolheadsprevail":"<p>Friendly Centered characters at range 0-4 from you treat their composure and endurance as increased by your ranks in Courtesy.</p>","cracknotasingletwig":"<p>At the start of a scene, you may choose any number of mundane terrain effects. You ignore the effects of these terrain qualities. (Other characters do not ignore them when making checks against you.) This effect persists until the end of the scene.</p>","curseofmusubinokami":"<p>Once per scene, after successfully performing The Ties that Bind ritual, you may spend 1 Void point to catch a glimpse of all major future consequences of the identified relationship. You also learn of one other relationship between your target and another character that will guarantee the predicted consequences will not come to pass.</p>","demonbegone":"<p>As an action, you may make a TN 3 Meditation (Void) check by plucking the string of a bow you are wielding, targeting each Otherworldly being within a number of range bands equal to your ranks in Meditation. If you succeed, each target suffers strife equal to your ranks in Meditation plus your bonus successes. (op): Each target must resist with a TN 3 Meditation (Void) check or treat its physical and supernatural resistances as 0. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</p>","divineprotection":"<p>You can perform the Threshold Barrier ritual as an action. When a Tainted being enters an area you have warded against it with this ritual, it suffers supernatural damage equal to your ranks in Meditation and the Prone condition.</p>","echoesofancientdays":"<p>When you use your school ability, you may choose a number of characters up to your ranks in Performance who can hear you. Each chosen character also gains the benefits of the kihō&#x27;s enhancement effect as long as it persists on you.</p>","elementalcharmer":"<p>You may importune invocations without making an offering.</p>","emeraldexplorer":"<p>Once per scene as a Support action, you may make a TN 1 Survival (Earth) check targeting one character in the scene. If you succeed on the check, that character and an additional number of characters you choose equal to your bonus successes ignore all negative effects of terrain qualities until the end of the scene.</p>","empathictransfer":"<p>When you nourish, you may remove one condition the target is suffering by transferring it to yourself. When you drain, you may remove one condition you are suffering by transferring it to one of your targets.</p>","emptysoulki":"<p>When you defend against damage, if all your Void Points are spent, treat your physical and supernatural resistances as being equal to your Void ring.</p>","essenceofemptiness":"<p>Once per scene, after a character rolls dice, you may receive 3 fatigue to alter any number of their rolled dice to blank results.</p>","experimentandadapt":"<p>Increase your supernatural resistance against Air, Earth, Fire, and Water invocations by your ranks in Theology. After another character performs an Air, Earth, Fire, or Water invocation targeting you, you may spend 1 Void Point to immediately perform that invocation, even if you have not learned it.</p>","favorofthefortunes":"<p>Once per scene, you may importune one invocation without making the sacrifices usually required and without the usual TN increase. Use the Meditation skill in place of the skill check normally required (you must still use the ring required for the invocation).</p>","favoredcounselor":"<p>When making a check to perform a ritual, you may spend opportunity as follows: (op)+: One participant in the ritual with vigilance lower than or equal to opportunity spent this way feels especially indebted to you. You gain the Ally [that character] advantage.</p>","foreseeninthestars":"<p>Once per game session, spend 1 Void point to reveal you have foreseen an event in the current scene. Retroactively declare one or more preparations you have taken, subject to GM approval. If preparations require a skill check, make it when you use this ability.</p>","fortitudeofthecradle":"<p>You may shield bash after you defend against damage, even if the check was successful. After you shield bash, your target must resist with a TN 4 Fitness (Air 3, Water 5) check or suffer the Disoriented and Prone conditions.</p>","healershands":"<p>When you make a check to remove a condition from another character, you may receive 2 fatigue to treat the TN as 1.</p>","heartofthedragon":"<p>Once per round, when performing an Attack action check, you may spend (op) as follows: (op): Perform a Strike action with a readied weapon you have not used for an Attack action this turn.</p>","hunterofthesupernatural":"<p>When making a check targeting an Otherworldly being, you may seize one of its advantages (see page 101 of the core rulebook) by receiving 2 fatigue instead of spending 1 Void point. If you do, your target receives strife equal to your ranks in Command.</p>","iwillalwaysreturn":"<p>Once per game session, you may call out for your steed. At the beginning of the following round, your horse arrives, regardless of any barriers that might normally have prevented it from reaching your location. If your steed has recently been slain, its spirit will possess the closest horse to you and come to your aid regardless, such is its loyalty to you.</p>","ingeniousdesign":"<p>When you construct an item, you may add or remove one quality from the item. You must describe to the GM how the item possesses (or lacks) the usual quality, and the GM is the final arbiter of whether an addition (or subtraction) is appropriate.</p>","insufferablegenius":"<p>After you succeed at a check to acquire or remember information, you may spend 1 Void point and choose any number of characters with whom you can communicate. You must describe how the knowledge you acquired helps each character you choose. Each of those characters reduces the TN of their next check by 1 (to a minimum of 1) and suffers 1 strife.</p>","killinggrip":"<p>When you inflict a critical strike on a target, if the target is Immobilized or Prone, you may receive 3 fatigue to increase the severity of the critical strike by two times your ranks in Fitness.</p>","kingdomofpaperandink":"<p>When one of your shikigami performs an action, it may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: Another one of your shikigami at range 0-3 of you may perform an action. Increase the (op) cost of this ability by (op) for each of your shikigami that has acted this turn.</p>","layoftheland":"<p>Once per game session as a Support action or during a narrative scene, you may change which terrain quality your school ability affects. While in terrain with the chosen quality, you may add up to two bonus successes to each check you make.</p>","legendaryendurance":"<p>Increase your endurance by your ranks in Survival. While riding a mount, increase the mount&#x27;s endurance by your ranks in Survival.</p>","lessonofthehawk":"<p>Once per scene, when performing an Attack action check, you may spend 1 Void Point to have your target treat their physical resistance as 0.</p>","lionspride":"<p>Once per game session as a Support action, you may attempt to convince everyone in the scene of the glorious reputation of one character, embellishing the truth as needed, by making a TN 5 Performance (Fire) check targeting one character. The TN of this check is 6 if you target yourself, and 4 if you target another Lion Clan character. If you succeed, reduce the TN of all of the character&#x27;s Social skill checks by 3 until the end of the scene, and the TN of all of the character&#x27;s other checks by 1.</p>","littletruths":"<p>When you perform a check targeting another character to which one of your advantages or disadvantages applies, you may choose another advantage or disadvantage that shares a type with it (see Advantages and Disadvantages, on page 99). Unless they have clear evidence to the contrary, the target comes to believe that you have the advantage or disadvantage you chose instead of the one you actually have. If the target attempts to seize or exploit this false advantage or disadvantage (see page 101), their check automatically counts as failing with a shortfall of 3. They suffer 3 strife and the Disoriented condition.</p>","logicalconclusion":"<p>Once per game session when making a non-Scholar skill check, instead of rolling skill dice equal to your ranks in the skill used, you may roll skill dice equal to one of your Scholar skills of your choice.</p>","majestyofthethrone":"<p>Once per scene, as a Scheme action, you may make a Command (Water) check targeting any number of characters at range 0–5 of you. The TN of this check is equal to the highest status rank among your targets. If you succeed, all targets suffer the Dazed and Disoriented conditions.</p>","masterofbeasts":"<p>Once per game as a Support action, summon a number of animals equal to your Water Ring that are combat rank 3 or lower. They are friendly and fulfill your commands until end of scene. If an animal becomes Compromised or incapacitated, it flees.</p>","masterofelements":"<p>Once per round, after you perform an invocation, you may spend 1 Void point to switch to any other stance and perform another invocation that shares no action types with the first invocation (Attack, Support, etc.).</p>","measuredforce":"<p>When you use your school ability to add kept dice to a check, you may add a number of your reserved dice up to your ranks in Fitness (instead of only one).</p>","ninthtailascension":"<p>Your true form now has nine tails. While you are in your true form, your supernatural resistance and physical resistance each increase by 2, and when you make a skill check, you may alter the result of one die containing (op) to a result containing (st). While you are in your true form, your Attack action checks gain the following new opportunity: (op)(op): After resolving this action, if your target is Incapacitated or Unconscious, you devour or banish their body or soul, instantly killing them.</p>","onewiththeshadows":"<p>When you perform a Ninjutsu technique, you may add two kept (ring) set to an (op) result to your check. You may do this 3 times per session.</p>","onewiththevoid":"<p>Once per scene, you may use one kihō technique you do not know. You may use the Meditation skill in place of the skill check normally required (you must still use the ring required for the kihō).</p>","postfacto":"<p>Once per game session as a Scheme and Support action, you may make a TN 3 Government (Earth) check. If you succeed, you reveal a huge legal loophole or arcane precedent that legally justifies the actions of you and your allies during the scene. Others can refuse to accept your logic, but must forfeit honor equal to your ranks in Government plus your bonus successes to do so.</p>","processionofseasons":"<p>After you resolve the effects of an invocation, if you have successfully activated at least one Air, one Earth, one Fire, and one Water invocation during this scene, you may have a number of characters up to your ranks in Survival each remove half their strife and fatigue (rounded up). Once per scene.</p>","purgethewicked":"<p>Once per game session, you may spend 1 Void point to wield an invocation against all the wicked in your sight. Instead of affecting its usual targets, the next invocation technique you perform targets each Tainted being in range.</p>","reflexivestrike":"<p>During a skirmish, if an opponent within range 0-1 of you attempts to move away from you, you may spend 1 Void point to immediately make two Strike actions against that opponent. Each action is resolved separately.</p>","rendingjawsofthelion":"<p>Once per round, when performing an Attack action check while Enraged, you may spend 1 Void point to alter each kept die containing (su) to a result containing (ex).</p>","reputationsentinel":"<p>You may use the Guard action during intrigues. When you do, increase the TN of Scheme action checks against the guarded target by 1, plus an additional 1 per two bonus successes.</p>","resilientreadiness":"<p>When you make a check to investigate a supernatural phenomenon, you may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: Increase your resistance against that phenomenon (such as a specific invocation, kihō, mahō, or NPC ability) by an amount equal to the (op) you spend this way. This effect persists until the end of the scene.</p>","ripplingflame":"<p>While performing a Fire invocation, you may spend a Void point to target additional characters equal to your ranks in Theology or to increase the maximum range of the technique by 1 range band.</p>","sacredfist":"<p>All of your kihō gain the following additional burst effect: If you have 3 or more bonus successes, your unarmed attack profiles gain the Sacred quality until the end of your next turn.</p>","scaledhide":"<p>When you defend against damage, you may treat your physical resistance and supernatural resistance as equal to your ranks in Fitness.</p>","scouringsirocco":"<p>Once per round, after you inflict the Incapacitated condition on a target (or defeat a minion NPC), you may perform a Strike action against a different target.</p>","sensingthebreeze":"<p>Once per round, after you defend against damage, you may move 1 range band and you may switch to a different stance.</p>","shadowassassin":"<p>Once per scene as an Attack and Movement action, summon a shadow assassin with no corporeal form that cannot be harmed. At the end of each of your turns, perform a Strike action using a readied weapon targeting any character in Obscuring terrain regardless of range. Damage dealt is supernatural. Persists until end of scene.</p>","shellofthetortoise":"<p>Once per game session as an action, you may invoke the shell of the Tortoise: the Emperor&#x27;s remit to operate as you deem necessary. Until the end of the scene, treat your status as 90, and other characters must forfeit honor and glory equal to the difference between your status rank and their status rank to accuse you of wrongdoing related to the acquisition or transport of goods, illicit or otherwise.</p>","slayersslash":"<p>Increase the severity of critical strikes you inflict on targets of silhouette 3 or larger by your ranks in Survival.</p>","smilingmountaintradition":"<p>You may train Social skills up to rank 6 (paying 12 XP per skill raised from rank 5 to rank 6 in this way).</p>","soulofdeepeststones":"<p>When you successfully make a check to augment or mend a target, add a number of bonus successes equal to your ranks in Fitness.</p>","spiritofthesacredhorse":"<p>Any steed you ride gains +4 endurance, +2 composure, +1 vigilance, and the Resplendent item quality. When you spend 1 or more Void points during a Martial Arts [Ranged] or Performance check, an item you have equipped gains the Sacred and Hewing item qualities, and you add kept dice set to (op) results equal to your Void ring.</p>","spreadingchaos":"<p>After you use your school ability during a duel or skirmish, your target and each other character friendly to them at range 0-3 suffers the Dazed condition. After you use your school ability in a mass battle, the leader of the cohort you targeted suffers the Dazed condition.</p>","spynetwork":"<p>As a downtime activity in any place of human habitation, you may make a TN 4 Skulduggery check to find an agent of the Daidoji spy network. If you succeed, you find this individual among the inhabitants and gain the Ally advantage for them. If you succeed with 2 or more bonus successes, the individual may occupy a low-to-mid-level position in a household or organization of your choosing.</p>","standofhonor":"<p>At the end of your turn, you may spend 1 Void point to prepare to fend off advancing foes; this effect persists until the start of your next turn. When an enemy enters the range of one of your readied weapons, you may immediately make a Strike action using that weapon and targeting that enemy; if you succeed, the target suffers the Immobilized condition in addition to any other effects.</p>","stirtheslumberingspirit":"<p>Once per game session as a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Artisan (Void) check to awaken an item&#x27;s spirit. If you succeed, until the end of the game session, it becomes a nemuranai (see page 307) with a sealed invocation of your choice based on the item&#x27;s history. The GM is the final arbiter of the appropriateness of any invocation selected this way.</p>","storiesastallasthemountain":"<p>Once per scene as a Scheme action you may make a TN 4 Performance (Air or Earth) check targeting a number of minion NPCs up to your ranks in Performance. If you succeed, each target decides that their actions really are unwise and leaves the scene, if able.</p>","stormlordsgambit":"<p>You may receive 1 additional strife to use your Sailor&#x27;s Fortune ability on any check instead of only a Trade skill check.</p>","stormsurge":"<p>When you perform an invocation that smites one or more targets, treat each target&#x27;s supernatural resistance as 1 lower per kept (st) symbol on the check.</p>","strengthofathousandancestors":"<p>Once per game session, as a Support action, you may summon the spirit of an ancestor to possess you until the end of the scene. While possessed, you count as an Otherworldly being and use the profile of the ancestor (a non-specific human NPC profile such as the Venerable Provincial Daimyō on page 315, or, at the GM&#x27;s discretion, a PC with up to 180 XP that you have created in advance). Your character does not remember any time they spend possessed.</p>","strikefirststrikelast":"<p>When you inflict a critical strike during a duel or skirmish, treat the deadliness of your weapon as increased by the difference between your initiative and your target&#x27;s initiative (subtracting the lower from the higher).</p>","strikewithnothought":"<p>Once per scene, as an Attack and Movement action, you may make a Martial Arts [Melee] (Void) check targeting one character at range 2-3 using a sheathed katana or wakizashi. The TN of this check is equal to your target&#x27;s vigilance. You immediately move to range 1 of your target and draw the weapon you used. If you succeed, your target suffers a critical strike with severity equal to the deadliness of your weapon plus your bonus successes. (op)+: One character of your choice at range 0-2 of your target per (op) spent this way suffers the Dazed and Disoriented conditions. (op)(op)+: Treat the maximum range of this technique as 1 higher per (op)(op) spent this way.</p>","strikewithoutshadow":"<p>When you succeed at an Attack or Movement action check, you may spend 1 Void point to add bonus successes equal to your ranks in Fitness.</p>","studentofmanycourts":"<p>Once per scene as a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Culture (Fire or Water) check targeting any number of other characters in the scene. If you succeed and chose Fire, each character gains the Emboldened condition. If you succeed and chose Water, each character removes 3 strife.</p>","suddenclarity":"<p>When you use your school ability, you may remove one or more of the following conditions from each chosen character: Dazed, Disoriented, Enraged, Exhausted, Intoxicated. Additionally, each chosen character removes 3 fatigue.</p>","surgeofbrilliance":"<p>When you craft an item, you may increase or decrease its rarity by up to your ranks in the skill you used to craft it. Once per game session when you make a check to create, refine, adapt, restore, or attune to an item, the check takes an action rather than a downtime activity.</p>","swiftcreation":"<p>Once per scene you may perform a ritual that uses the Medicine skill as an action as if it were a downtime activity.</p>","templeoftheheart":"<p>You may keep two kami within you at once instead of one. All effects of The Body Is a Shrine still apply. If two kami share an element, the effects do not stack for that element.</p>","tenacityoftheforge":"<p>When you create a new set of armor, you may apply two different patterns you know to it (instead of one).</p>","thecloudspart":"<p>Once per round, you may spend 1 Void point to add bonus successes equal to your honor rank to a successful Attack or Support action check.</p>","theeffortlesspath":"<p>When making a check to activate a kihō, you may spend (op) as follows: (op): If you succeed on this check, after you activate the kihō, you may perform a Strike action with a weapon you have readied in a one-handed grip.</p>","theeyesbetraytheheart":"<p>Once per scene when performing a skill check to investigate, you may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: You may reserve up to one dropped die per (op) spent this way. The next time you perform a check to interact with the person or thing you were investigating (such as a check targeting that person or a check to use that object), you may add any number of these reserved dice as kept dice. Then, remove any unused reserved dice.</p>","thefinalsilence":"<p>As an Attack and Movement action, you may make a TN 4 Martial Arts [Unarmed] (Air) check targeting any number of minion NPCs at range 0-4. If you succeed during a narrative scene, you silently kill all targets over the course of a few minutes. If you succeed during a conflict scene, at the end of each of your turns, you may silently kill one of these targets at range 0-2 (in addition to your other actions).</p>","theflowerbindstheroom":"<p>Once per game session, you can use your school ability on any check (action or downtime activity) to alter your environment. When you do, you may also add or remove one supernatural terrain quality from the area you affect.</p>","theherdflourishestogether":"<p>When you make a Social skill check, you may spend (op) as follows: (op)(op): Choose another character&#x27;s social objective that you know. You may transfer any number of momentum points you have accrued to the completion of their objective. After that character completes their objective, you gain the Support of [That Character&#x27;s Group] advantage if you do not have it already.</p>","theladysgrace":"<p>Once per scene, you may spend 1 Void point to reduce your strife to 0. When you do, each friendly character in the scene may reduce their strife by your honor rank.</p>","thelowestbow":"<p>When performing an Attack action using Martial Arts [Melee], you may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: Choose one character other than your target at range 2 with vigilance lower than or equal to (op) spent this way. That character suffers a critical strike with severity equal to your weapon&#x27;s deadliness plus your ranks in Martial Arts [Melee].</p>","themountaindoesnotfall":"<p>At the beginning of your turn, you may spend 1 Void point. If you do, ignore all of your conditions, terrain, and negative persistent effects of techniques and abilities. Do not apply your disadvantages to checks. If you would die, you cling to life for a few moments longer instead (but still die when the effect ends). This effect persists until the end of your next turn.</p>","thenobleheartshinesthrough":"<p>Once per scene, spend 1 Void point to target any non-Shadowlands creature of silhouette 3 or greater, giving the target the Loyal Steed ability until end of scene. Make a Courtesy (Water) or Theology (Void) check with TN equal to target&#x27;s vigilance. If you succeed, the target is favorable and willing to be ridden. Horses of the Blessed Herd (Utaku steeds) are immune.</p>","thespiritsunbound":"<p>At the end of your turn, you may spend 1 or more Void points to unleash the powers within an equal number of your meishōdō talismans, destroying these talismans and freeing the entities within. You may immediately perform each of the invocations for which the talismans were created, reducing the TN by 3.</p>","thestandingdeath":"<p>Once per game session, when you perform the Challenge action, you may choose up to 6 additional characters who can hear you as targets. These targets must have status lower than or equal to your original target&#x27;s. If you succeed, each target must fight you in a clash one at a time in an order of their choosing (or flee the battle). Each clash lasts one round. After each clash, you regain fatigue equal to your Earth Ring. Until all clashes have concluded (or you have been killed), none of your targets can perform Attack or Scheme actions outside of their individual clashes.</p>","totreadthesword":"<p>When you use the Guard action, instead of guarding one character, you may choose to guard a number of other characters in range up to your ranks in Martial Arts [Melee].</p>","towerofivory":"<p>After you defend against damage, increase your physical resistance by 1. This effect can stack a number of times equal to your ranks in Meditation and persists until the end of the scene.</p>","treasuresofthecarp":"<p>Once per game session, you may give away one item in your possession to reduce the TN of the next Social skill check you make targeting the recipient by an amount equal to the rarity of the item. For each point by which this would reduce the TN below 1, add a kept (ring) set to an (op) result to your check.</p>","unbreakableresolve":"<p>Compromised characters affected by your school ability can keep a number of dice containing (st) up to your ranks in Command.</p>","unseenblade":"<p>When you perform an Attack action, you may spend (op)+ as follows: Choose a character in range of the weapon you used with vigilance lower than your original target. If you succeed, that character suffers physical damage equal to your weapon&#x27;s base damage plus your ranks in Fitness.</p>","usherinthenewage":"<p>As a downtime activity, you may overcome or bypass an NPC’s guards or other security measures in order to gain access to them. Make a Skulduggery (Air) check targeting the NPC, with a TN equal to their highest conflict rank. If you succeed and the chosen NPC is a minion or an adversary the GM deems non-essential to the campaign plot, you accomplish your goal, such as assassinating the NPC or delivering an effective threat, in a method of your choosing (subject to the GM’s approval). If the NPC is an important adversary, you confront the NPC alone, likely beginning a conflict scene. (op)(op): Your efforts go completely unnoticed by anyone except possibly the target. (op)(op): If you kill the target, their death appears to be the result of an accident or natural causes (although a skilled investigator may still uncover the truth).</p>","victoryisthegreatesthonor":"<p>Once per session after failing a Martial or Social check, you may stake up to your school rank in honor to try again, adding bonus successes equal to the honor staked. If you fail, you forfeit all honor staked. If you succeed, you instead gain 1 honor and 1 glory.</p>","walkthehiddenways":"<p>When you use your school ability in a place already linked to a particular realm, you may move yourself and a number of characters up to your ranks in Meditation into that realm fully, leaving the Mortal Realm. As a Support action, you may make a TN 2 Meditation (Void) check to return yourself and a number of characters up to your ranks in Meditation to the Mortal Realm.</p>","whispersofthekami":"<p>You may spend 1 Void point to use your school ability an additional time this scene. You may do this multiple times.</p>","withthesoulofalion":"<p>After you perform an Attack action, each of your bonded animals may perform an Attack action against the same target, if able. If your attack action did not succeed, reduce the TN of each of your bonded animals&#x27; Attack action check by 2.</p>","worldofshadows":"<p>You may spend 1 Void point to attempt to establish that something in the scene has been an illusion all along. This could be an object, image of a person, or other illusory phenomenon you could summon with an invocation. You must make the check to summon this illusion using an invocation, with adjustments to the TN for plausibility determined by the GM. If you succeed, you reveal that the thing you chose is in fact an illusion you wove, and has been for at least a few moments. If you fail, your character clearly did not think to set up an illusion—the object is as it appears. As with all matters, the GM has final say over acceptable uses of this ability.</p>","yotogispiercinggaze":"<p>You can perceive beings that are normally invisible to human sight, such as spirits and characters concealed by supernatural abilities. When you deal damage to an Otherworldly being, you ignore an amount of its resistance up to your ranks in Meditation.</p>","hasegawasdenial":"<ul><li>Prerequisites: Crab Clan shugenja, school rank 3</li><li>XP Cost: 3</li><li>After successfully using an invocation to smite a target, the area at range 0-3 of the target becomes Dangerous terrain for Tainted beings. Persists until start of your next turn.</li></ul>","ichissecondsight":"<ul><li>Prerequisites: Witch Hunter, Crab Clan</li><li>XP Cost: 3</li><li>After successfully using an invocation to scry, any Supernatural or Tainted beings perceived glow faintly with an aura visible to the shugenja, even through smoke, mist, fog, or obscured vision.</li></ul>","maikarasrebuke":"<ul><li>Prerequisites: Shugenja</li><li>XP Cost: 3</li><li>After successfully using a Fire invocation to smite a target, that target treats the next attack targeting them as having the Sacred quality. Persists until end of scene.</li></ul>","asinglemoment":"<p>When you perform an Attack action that uses a sheathed Razor-Edged weapon, you may spend (op): Void (op)(op): Your target cannot defend against the damage unless they spend a Void point. Any (op): After resolving, you may sheathe the weapon you used.</p>","athousandstingingcuts":"<p>When you provide assistance on the Martial Arts [Melee] Attack action check of another character at range 0-2, the character you are assisting treats their target&#x27;s physical resistance as 1 lower for each assisting character with this ability.</p>","accustomedtoattention":"<p>When making a check to boast or get people&#x27;s attention, you may negate up to 2 (st) symbols.</p>","baneofsorcerers":"<p>When you make a check to resist the effects of a mahō technique, you may spend (op): Reduce the TN of your next check targeting the mahō practitioner by 1 per (op). (op)(op): If you succeed on the check to resist, the mahō practitioner receives strife equal to your ranks in Theology.</p>","beholdthelegend":"<p>Once per scene, after you make a successful Martial Arts check that inflicts fatigue or a critical strike on the target, you may have each friendly character at range 0-3 of you or the target remove an amount of strife equal to the TN of the check.</p>","blessingofthetrees":"<p>Once per scene when interacting with positive intentions towards a kami or other nature spirit, you may turn one kept die to the (ex) symbol.</p>","byimperialcommand":"<p>Once per scene as a Support action, choose a number of characters up to your ranks in Command and demand they pull themselves together. Each chosen character removes 3 strife.</p>","calmingwords":"<p>Once per scene, as a Scheme and Support action, you may reduce the strife of all characters in the scene by your ranks in Sentiment.</p>","captureevil":"<p>Reduce the TN of your Survival checks to track down a Tainted being by 1. When you inflict a critical strike on a Tainted being, you may spend (op)(op): The target suffers the Dazed, Disoriented, or Immobilized condition.</p>","celestialinfluence":"<p>Reduce the TN of your Attack and Scheme action checks targeting Otherworldly beings by 1 (to a minimum of 1).</p>","communewiththechanged":"<p>Once per scene, make TN 3 Sentiment or Survival (Water 2) check to peer into the soul of a yokai you can perceive. If you succeed, identify two of: - The yokai&#x27;s greatest current need - One of the yokai&#x27;s weaknesses - The yokai&#x27;s greatest strength - Whether the yokai is alone or in a group - Whether the yokai could be parlayed with Additionally, TN of checks to interact with yokai socially are reduced by 1 (minimum 1).</p>","earseverywhere":"<p>Once per game session as a Scheme and Support action or downtime activity targeting a location or social group, make a TN 4 Sentiment (Air) check. If you succeed, discover the latest relevant happenings and which current rumors are false. If discerning someone&#x27;s qualities is your social objective in an intrigue, score momentum points equal to your Air Ring plus bonus successes. (op): Plant a rumor that spreads among the targeted group.</p>","enderofworks":"<p>When a fortification&#x27;s difficulty value would be reduced during a mass battle, the value is lowered by that amount plus your ranks in Labor instead. If there is a cohort occupying it, that cohort&#x27;s army suffers panic equal to your ranks in Skulduggery.</p>","enlightened":"<p>When you are selected as a target of an action requiring a skill check, you may spend a Void point to increase or decrease the TN of the check by an amount up to your ranks in Meditation (minimum 1).</p>","everystonehasitsplace":"<p>When undertaking a downtime activity to prepare your castle for an important event (a wedding, battle, or Winter Court), you may change all rolled blank results to (op) results.</p>","eyesoftheancestors":"<p>Once per game session as a Support action, you may spend 1 Void point to summon the spirit of an ancestor to partially possess you until the end of the scene. Choose a ring and a skill from that ancestor&#x27;s profile; while possessed, you count as an Otherworldly being and use your ancestor&#x27;s ring value and skill rank in place of your own, as well as your ancestor&#x27;s honor value. Your ancestor can use any non-unique human NPC profile (or a kitsu&#x27;s or other supernatural being&#x27;s profile, if appropriate). The higher of this NPC&#x27;s conflict ranks cannot exceed your school rank plus your ranks in Meditation. The ancestor spirit may divulge pertinent information at the GM&#x27;s discretion. Afterward, you have only a hazy memory of anything you experienced while possessed.</p>","eyesoftheyodhaniya":"<p>When you make a check to see through supernatural illusion, reduce the TN by 1. If you are in Defiled terrain, reduce the TN by 2 instead.</p>","firstforgeyourself":"<p>When you make a check to craft an item, you may suffer a number of fatigue up to your ranks in Fitness. If you do, change that many results containing (su) to (op) results.</p>","furyofmatsu":"<p>Once per scene, when you deal damage to a target or deal attrition to an enemy leader&#x27;s cohort, increase the damage or attrition by an amount equal to the difference between your honor rank and the target&#x27;s honor rank.</p>","goblinkiller":"<p>When making a Martial Arts [Any] check targeting a goblin, you may spend (op)+: Each other goblin at range 0-2 of your target receives 1 strife per (op) spent.</p>","inspiredcreations":"<p>When crafting an item, you may spend (op)(op)(op): The item is a singular masterwork. You must name it. Once per game session when making a check using the item, a character may add 1 (ring) set to any result of their choice.</p>","instinctivecommand":"<p>After you perform an action, you may receive 2 fatigue to have any number of your animal companions each take an action that shares a type with your action (still limited to one action of each type per round).</p>","invincibleblade":"<p>When you perform an Attack or Support action check that uses a sword, you may spend (op) as follows: Void (op)+: Reduce the severity of the next critical strike you would suffer (before your Fitness check to resist) by your ranks in Meditation plus 1 per (op) spent. Persists until start of your next turn. Any (op)(op): Increase the base damage and deadliness of your weapon by 3. Persists until end of scene. Cumulative if activated multiple times.</p>","justiceofthechampion":"<p>When you make a Command or Courtesy check targeting a member of your clan, you may spend (op)+: The target receives or removes (your choice) strife equal to (op) spent this way.</p>","kirifusoath":"<p>As a Support action, you may suffer the Enraged condition. While you are Enraged, you can perform Attack actions even while Incapacitated.</p>","leadfromthefront":"<p>When you defeat an opponent in a clash, your cohort removes panic equal to the opponent&#x27;s glory rank. Once per round when you succeed at an Attack action check during a mass battle, your cohort removes panic equal to half of the attrition you inflict.</p>","learnedfromhistory":"<p>During a mass battle, when you accrue 1 or more momentum points toward the Draw Them In or Seize Victory strategic objective, you accrue that many momentum points plus 1 instead. Additionally, if your action completes that strategic objective, the enemy army receives additional casualties and panic equal to your ranks in Tactics.</p>","linguisticliason":"<p>You learn the languages of the group for which you are an interpreter. The first time you make a check to interact socially with a member of this group each encounter, reduce the TN by 1.</p>","masterofthelariat":"<p>When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Ranged] Attack action check using a Snaring weapon, add 1 kept skill die set to (su)(op).</p>","meishodosecrets":"<p>You are learned in the Way of Names and can wield meishōdō. Grants new options in Otherworldly Encounters. You can sustain one meishōdō talisman of your own creation. If you create a second, you must choose one and release the spirit within it.</p>","mercilesseyes":"<p>When making a check to plan an assassination or attack with lethal intent, you may negate up to 2 (st) symbols.</p>","nosacrificetoogreat":"<p>One character is assigned as your charge; they can order you to treat someone else as your charge until they lift this order. If your charge is at range 0-2, you may spend 1 Void point to replace your charge as the target of an Attack action. If you suffer a critical strike as a result, gain 1 Void point.</p>","practicedprevaricator":"<p>When you make a check to deceive or hide from someone, you may negate up to 2 (st) symbols.</p>","privilegedposition":"<p>Once per session, when acting in your lord&#x27;s interest, you may use their status rank as your own.</p>","procurementandsupply":"<p>When you make a check as a downtime activity to provision an army, you may spend (op) as follows: (op)+: If you succeed, your army increases its discipline and strength each by 1 per (op) spent. This effect persists until the end of the next mass battle scene.</p>","sacredmantras":"<p>You can purchase mantra techniques.</p>","servantofthekami":"<p>You may importune invocations even if you do not know any invocations. When you importune, do not increase the TN by 1 (although you still increase TN if the invocation rank is higher than your school rank).</p>","skilledattendant":"<p>When you provide assistance on a Scholar skill check, the character you are assisting may roll (skill) equal to your ranks in that skill instead of their own.</p>","slayerofimmortals":"<p>When you perform an Attack action, you can spend (op)+: You attempt to ascertain your target&#x27;s mortal weaknesses. Target must resist with a Sentiment check; TN equals your ranks in Survival plus (op) spent (Air +2, Fire -2). If target fails, you learn one key clue to defeating it permanently. If you already know how to defeat it, reduce TN of your next check against it by 2.</p>","soothingcadence":"<p>When making a skill check to communicate with a group of three or more people, you may keep up to one extra die. If your check succeeds, each other character in the scene removes strife equal to your bonus successes.</p>","spiritualprotector":"<ul><li>For reasons known or unknown, a spirit watches over you and intercedes in subtle ways to protect you from harm. It may alert you to danger or interpose a mild obstacle to those who wish you harm.</li><li>When performing a check for which your spiritual protector is a benefit (such as Fitness [Void] check to avoid a surprise attack through sheer instinct or a Survival [Void] check to notice an imminent hazard), you may reroll up to two dice.</li></ul>","strengthoftheelements":"<p>Choose one: Air, Earth, Fire, or Water. This is your elemental specialty. Once per scene after making a Martial skill check that uses the ring of your elemental specialty, you and a number of targets at range 0-3 (or other cohort leaders in the scene) up to your ranks in Command may remove strife equal to your ranks in that ring.</p>","superiorcommand":"<p>While you are the commander of an army during a mass battle, your army&#x27;s discipline value is increased by your ranks in Command. Additionally, when making an Initiative check during a mass battle, increase the result by your ranks in Tactics.</p>","swallowthelight":"<p>Once per session as an Attack and Scheme action, make a Theology (Water) check targeting a character at range 0-1 (TN = target&#x27;s vigilance). If you succeed, choose one ring. Target treats that ring as reduced by half (min 1), and you treat yours as increased by the amount reduced. Derived attributes change accordingly. Persists for rounds equal to your Void Ring.</p>","taintedwarrior":"<p>Increase the TN of all your non-Command Social skill checks by 1, and reduce the TN of all your Martial Arts [Any] skill checks targeting Tainted beings by 1 (minimum 1). Non-Tainted beings receive 1 strife whenever they make a Social skill check targeting you.</p>","takethemalive":"<p>When you make an Attack action using a weapon with the Snaring quality, you may alter any number of kept dice containing (su) or (ex) to results set to (op).</p>","thehandofourancestors":"<p>After you perform a successful Rally action, the targeted cohort deals 1 additional attrition when its leader performs a successful Attack action check. This effect persists for one round.</p>","timetesteddefense":"<p>After an Attack action check targeting you fails, the attacker suffers strife equal to their shortfall.</p>","trustworthycadence":"<p>When making a social skill check targeting a character with status 20 or lower, reduce the TN by 1.</p>","unrelentingandinevitable":"<p>When you receive strife due to the effect of an Otherworldly or Tainted being, reduce the strife by your ranks in Meditation. When another character makes a check to resist an effect of an Attack action you perform (including resisting a critical strike), increase the TN of that check by 1.</p>","unsurpassedsoul":"<p>When you make a Martial Arts [Unarmed] check targeting another character, if your Void ring is higher than or equal to your target&#x27;s Void ring, reduce the TN by 2 (to a minimum of 1).</p>","voiceofauthoritydaimyo":"<p>Once per game session when making a Scheme or Support action check using a Social skill, you may choose additional targets equal to your Glory rank. You cannot choose any additional target with vigilance higher than the highest among your initial targets.</p>","voiceofauthorityemeraldmagistrate":"<p>Once per game session when making a Scheme or Support action check using a Social skill, you may choose additional targets equal to your Glory rank. You cannot choose any additional target with vigilance higher than the highest among your initial targets.</p>","wisdomofcountlesslifetimes":"<p>When making a skill check, you may spend 1 Void point to treat your skill rank as 1 higher, to a maximum of 6. If you fail the check, gain 1 Void point.</p>","wrathoftheelements":"<p>Choose one: Air, Earth, Fire, or Water. This is your elemental specialty. Once per scene after making a Martial skill check that uses the ring of your elemental specialty, you may inflict an amount of strife or panic equal to your ranks in that ring against a target at range 0-3 or a cohort in the scene.</p>"};
